window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-1"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 第一章：失竊的二十四小時\n\n## 一、不存在的星期三\n\n鹿陽國小六年一班的早自習鐘聲響起時，十二歲的誠浩正盯著自己的鉛筆盒發呆。\n\n他的鉛筆盒跟其他同學都不一樣——那是一個被他親手改裝過的金屬鐵盒，側面嵌著兩顆從報廢計算機拆下來的小齒輪，只要按下一枚彈簧卡榫，鐵盒蓋子就會像老式火車車門一樣，伴隨著清脆的「喀噠」聲向兩側自動滑開。\n\n平常這個時候，誠浩早就迫不及待拿出藏在書包底層的小螺絲起子開始搗鼓他的微型零件了。但今天，他連碰都沒碰那把心愛的工具。\n\n一種說不上來的古怪感，像一隻冰涼的小蟲子，順著他的背脊慢慢往上爬。\n\n「喂，將江。」誠浩忍不住轉過頭，用筆頭輕輕戳了戳前座的同桌，「今天星期幾？」\n\n留著平頭的將江嘴裡還塞著半塊菠蘿麵包，含糊不清地翻了個白眼：「你睡傻啦？黑板上不是寫得清清楚楚嘛。」\n\n誠浩抬起頭。\n\n教室正前方那塊嶄新的液晶智慧黑板，右上角跳動著幾行冰冷平滑的白色電子字體：\n\n> **2026 年 10 月 17 日**  \n> **星期四｜晨間氣溫 21°C**  \n> **今日值日生：誠浩、葉旖緁**\n\n誠浩的瞳孔猛然縮緊了一下。\n\n「星期四？」他的聲音不自覺地拔高了半度，「等等……昨天不是星期二嗎？我們昨天下午還在操場踢球，我記得我被足球踢中鼻樑，流鼻血被送去保健室……那不是昨天的事嗎？」\n\n「你在說什麼夢話啊？」將江嚼著麵包笑出聲來，「星期二踢球那是前天！昨天是星期三，正常上課啊。」\n\n「昨天是星期三？」誠浩的心跳開始加速，他盯著將江，「那我問你，昨天第三節是什麼課？」\n\n「昨天第三節……」將江臉上的笑容忽然凝固了一瞬間。\n\n誠浩清清楚楚地看見，將江那雙平平無奇的眼睛裡，似乎閃過了一道極其微弱、極不自然的滯澀感，就像電視螢幕突然卡住了一幀畫面。\n\n大約過了整整三秒鐘，將江才眨了眨眼，神情恢復正常，隨口說道：「就……就自然課啊。老師教了植物光合作用，還有……還有磁鐵什麼的吧。哎呀，反正就是上課嘛，誰會去記那麼清楚！」\n\n「那自然老師穿什麼顏色的衣服？昨天中午吃什麼菜？」誠浩逼問。\n\n將江被問得有些煩躁，抓了抓頭髮：「哎呀誠浩你有毛病是不是！誰沒事記營養午餐吃了幾根青菜啊？反正吃飽了不就行了！」\n\n將江轉回身去不再理他。\n\n誠浩轉頭望向整間教室。二十幾個同學有的在抄聯絡簿，有的在聊天，有的在打哈欠。每個人看起來都那麼正常，但只要仔細觀察就會發現，沒有任何一個人能在三秒鐘之內說出昨天具體發生過的一件小事。\n\n全班的記憶，就像被一塊巨大的無形橡皮擦，乾乾淨淨地抹掉了昨天整整二十四個小時，只留下一層模模糊糊、似是而非的「印象」。\n\n---\n\n## 二、空白的筆記本\n\n就在這時，一陣輕微而急促的腳步聲在誠浩身旁停了下來。\n\n誠浩轉頭，看見了班長葉旖緁。\n\n葉旖緁梳著一絲不茍的黑色高馬尾，鼻樑上架著一副細金屬框眼鏡。在鹿陽國小，她是出了名的「邏輯怪物」——她能在五分鐘內背下一整張化學元素週期表，每天的生活嚴格按照分鐘規劃，連每天喝了多少毫升的水都會記錄下來。\n\n但此刻，葉旖緁的臉色蒼白得像一張剛出廠的影印紙。\n\n「誠浩，出來一下。」旖緁壓低聲音，語氣裡帶著一種誠浩從未聽過的緊繃。\n\n誠浩連忙站起身，跟著她快步走出了喧鬧的教室，來到走廊盡頭安靜的飲水機旁。\n\n旖緁環顧四周，確認沒有巡邏老師或巡邏機器人走過來，才深吸一口氣，將懷裡那本厚厚的黑皮筆記本遞到了誠浩面前。\n\n那是旖緁寸步不離的隨身筆記。誠浩低頭看去，只見旖緁正翻開在最近的幾頁。\n\n十月十四日（週一），工整得像印刷體的字跡記滿了待辦事項，右邊打了整齊的小勾。  \n十月十五日（週二），同樣記得密密麻麻，連體育課將江踢球踢歪的角度都畫了簡圖。  \n然後，是下一頁。\n\n那一頁的最頂端，用藍色鋼筆端端正正地寫著：  \n`2026年10月16日 星期三`。\n\n然而，在日期下方，整整一大頁橫線紙上——  \n**空無一字。**\n\n甚至連一個不小心劃下的墨水點都沒有，乾淨得讓人發毛。\n\n「你看見了？」旖緁的聲音帶著一絲難以察覺的顫抖，「我從國小一年級開始寫日記，無論感冒發燒還是出門旅遊，我從來沒有落下一天。如果昨天我們真的坐在教室裡上了一整天課，我的筆記本上絕對不可能一個字都沒有。」\n\n「妳也不記得昨天了？」誠浩急促地問。\n\n「不是『不記得』，」旖緁推了推眼鏡，眼神銳利得驚人，「是大腦裡根本沒有這段資料。我嘗試回憶昨天的早餐、上學走的路、甚至幾點上床睡覺……誠浩，我的大腦裡是一片雪花亂碼，就像錄影帶被磁鐵洗過一樣。」\n\n「果然……」誠浩喃喃自語，「全校的人都跳過了昨天，而且除了我們兩個，大家都覺得今天直接跳到星期四是理所當然的！」\n\n「不，不只是全校。」旖緁指了指走廊窗外遠處的齒輪鎮街景，「今天早上我出門時問過麵包店阿姨，她也說昨天正常營業，可當我問她昨天的招牌牛角麵包賣了幾個時，她足足愣了五秒鐘才隨便敷衍過去。全鎮人的大腦……被動了手腳。」\n\n---\n\n## 三、爺爺的幽靈護目鏡\n\n這句話讓誠浩的後背泛起一層雞皮疙瘩。\n\n「等一下，」誠浩像是突然想起了什麼，猛地一把拉開自己的書包拉鍊，「旖緁，妳看這個。」\n\n他從書包最深處掏出了一件用厚毛巾包裹的奇怪物件。\n\n毛巾揭開，裡面是一副造型極為復古的飛行員護目鏡。鏡框是由深暗色的黃銅打造的，邊緣佈滿了精密的機械卡扣與微型齒輪，兩片橢圓形的鏡片並不是普通的透明玻璃，而是呈現出一種奇異的深紫色，在日光下隱隱流轉著如彩虹般的浮油光澤。\n\n「這是我爺爺留下的。」誠浩壓低聲音說。\n\n誠浩的爺爺曾是齒輪鎮最傳奇的高級機械工程師，但在三年前突然不辭而別，只留下閣樓裡滿滿幾十箱古怪的機械圖紙與未完成的零件。\n\n「今天早上七點，我被閣樓裡一陣很刺耳的蜂鳴聲吵醒。」誠浩說，「這副放在鐵箱最底層的護目鏡，竟然自己在發光、發熱。我覺得不對勁，就把它偷偷帶到學校來了。」\n\n旖緁看著護目鏡邊緣細小如螞蟻的刻度線，眉頭緊皺：「這不是普通的護目鏡。鏡框兩側有微型的光譜濾鏡和光學偏振晶片……你試過戴上它嗎？」\n\n「還沒，」誠浩嚥了口唾沫，「在教室裡戴太惹眼了。」\n\n「現在試試。」旖緁果斷地說，轉身替誠浩擋住走廊另一頭的視線，「快。」\n\n誠浩點了點頭。他握住黃銅鏡框，雙手微微有些發抖。他深吸一口氣，將這副冰涼的護目鏡套在了頭上，拉下鏡片——\n\n剎那間，誠浩的世界徹底變了。\n\n原本乾淨潔白、鋪著米黃色瓷磚的學校走廊，瞬間褪去了日常的色彩。\n\n眼前的空間被一層極其繁複、淡藍色的立體光格所覆蓋！\n\n牆壁上的白油漆彷彿變成了半透明，誠浩竟然能透過鏡片，清清楚楚地看見隱藏在水泥牆體深處的電線、水管，以及……數以百計完全不屬於這所學校的粗大黑色數據光纜！那些光纜如同某種巨大怪獸的血管，正隱隱閃爍著深紫色的脈衝光，全部朝著走廊盡頭的校長室方向匯聚。\n\n更詭異的是，在平整的地板磚上，憑空印著一串串發光的紫色腳印，歪歪斜斜地穿透了緊閉的儲藏室大門。\n\n「天啊……」誠浩倒抽了一口涼氣，雙腿差點發軟。\n\n「誠浩？你看見了什麼？」站在一旁的旖緁看見誠浩臉色大變，連忙問道。\n\n「你看不到嗎？」誠浩指著前方的半空，「就在那裡！在校長室的門楣上方！」\n\n旖緁摘下眼鏡揉了揉眼睛，搖頭：「那裡只有校規標語牌。」\n\n「不是！」誠浩的聲音發顫，「那是一塊浮空的紅色半透明方框！」\n\n在誠浩的視野裡，校長室金屬門牌上方懸浮著一個巨大的警報視窗，上面的文字正以每秒兩次的速度瘋狂閃爍：\n\n> `[CRITICAL ALERT: TIMELINE PATCH v4.04 INSTALLED]`  \n> `[異常代碼：星期三日誌已被隔離移入伺服器]`  \n> `[未授權記憶殘留檢測中……]`\n\n而在那個警報框下方，還有一串極長、以光點形式烙印在走廊牆面上的神秘數字代碼！\n\n---\n\n## 四、牆上的加密警報\n\n「快，旖緁，拿筆！」誠浩一把抓住旖緁的手臂，「牆上有光，有一串數字！它們正在慢慢變淡，好像快要消失了！」\n\n旖緁沒有絲毫猶豫，立刻翻開黑皮筆記本，拔開鋼筆筆蓋：「念給我聽！」\n\n誠浩死死盯著護目鏡中漸漸模糊的紫色光斑，飛快地念道：\n\n「`04`……空格……`15`……`14`……`20`！」  \n「下一組：`04`……`18`……`09`……`14`……`11`！」  \n「最後一組：`13`……`09`……`12`……`11`！」\n\n旖緁的鋼筆在紙面上飛速滑動，留下一串清晰的數字：\n\n```\n04 - 15 - 14 - 20\n04 - 18 - 09 - 14 - 11\n13 - 09 - 12 - 11\n```\n\n念完最後一個數字，誠浩看見牆上的光斑像水滴蒸發一樣，彻底化作虛無，消失得無影無蹤。\n\n「記下來了嗎？」誠浩大口喘著氣，將護目鏡推到額頭上。眼前的走廊瞬間又變回了那副平靜、無聊的校園模樣。\n\n「記下來了。」旖緁盯著紙上的三組數字，鼻樑上的鏡片反射著窗外的晨光。\n\n她的手指在筆記本邊緣輕輕敲擊，這是她大腦全速運轉時的習慣動作。\n\n「這不是隨機數列。」旖緁冷靜地分析，「最大數字不超過 26，而且全是兩位數配對……誠浩，這是最基礎的 A1Z26 字母代換密碼！每一個數字對應英文字母表中的一個位置。」\n\n旖緁立刻在數字下方飛快地寫下對應的字母：\n\n* 第一組：\n  * 04 ＝ **D**\n  * 15 ＝ **O**\n  * 14 ＝ **N**\n  * 20 ＝ **T**\n  * ➡️ **DONT**（不要）\n\n* 第二組：\n  * 04 ＝ **D**\n  * 18 ＝ **R**\n  * 09 ＝ **I**\n  * 14 ＝ **N**\n  * 11 ＝ **K**\n  * ➡️ **DRINK**（喝）\n\n* 第三組：\n  * 13 ＝ **M**\n  * 09 ＝ **I**\n  * 12 ＝ **L**\n  * 11 ＝ **K**\n  * ➡️ **MILK**（牛奶）\n\n三組單詞連成了一句完整的話。\n\n旖緁盯著筆記本上的那行英文，瞳孔微微放大。\n\n「**DONT DRINK MILK**……」誠浩跟著念了出來，聲音瞬間乾澀，「不要……喝牛奶？」\n\n「牛奶？」旖緁猛然抬頭，「我們學校每天上午第二節下課，都會免費發放一瓶的——」\n\n「齒輪鎮高科技智慧乳業贊助的『高鈣健腦鮮乳』！」誠浩接上了她的話，臉色瞬間慘白。\n\n---\n\n## 五、致命的鈴聲\n\n**「噹——啷——啷——」**\n\n就在誠浩話音剛落的同一秒，走廊上方的高音廣播喇叭突兀地炸響了！\n\n那不是平時柔和悠揚的下課鐘聲，而是一種尖銳、刺耳，帶著微弱高頻電流雜音的合成音效。\n\n「請全體六年級同學注意，」廣播裡傳來了副校長平靜得近乎詭異的播報聲，「今日營養加餐已送達各班。為配合智慧健康監測計畫，請所有同學在五分鐘內飲用完畢，嚴禁丟棄或帶出教室。」\n\n與此同時，走廊盡頭傳來了一陣沉重的履帶滾動聲。\n\n一輛全不鏽鋼密封的保溫餐車，正由一台圓筒狀的校園清潔巡邏機器人緩緩推向六年一班的門口。餐車上整齊地碼放著幾十瓶玻璃瓶裝的鮮奶，瓶蓋上印著淡藍色的智慧晶片標籤。\n\n走廊上的其他同學們發出一陣歡呼，像平時一樣嬉皮笑臉地湧向餐車，紛紛拿起牛奶擰開瓶蓋。\n\n誠浩急忙重新將護目鏡拉下。\n\n只看了一眼，他的血液就幾乎凍結了。\n\n在護目鏡的紫外視野下，每一瓶透明的鮮奶內部，竟然都飄浮著一團極微小、肉眼完全看不見的銀色金屬螢光點！而在教室的天花板正中央，不知道什麼時候安裝了一個倒扣漏斗狀的黑色信號發射器，正朝著整間教室的牛奶瓶源源不斷地發射著微弱的脈衝波！\n\n教室裡，誠浩最好的朋友將江已經撕開了塑膠封口，揚起脖子，正要把冰涼的牛奶往嘴裡灌——\n\n「將江！住手！不要喝！」\n\n誠浩再也忍不住了，狂吼著拔腿朝教室門口猛衝過去！\n\n然而，就在誠浩吼出這句話的瞬間，走廊上原本緩慢移動的清潔機器人突然猛地一頓。\n\n它原本閃爍著安全綠光的機械眼部，「卡塔」一聲，瞬間切換成了猩紅如血的警暴模式！\n\n與此同時，誠浩護目鏡的右下角，一行血紅色的全新代碼以極其瘋狂的速度彈了出來：\n\n> `[WARNING: UNAUTHORIZED SPECTRUM DETECTED]`  \n> `[警告：偵測到非法觀察者]`  \n> `[目標身分鎖定：鹿陽國小 六年一班 誠浩]`  \n> `[執行強制記憶覆蓋程序——清除協議啟動！]`\n\n整條走廊上的三台清潔機器人同時轉動了底盤，履帶在瓷磚地上刮出刺耳的摩擦聲，伸出鋼鐵鑄造的抓捕機械臂，直直朝著誠浩猛撲了過來！\n\n---\n\n*(第一章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第一章：失竊的二十四小時 (Chapter 1: The Stolen Twenty-Four Hours)\n\n## 一、不存在的星期三 (I. The Wednesday That Never Was)\n\nWhen the morning study bell rang across Class 6-1 at Lu-Yang Elementary, twelve-year-old Cheng Hao sat staring blankly at his pencil case.\n\nHis pencil case was unlike anyone else's—a custom metal tin he had modified with his own hands. Embedded on its side were two tiny spur gears salvaged from an old, discarded calculator. With a light flick of a brass spring latch, the tin lid slid smoothly open to both sides like the doors of a vintage train car, accompanied by a crisp, satisfying *click-clack*.\n\nUsually by this hour, Cheng Hao would have already fished out his trusty miniature screwdriver from the bottom of his backpack, eager to tinker with his collection of clockwork gears and brass wires. But today, he hadn't even touched his favorite tool.\n\nAn inexplicable, eerie sensation—like a cold beetle creeping along his spine—was slowly inching upward.\n\n\"Hey, Jiang Jiang,\" Cheng Hao whispered, tapping his pencil eraser against the shoulder of the boy sitting in front of him. \"What day is today?\"\n\nJiang Jiang, sporting a buzz cut and a mouth half-stuffed with a pineapple bun, rolled his eyes and mumbled, \"Did you sleep through your alarm or something? It's written right there on the blackboard.\"\n\nCheng Hao looked up.\n\nIn the upper-right corner of the classroom's sleek, newly installed smart LCD blackboard, smooth lines of crisp white digital text glowed faintly:\n\n> **October 17, 2026**  \n> **Thursday | Morning Temp: 21°C**  \n> **Class Monitors on Duty: Cheng Hao, Ye Yijie**\n\nCheng Hao's pupils snapped tight.\n\n\"Thursday?\" His voice pitched up half an octave without him realizing it. \"Wait a minute... wasn't yesterday Tuesday? We were playing soccer on the field yesterday afternoon! I vividly remember taking a ball straight to the bridge of my nose and getting sent to the nurse's office with a nosebleed... Wasn't that yesterday?!\"\n\n\"What kind of daydream are you stuck in?\" Jiang Jiang chuckled through a mouthful of crumbs. \"Soccer on Tuesday was two days ago! Yesterday was Wednesday. Regular school day.\"\n\n\"Yesterday was Wednesday?\" Cheng Hao's heart rate spiked. He leaned closer, locking eyes with his friend. \"Then tell me: what class did we have for third period yesterday?\"\n\n\"Yesterday's third period...\" The grin on Jiang Jiang's face froze mid-chew.\n\nCheng Hao saw it clearly—a fleeting, unnatural glitch fluttered across Jiang Jiang's ordinary eyes, as if a paused frame had seized a television screen.\n\nIt took three full, agonizing seconds before Jiang Jiang blinked, his expression snapping back to nonchalant ease. \"Well... science class, obviously. The teacher went over plant photosynthesis, and... and magnets, or whatever. Man, who keeps track of every single lesson? School is school!\"\n\n\"Then what color shirt was the science teacher wearing? What did we have for school lunch yesterday?\" Cheng Hao pressed, his pulse hammering in his throat.\n\nIrritated, Jiang Jiang scratched his messy hair. \"Dude, what is your problem today?! Who counts how many stalks of bok choy they ate at lunch? As long as you're full, who cares!\"\n\nJiang Jiang turned back around, ignoring him.\n\nCheng Hao glanced around the room. Two dozen classmates were either copying down homework assignments, chattering about comics, or yawning lazily. Everyone appeared completely normal on the surface. Yet, with closer scrutiny, it became chillingly apparent: not a single kid in the room could recall one concrete, specific detail from the previous day in under three seconds.\n\nIt was as if an immense, invisible eraser had wiped clean twenty-four solid hours from every brain in the class, leaving behind nothing but a hazy, fabricated smear of \"vague impressions.\"\n\n---\n\n## 二、空白的筆記本 (II. The Blank Notebook)\n\nJust then, a pair of light, hurried footsteps halted beside Cheng Hao's desk.\n\nHe looked up and found class president Ye Yijie standing over him.\n\nYijie wore her glossy black hair in a meticulous, immaculate high ponytail, framed by thin wire-rimmed glasses perched on her nose. At Lu-Yang Elementary, she was renowned as the undisputed \"Logic Prodigy\"—she could recite the entire periodic table in under five minutes, mapped her daily schedule down to the exact minute, and even logged the precise milliliters of water she drank each day.\n\nYet right now, Yijie's face was as stark white as a freshly pressed sheet of printer paper.\n\n\"Cheng Hao, outside. Now,\" she whispered, her tone strung with a taut urgency he had never heard before.\n\nCheng Hao stood up immediately, following her brisk stride out of the bustling classroom to the quiet corner beside the hallway water fountain.\n\nYijie scanned the corridor, ensuring no patrol teachers or cleaning androids were approaching. Taking a deep breath, she pulled out a thick, black leather-bound notebook clutched to her chest and held it open before Cheng Hao's eyes.\n\nIt was her daily bullet journal—the one item that never left her side. Cheng Hao looked down at the most recent entries.\n\n*October 14 (Monday)*: Neat, print-perfect handwriting filled the page with actionable checklists, each accompanied by a crisp checkmark on the right.  \n*October 15 (Tuesday)*: Equally dense, featuring even a hand-drawn diagram illustrating the precise trajectory of Jiang Jiang's mishit soccer ball.  \nThen came the next page.\n\nAt the very top, written in flawless royal-blue fountain pen ink, sat the header:  \n`Wednesday, October 16, 2026`.\n\nYet beneath the date, across the entire lined sheet—  \n**It was entirely blank.**\n\nNot a single scribble. Not even an accidental stray dot of ink. It was so immaculate it made Cheng Hao's skin prickle.\n\n\"Do you see it?\" Yijie's voice trembled with a rare fracture of composure. \"I have kept a daily log since first grade. Rain or shine, whether burning with a fever or traveling abroad, I have never missed a single entry. If we truly sat in class and went through a normal school day yesterday, it would be mathematically impossible for this page to be void of a single stroke.\"\n\n\"You don't remember yesterday either?\" Cheng Hao whispered urgently.\n\n\"It isn't a matter of 'forgetting,'\" Yijie pushed her glasses up, her gaze piercingly sharp. \"The data simply does not exist in my brain. I tried tracing yesterday's breakfast, the route I took to school, even the hour I fell asleep... Cheng Hao, my mind is blank static, like a cassette tape scrubbed by an industrial electromagnet.\"\n\n\"I knew it...\" Cheng Hao muttered. \"The whole school skipped yesterday. And except for the two of us, everyone thinks jumping straight to Thursday is completely natural!\"\n\n\"No, it isn't just the school,\" Yijie pointed through the corridor window toward the distant rooftops of Gear Town. \"On my way here this morning, I asked the bakery lady. She insisted the shop was open as usual yesterday. But when I asked how many of her signature croissants she sold, she froze for five full seconds before brushing me off with a vague excuse. The entire town's memory... has been tampered with.\"\n\n---\n\n## 三、爺爺的幽靈護目鏡 (III. Grandpa's Ghost Goggles)\n\nThat revelation sent a cold shiver racing down Cheng Hao's back.\n\n\"Wait a second,\" Cheng Hao gasped, his eyes widening as a sudden memory hit him. He reached down and yanked open his backpack zipper. \"Yijie, look at this.\"\n\nFrom the deepest pocket of his bag, he pulled out an unusual bundle wrapped in a thick towel.\n\nUnwrapping the cloth, he revealed a pair of vintage aviator-style goggles. The frames were forged from weathered, deep-toned brass, their rims fitted with miniature mechanical gears and microscopic dials. Instead of regular clear glass, the twin oval lenses were crafted from a mysterious, iridescent purple crystal that shimmered with an oily, rainbow sheen in the morning light.\n\n\"My grandfather left these behind,\" Cheng Hao murmured under his breath.\n\nHis grandfather had once been Gear Town's most legendary chief mechanical engineer—until he vanished mysteriously three years ago, leaving an attic crammed with dozens of wooden crates filled with cryptic blueprints and unfinished clockwork devices.\n\n\"At seven o'clock this morning, a piercing, high-pitched hum woke me up in the attic,\" Cheng Hao explained. \"These goggles, buried at the very bottom of an iron chest, were glowing and emitting heat all by themselves. I knew something was wrong, so I smuggled them to school.\"\n\nYijie leaned in, examining the microscopic vernier scales etched along the brass rims with a furrowed brow. \"These aren't ordinary aviator goggles. Both temples are equipped with miniature optical spectrometers and polarized prism chips... Have you tried putting them on?\"\n\n\"Not yet,\" Cheng Hao swallowed hard. \"Wearing something like this in homeroom would draw way too much attention.\"\n\n\"Try them now,\" Yijie said decisively, stepping sideways to block the view of the corridor. \"Hurry.\"\n\nCheng Hao nodded. His hands trembled slightly as he lifted the cool brass frames. Taking a deep breath, he pulled the leather strap over his head and slid the lenses down over his eyes—\n\nIn a heartbeat, his entire universe shattered.\n\nThe plain, mundane school hallway—with its bland cream-colored tiles and pale walls—instantly lost its ordinary facade.\n\nThe space before his eyes was inundated with a dizzying, three-dimensional grid of glowing cyan vector lines!\n\nThe white plaster on the walls appeared semi-transparent. Through the purple lenses, Cheng Hao could clearly see the plumbing, electrical conduits, and... hundreds of heavy, jet-black data cables that had no business existing inside an elementary school! Those conduits pulsed with deep purple light like the veins of an underground leviathan, snaking through the concrete and converging toward the principal's office at the far end of the hall.\n\nEven more bizarre: glowing purple footprints hovered above the tiled floor, marching in an erratic line straight through the locked metal door of the janitor's closet.\n\n\"Sweet gears of steam...\" Cheng Hao gasped, his knees buckling under a sudden wave of vertigo.\n\n\"Cheng Hao? What do you see?\" Yijie asked, catching his elbow as she noticed the color drain from his face.\n\n\"You really can't see it?\" Cheng Hao pointed frantically into midair. \"Right there! Suspended right above the lintel of the principal's office!\"\n\nYijie slipped off her wire glasses, rubbed her eyes, and shook her head. \"There's only the wooden school motto plaque.\"\n\n\"No!\" Cheng Hao's voice shook. \"It's a floating, semi-transparent crimson terminal window!\"\n\nIn Cheng Hao's polarized vision, a massive alert dialog box hung suspended above the doorframe, pulsing rapidly with alarming warning signs:\n\n> `[CRITICAL ALERT: TIMELINE PATCH v4.04 INSTALLED]`  \n> `[ANOMALY CODE: WEDNESDAY SYSTEM LOG QUARANTINED TO MAINFRAME]`  \n> `[UNAUTHORIZED MEMORY RESIDUE SCAN IN PROGRESS...]`\n\nAnd right beneath that flashing warning box, an extended sequence of luminous digital glyphs was branded directly onto the hallway wall!\n\n---\n\n## 四、牆上的加密警報 (IV. The Encrypted Warning on the Wall)\n\n\"Quick, Yijie, pen and paper!\" Cheng Hao grabbed her sleeve. \"There's glowing text on the wall—a string of numbers! They're fading fast!\"\n\nWithout hesitation, Yijie flipped open her notebook and uncapped her fountain pen. \"Read them to me!\"\n\nCheng Hao stared intently at the shimmering purple glyphs through the crystal lenses, reading at top speed:\n\n\"`04`... space... `15`... `14`... `20`!\"  \n\"Next group: `04`... `18`... `09`... `14`... `11`!\"  \n\"Final group: `13`... `09`... `12`... `11`!\"\n\nYijie's fountain pen flew across the paper with razor precision, leaving a crisp trail of ink:\n\n```\n04 - 15 - 14 - 20\n04 - 18 - 09 - 14 - 11\n13 - 09 - 12 - 11\n```\n\nThe moment Cheng Hao spoke the last syllable, the glowing numbers on the wall evaporated like droplets on a hot boiler, vanishing without a trace.\n\n\"Did you get them all?\" Cheng Hao panted, pushing the heavy goggles up onto his forehead. In an instant, the hallway reverted to its boring, sunlit everyday appearance.\n\n\"Every single one,\" Yijie replied, studying the three clusters of digits. The morning sun reflected sharply off her glasses.\n\nHer index finger tapped against the leather edge—her trademark habit whenever her mind hit overdrive.\n\n\"These aren't random numbers,\" Yijie analyzed coolly. \"No value exceeds 26, and they are arranged in paired two-digit blocks... Cheng Hao, this is the classic A1Z26 substitution cipher! Each number corresponds to the ordinal position of an English letter.\"\n\nUnderneath the numbers, Yijie quickly jotted down their alphabetical equivalents:\n\n* **Group 1:**\n  * 04 = **D**\n  * 15 = **O**\n  * 14 = **N**\n  * 20 = **T**\n  * ➜ **DONT**\n\n* **Group 2:**\n  * 04 = **D**\n  * 18 = **R**\n  * 09 = **I**\n  * 14 = **N**\n  * 11 = **K**\n  * ➜ **DRINK**\n\n* **Group 3:**\n  * 13 = **M**\n  * 09 = **I**\n  * 12 = **L**\n  * 11 = **K**\n  * ➜ **MILK**\n\nTogether, the deciphered words formed a complete, urgent sentence.\n\nYijie's breath caught in her throat.\n\n\"**DONT DRINK MILK**...\" Cheng Hao read the words aloud, his voice turning dry as dust. \"Don't... drink the milk?\"\n\n\"Milk?\" Yijie's head snapped up. \"Every morning after second period, the school hands out free bottles of—\"\n\n\"—the 'Smart-Brain High-Calcium Milk' sponsored by Gear Town Dairy Labs!\" Cheng Hao finished her sentence, his face turning ghostly pale.\n\n---\n\n## 五、致命的鈴聲 (V. The Deadly Chime)\n\n***CLANG—CLANG—CHIME—***\n\nThe very instant the words left Cheng Hao's mouth, the high-gain loudspeakers mounted along the corridor rafters screeched to life.\n\nIt was not the gentle, melodic chime that normally signaled morning recess. It was a sharp, grating, synthesized screech laced with high-frequency electrical static.\n\n\"Attention, all sixth-grade students,\" the vice principal's voice came through the intercom, calm to the point of being robotic. \"Today's nutritional supplement has been delivered to each homeroom. In accordance with the Smart Health Monitoring Initiative, all students must consume their milk within five minutes. Discarding or removing bottles from the classroom is strictly prohibited.\"\n\nSimultaneously, the heavy rumble of tank treads echoed from the far end of the corridor.\n\nA sealed, stainless-steel insulated cart was being pushed toward Class 6-1 by a cylindrical, barrel-bodied campus cleaning patrol robot. Stacked neatly upon the shelves were dozens of glass bottles of fresh milk, their plastic caps marked with faint cyan smart-chip labels.\n\nInside the classroom, cheerful shouts broke out as kids swarmed the cart as they did every morning, cracking the seals with laughter.\n\nCheng Hao frantically yanked the Ghost Goggles back over his eyes.\n\nA single glance nearly froze the marrow in his bones.\n\nUnder the ultraviolet spectrum of the goggles, tiny, luminous speckles of metallic silver floated inside every single bottle of milk—completely invisible to the naked eye! And suspended directly in the center of the classroom ceiling, an inverted funnel-shaped black transmitter had been installed, beaming continuous micro-pulses directly down upon the bottles!\n\nInside the room, his best friend Jiang Jiang had already peeled back the plastic seal. He tilted his head back, bringing the icy bottle to his lips—\n\n\"Jiang Jiang! Stop! DON'T DRINK IT!\"\n\nUnable to hold back for another second, Cheng Hao screamed at the top of his lungs and bolted toward the classroom doorway!\n\nThe instant his shout tore through the air, the cleaning patrol robot in the hallway lurched to a violent stop.\n\nIts optical scanner, which had been glowing with a peaceful green status light, snapped shut with a mechanical *clack*—and blazed alive in a furious, blood-red combat protocol!\n\nAt the same time, in the lower-right corner of Cheng Hao's goggles, a cascade of crimson system warnings erupted across the lens:\n\n> `[WARNING: UNAUTHORIZED SPECTRUM DETECTED]`  \n> `[ALERT: ILLEGAL OBSERVER IDENTIFIED]`  \n> `[TARGET LOCKED: CHENG HAO, CLASS 6-1, LU-YANG ELEMENTARY]`  \n> `[EXECUTING FORCED MEMORY OVERWRITE——PURGE PROTOCOL ENGAGED!]`\n\nDown the corridor, three cleaning robots pivoted on their treads simultaneously. Steel tracks shrieked against the polished ceramic floor as they extended heavy pneumatic capture claws, charging full throttle straight toward Cheng Hao!\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 1, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 第二章：會打摩斯的金屬魔術方塊\n\n## 一、走廊上的生死追逐\n\n三台原本笨重圓滾的清潔巡邏機器人，此刻像變成了三隻飢餓的金屬獵犬。\n\n它們眼部的LED螢幕閃爍著刺目的猩紅感嘆號，底部橡膠履帶在光滑的米黃色瓷磚地上瘋狂打滑，隨後伴隨著「刺啦——」一聲尖銳的摩擦巨響，猛然彈出兩根足足有一米長的銀灰色機械抓捕臂！\n\n「警告：非法觀察者！立刻停止行動，接受記憶校準！」\n\n冰冷無情的機械廣播在走廊裡迴盪。\n\n教室門口，將江還舉著那瓶鮮奶，嘴巴張得大大的，整個人徹底嚇傻了：「誠……誠浩？這幾台掃地機器人怎麼瘋了？它們怎麼長出鉗子來了？！」\n\n「趴下！」\n\n誠浩根本來不及多作解釋，整個人如同一頭敏捷的獵豹貼地飛撲過去！\n\n他的肩膀狠狠撞在將江的腰際，兩人一起滾進了教室門口。就在千鈞一髮之際，將江手裡那瓶「智慧健腦鮮乳」脫手飛出，重重砸在一台機器人的鋼鐵底盤上，「啪嚓」一聲粉碎！\n\n乳白色的液體濺了一地。\n\n透過額頭上的幽靈護目鏡，誠浩看得清清楚楚——地上的牛奶接觸到空氣的瞬間，那些微小的金屬螢光點竟然像有生命的納米蟲一樣劇烈蠕動，隨後化作縷縷極淡的紫煙消散在空氣中。\n\n「我的天……」將江摔得屁股生疼，看著滿地的碎片直揉眼睛。\n\n「沒時間發呆了！」\n\n這時，一隻纖細卻有力的手猛地抓住了誠浩的衣領。\n\n是葉旖緁！\n\n只見這位平日裡優雅冷靜的學霸班長，不知何時已經抄起了走廊消防栓旁邊的一把大號乾粉滅火器。她毫不猶豫地拔掉保險銷，雙手緊握噴管，對準衝在最前面的那台清潔機器人的光學鏡頭，狠狠按下了壓把！\n\n「噗——呼——！！」\n\n濃密刺鼻的白色乾粉如同暴風雪般呼嘯而出，劈頭蓋臉地將領頭的機器人噴了個正著！\n\n乾粉瞬間糊滿了機器人的光學感測器。猩紅色的電子眼在一片白茫茫中瘋狂閃爍，發出刺耳的系統報錯聲：\n\n`[光學鏡頭遮蔽度 98%……啟動聲納輔助……]`\n\n「幹得漂亮，旖緁！」誠浩大喊一聲，隨即從口袋裡抽出他的瑞士刀螺絲筆，按動側邊的紅色卡榫。\n\n「喀噠！」一根細長的平頭導電金屬探針彈了出來。\n\n誠浩趁著機器人原地轉圈重啟系統的兩秒空隙，一個滑鏟鑽到了機器人身後，準確無誤地將金屬探針狠狠刺入了機器人後頸處一條裸露的接地電線接口！\n\n「滋滋滋——劈啪！」\n\n一串耀眼的藍白色電火花瞬間爆開。\n\n那台重達六十公斤的清潔機器人渾身劇烈抽搐了一下，頭頂冒出一縷黑煙，機械臂軟綿綿地垂了下來，徹底癱瘓在地上。\n\n「還剩兩台！」旖緁丟掉空滅火器，一把拉起誠浩，「全校的安保系統都被驚動了，走廊盡頭的防火鐵捲門正在降下！去哪裡？」\n\n誠浩抬頭看去，只見走廊頂端的金屬鐵捲門正伴隨著刺耳的蜂鳴聲緩緩下壓。\n\n「舊校舍！」誠浩當機立斷，指向走廊側邊那扇通往老校區的木質防火門，「去三樓那間廢棄的舊物理實驗室！快跑！」\n\n---\n\n## 二、塵封的舊實驗室\n\n兩人推開生鏽的逃生通道小門，一路沿著狹窄昏暗的木質樓梯狂奔。\n\n身後傳來另外兩台機器人履帶碾過樓梯的沉重撞擊聲，以及防火門被機械臂瘋狂撞擊的巨響。\n\n鹿陽國小的舊校舍建於六十年前，據說是齒輪鎮第一代機械工程師們親手設計的。這裡的走廊鋪著老舊的柚木地板，空氣中瀰漫著機油、舊紙張與淡淡鐵鏽的味道。因為被列為危樓，平時根本沒有任何學生敢靠近。\n\n「砰！」\n\n誠浩反手將舊物理實驗室沉重的橡木大門重重甩上，順手拉下了兩道厚實的生鏽插銷。\n\n門外傳來履帶急停與金屬掃描光束掠過門縫的微弱「嗡嗡」聲，但由於舊校舍全由厚重的紅磚與鉛板隔音層構成，門外的機器人似乎暫時失去了信號鎖定，在走廊裡漫無目的地徘徊。\n\n實驗室內安靜得只能聽見兩人急促粗重的喘息聲。\n\n正午微弱的陽光透過積滿灰塵的毛玻璃窗灑進來，空氣中無數塵埃在光柱中緩緩起舞。\n\n「呼……呼……」旖緁扶著滿是灰塵的實驗台，推了推歪掉的金屬眼鏡，胸口劇烈起伏，「誠浩……剛才在走廊上，機器人發出的清除指令……鎖定的目標是你。這絕對不是單純的設備故障。」\n\n「我知道。」誠浩撫摸著頭上的黃銅護目鏡，目光凝重，「是因為這副護目鏡。它能看見不該看見的代碼。那些把昨天『星期三』抹掉的人，不希望任何人看破他們的把戲。」\n\n「那……你為什麼要帶我來這裡？」旖緁環顧四周。\n\n這間實驗室堆滿了落滿蛛網的老式天平、手搖發電機、還有幾具用黃銅齒輪組裝的機械天文儀模型。\n\n「因為我爺爺留給我的舊手冊裡，有一張泛黃的學校草圖。」誠浩走到實驗室最深處的一面老舊黑板前，「爺爺在手冊最後一頁寫著一句話：『如果你迷失在代碼的世界裡，去青木的根部，找尋金屬的心跳。』」\n\n「青木的根部……」旖緁喃喃道，「鹿陽國小在四十年前改名前，原本的名字就叫『青木私塾』！」\n\n「沒錯！」\n\n誠浩蹲下身子，鑽到了講台下方最角落的暗處。\n\n那裡放著一台早已報廢的舊式顯微鏡收納箱。誠浩用力將沉重的木箱挪開，地面上赫然出現了一塊由四顆巨大內六角螺絲固定的暗灰色鉛金屬暗格！\n\n暗格表面覆蓋著厚厚的油泥，正中央嵌著一個極其精巧的旋轉密碼鎖盤。\n\n---\n\n## 三、齒輪與質數的謎題\n\n「找到了！」誠浩興奮地喊道，連忙掏出螺絲筆擦掉表面的污垢。\n\n鉛金屬板上沒有鑰匙孔，只有三個獨立的金屬刻度轉盤，每個轉盤上刻著數字 `0` 到 `9`。\n\n而在轉盤上方，用工整的機械刻刀刻著三行泛著銅綠的謎題：\n\n```\n第一個數：十以內最大的質數。\n第二個數：一打的一半，除以最小的合數。\n第三個數：二進位數字「1001」所代表的十進位數值。\n```\n\n「三位數密碼鎖！」誠浩看著金屬板上的刻字，「這是我爺爺親手設計的防撬機關，如果連續輸入錯誤三次，裡面的自毀硫酸管就會融化所有東西！」\n\n「別慌，交給我。」\n\n旖緁蹲在暗格旁，眼神瞬间恢復了學霸專屬的冷靜與犀利。她盯著那三行刻字，大腦如同精密的超級電腦飛速運算。\n\n「第一行：『十以內最大的質數』。」旖緁開口，聲音平穩清晰，「十以內的質數有 2、3、5、7。其中最大的是——**7**！」\n\n誠浩點點頭，伸出手指，將第一個轉盤緩緩撥動。\n\n「咔、咔、咔……」金屬卡簧發出悅耳的脆響，停在數字 **7** 上。\n\n「第二行：『一打的一半，除以最小的合數』。」旖緁接著說，「一打是 12，一半就是 6。最小的合數不是 1，不是 2，不是 3，而是 4！等等……6 除以 4 不是整數！」\n\n誠浩的心臟猛地一跳：「不是整數？難道是餘數？還是小數點？」\n\n「冷靜，再讀一遍字面邏輯！」旖緁眉頭緊鎖，死死盯著那行刻字，「『一打的一半』……如果不是指數量呢？如果是指時鐘指針的一打（12小時）？不對……」\n\n突然，旖緁眼睛一亮：「看英文刻痕！在『合數』兩個字下方，有一道極淡的英文縮寫：`div`！在電腦程式語言裡，`div` 代表的是『整數除法，只取商數，捨去餘數』！6 除以 4，商數是 1，餘數是 2！所以只取商數——**1**！」\n\n「好！」誠浩深吸一口氣，將第二個轉盤精準地撥到了數字 **1**。\n\n「最後一個數：二進位數字『1001』。」旖緁嘴角微微揚起，露出一抹自信的微笑，「這對我們來說太簡單了。二進位從右往左權重分別是 1、2、4、8。『1001』就是：1 個 8，加 0 個 4，加 0 個 2，加 1 個 1。8 ＋ 1 等於——**9**！」\n\n「密碼是：**7 - 1 - 9**！」\n\n誠浩屏住呼吸，手指輕輕搭在第三個轉盤上，輕輕一推。\n\n「喀噠！」\n\n數字 **9** 歸位的剎那，鉛金屬暗格深處傳來了一陣極其複雜、連鎖反應般的金屬齒輪咬合聲！\n\n「滋——嗡——」\n\n一陣清脆的氣壓釋放聲響起，厚重的鉛板蓋子緩緩向上彈開了一道兩指寬的縫隙。\n\n---\n\n## 四、甦醒的摺紙柴犬\n\n誠浩與旖緁小心翼翼地合力掀開鉛板蓋。\n\n暗格裡面鋪著厚厚的紅色防震絲絨。而在絲絨的正中央，靜靜地躺著一枚巴掌大小的金屬立方體。\n\n那立方體通體泛著深邃的啞光銀色，外表面並不是光滑平整的，而是由數百片薄如蟬翼、交錯折疊的記憶合金薄片緊密咬合在一起，看起來就像一個精密無比的六面魔術方塊。\n\n「這就是……爺爺留下的東西？」誠浩伸出手，將那枚沉甸甸的金屬方塊捧在手心。\n\n方塊冰涼刺骨。\n\n但就在誠浩戴著護目鏡靠近的一瞬間，護目鏡鏡片上那圈微型光譜濾鏡忽然發出了一聲極輕的微鳴。\n\n護目鏡的鏡框與金屬方塊之間，似乎產生了一種看不見的磁場共振！\n\n「嗡——」\n\n金屬方塊正中央的一條微細縫隙中，突然亮起了一道清澈純淨的幽藍色光芒！\n\n緊接著，不可思議的一幕發生了——\n\n「喀噠！喀噠！喀噠！」\n\n一連串清脆如鐘錶齒輪跳動的機械響聲中，金屬方塊上的數百片合金薄片竟然如同活過來一般，優雅而繁複地向外層層展開！\n\n它的四角向外延伸，折疊出四條線條流暢的機械小短腿；金屬頂端翻轉升起，重組出一顆輪廓分明的柴犬腦袋，兩隻三角形的小耳朵敏銳地豎立起來；而在它的身後，一條由七節金屬環扣串連而成的小尾巴歡快地彈了出來！\n\n一隻由高科技記憶合金折疊而成的機械摺紙柴犬，活靈活現地站在了誠浩的手掌心上！\n\n它的兩隻眼睛是兩枚極小、極精密的幽藍色微型光學鏡頭，此時正微微轉動著，發出輕微的對焦聲。\n\n「哇……」旖緁忍不住輕呼出聲，眼睛裡滿是震撼，「這簡直是……機械工藝的奇蹟！」\n\n機械小狗歪了歪腦袋，藍色鏡頭在誠浩臉上的護目鏡上停留了兩秒，似乎完成了虹膜與設備識別。\n\n隨後，它歡快地從誠浩手掌上跳到了滿是灰塵的實驗台上，小鐵爪在木頭桌面上發出「噠噠噠」的清脆聲響。\n\n「嗶——啵！」\n\n小狗張開金屬小嘴，發出了一聲奶聲奶氣的電子音效。\n\n在它的金屬項圈上，一行極小的激光刻字清晰可見：\n\n`MODEL: PICO-001 (皮可)`\n\n「你叫皮可？」誠浩驚喜地看著它。\n\n皮可甩了甩小腦袋，似乎在表達肯定。但下一秒，它的藍色雙眼突然驟變為警惕的橙黃色！\n\n它的小鼻子在空氣中使勁嗅了嗅——那是它隱藏在高靈敏度鼻頭內的光譜與信號分析儀正在全速運轉。\n\n「嗒！嗒！嗒！——嗒嗒嗒！——嗒！嗒！嗒！」\n\n皮可的金屬尾巴突然高高豎起，開始以極快的頻率，重重敲擊在實驗台的一塊鋼質鐵板上！\n\n「他在敲東西？」誠浩一愣。\n\n「等等！別出聲！」旖緁猛地一把抓緊了黑皮筆記本，耳朵豎了起來，「三短、三長、三短……這是摩斯密碼！」\n\n---\n\n## 五、地下二樓的紅色座標\n\n旖緁手裡的鋼筆幾乎劃破紙面：\n\n「`···` 是 **S**！」  \n「`---` 是 **O**！」  \n「`···` 是 **S**！」  \n「它在發求救訊號？不對，後面還有！」\n\n皮可的尾巴敲擊節奏驟然變換，敲擊聲變得急促而連貫：\n\n「嗒嗒——嗒——（`··-` 是 **U**）」  \n「嗒——嗒嗒（`-··` 是 **D**）」  \n「嗒——（`-` 是 **T**）」  \n「嗒嗒嗒嗒（`····` 是 **H**）」  \n「嗒（`·` 是 **E**）」  \n「嗒——嗒（`--` 是 **M**）」  \n「嗒嗒（`··` 是 **I**）」  \n「嗒——嗒（`--` 是 **M**）」  \n「嗒嗒嗒（`···` 是 **S**）」  \n「嗒嗒——（`··-` 是 **U**）」  \n「嗒——嗒（`--` 是 **M**）」\n\n「**U - D - T - H - E - M - I - M - S - U - M**？」旖緁一邊拼讀，眉頭越皺越緊，「這根本不是英文單詞啊！難道是隨機亂碼？」\n\n「不，不是亂碼！」誠浩盯著皮可那雙緊張閃爍的眼睛，腦海中靈光一閃，「旖緁，把字母倒過來讀！或者……凱撒位移？」\n\n「等等！」旖緁的指尖在紙面上猛地一頓，倒抽一口冷氣，「將每個字母向前移位一位！U 前面是 T，D 前面是 C……不對，看單詞的分隔——」\n\n旖緁飛快地用斜線切開：\n\n`UD` ➡️ **UNDER**（地下）  \n`THE` ➡️ **THE**（那個）  \n`M-U-S-E-U-M` ➡️ **鐘樓地底博物館**！\n\n「**UNDER THE MUSEUM**！它說秘密在學校老鐘樓地下的舊校史博物館裡！」\n\n話音剛落，只見皮可胸口的一塊金屬板「啪」地彈開，一束強烈的高清全息光束從它胸膛投射到半空中！\n\n那是一張鹿陽國小立體的三維地下透視圖！\n\n在整座校舍的三維模型中，地下一樓是平平無奇的鍋爐房與庫房。但在地下一樓的正下方，赫然存在著一個巨大的、全校任何建築圖紙上都從未標記過的龐大空間！\n\n那個空間閃爍著觸目驚心的血紅色倒數計時光芒，正中央清晰地標註著四個燃燒著紅光的數字：\n\n> `[ZONE: UNDERGROUND B2]`  \n> `[ROOM 404: 核心中央處理室]`  \n> `[全鎮記憶永久重置倒數：47 小時 59 分 59 秒]`\n\n「地下二樓……404 室真的存在！」誠浩的心臟狂跳不已。\n\n然而，還沒等兩人喘過氣來，實驗室厚重的橡木大門突然傳來「咚！！」的一聲沉悶巨響！\n\n門縫下方，一束刺眼的藍色高溫切割激光「嗤嗤」冒著火星，正以恐怖的速度自上而下，將兩道生鏽的鐵插銷齊齊切斷！\n\n門外，傳來了一個經過機械變調、冰冷徹骨的聲音：\n\n「找到你們了，六年一班的小老鼠。」\n\n---\n\n*(第二章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第二章：會打摩斯的金屬魔術方塊 (Chapter 2: The Morse-Code Metal Cube)\n\n## 一、走廊上的生死追逐 (I. Life-and-Death Corridor Pursuit)\n\nThe three cleaning patrol androids, formerly clumsy and barrel-shaped, had transformed into a pack of ravenous metal hounds.\n\nBlinding crimson exclamation marks flickered across their optical LED screens. Their heavy rubber treads screeched against the polished cream floor tiles, and with a shrill, deafening metallic scrape, two three-foot-long silver-gray capture claws erupted from their chassis!\n\n\"WARNING: UNAUTHORIZED OBSERVER! CEASE MOVEMENT IMMEDIATELY AND SUBMIT TO MEMORY CALIBRATION!\"\n\nThe cold, synthesized robotic broadcast echoed violently down the hallway.\n\nBy the classroom doorway, Jiang Jiang stood frozen, holding his milk bottle high with his jaw dropped wide open in utter shock: \"Ch-Cheng Hao?! Have those floor sweepers gone crazy?! Why do they have giant steel claws?!\"\n\n\"GET DOWN!\"\n\nThere was zero time for explanations. Cheng Hao lunged across the floor like a sprinting leopard!\n\nHis shoulder slammed hard into Jiang Jiang's waist, sending both boys tumbling across the threshold. In that split second, the glass bottle of \"Smart-Brain High-Calcium Milk\" slipped from Jiang Jiang's fingers, crashing squarely onto the leading robot's armored treads and shattering with an explosive *crack*!\n\nMilky white liquid splattered in every direction across the floor.\n\nThrough the purple lenses of his Ghost Goggles, Cheng Hao witnessed something chilling—the instant the spilled milk hit the open air, the microscopic metallic flecks within squirmed frantically like living nanobots, then dissolved into faint tendrils of pale purple smoke and vanished.\n\n\"Sweet mother of gears...\" Jiang Jiang groaned, rubbing his bruised tailbone as he stared at the glittering glass shards.\n\n\"No time to daydream!\"\n\nA slender but iron-firm grip suddenly seized Cheng Hao by the back of his collar.\n\nIt was Ye Yijie!\n\nThe usually composed, poised top-student class president had already unhooked a heavy-duty industrial dry-chemical fire extinguisher from beside the corridor hydrant. Without hesitation, she ripped out the safety pin, aimed the nozzle straight at the lead robot's glowing optical sensor, and clamped down on the handle!\n\n*WHOOOOSH——!!*\n\nA blinding blizzard of dense, acrid white powder erupted with a roar, engulfing the front-running robot in an instant!\n\nThe white chemical cloud instantly coated the machine's optical lenses. Its scarlet sensor eyes flashed erratically amidst the whiteout, screeching with shrill error beeps:\n\n`[OPTICAL SENSOR VISIBILITY 2%... ENGAGING AUXILIARY SONAR NAVIGATION...]`\n\n\"Brilliant move, Yijie!\" Cheng Hao yelled. He pulled his multi-tool pen from his pocket and flicked the red side-latch.\n\n*Click!* A long, slender flathead conductive metal probe snapped out from the casing.\n\nSeizing the two-second window while the blinded robot spun in circles rebooting, Cheng Hao slid beneath its steel tracks, driving the metal probe with pinpoint accuracy straight into an exposed grounding port at the back of its neck!\n\n*Zzzzz-CRACKLE!*\n\nA bright cascade of electric blue sparks detonated outward.\n\nThe hundred-and-thirty-pound cleaning robot shuddered violently. A thin wisp of dark smoke curled from its head casing as its pneumatic claws went limp, collapsing onto the tiles in a completely paralyzed heap.\n\n\"Two more behind us!\" Yijie tossed aside the empty fire extinguisher cylinder and pulled Cheng Hao to his feet. \"The entire school's security grid has been triggered! The fire shutter gates at the end of the hall are descending! Where do we run?\"\n\nCheng Hao glanced down the corridor. Sure enough, heavy steel shutter gates were grinding downward from the ceiling rafters accompanied by shrill, blaring alarms.\n\n\"The Old Schoolhouse!\" Cheng Hao made a split-second decision, pointing toward a heavy wooden fire door along the side corridor that led to the vintage wing. \"Third floor, the abandoned physics lab! Run!\"\n\n---\n\n## 二、塵封的舊實驗室 (II. The Dust-Laden Old Lab)\n\nThe two threw open the rusted emergency exit door and dashed up the narrow, dimly lit wooden staircase.\n\nBehind them came the thundering impact of steel treads rattling against the wooden steps, accompanied by the violent pounding of mechanical claws against the fire door.\n\nLu-Yang Elementary's Old Schoolhouse had been erected sixty years ago, reportedly designed by Gear Town's very first generation of master mechanical engineers. Its hallways were lined with weathered teak floorboards, and the air carried a heavy nostalgic scent of machine oil, yellowed parchment, and oxidized brass. Because the building was marked as an aging structure, virtually no students ever dared approach it.\n\n*SLAM!*\n\nCheng Hao swung the massive oak door of the old physics laboratory shut behind them, throwing two heavy, rusted iron deadbolts firmly into place.\n\nOutside the door, the rumble of treads skidded to a halt. A faint ultrasonic hum indicated sensor beams sweeping across the door frame. But because the vintage wing was built with solid red brick and lead-insulated soundproofing panels, the patrol bots seemed to lose their lock, wandering aimlessly down the hallway outside.\n\nInside the vast room, the only sound was the two children's ragged, heavy panting.\n\nThin beams of midday sunlight streamed through the grime-caked frosted windows, illuminating countless specks of dust dancing lazily in the air.\n\n\"Phew... phew...\" Yijie leaned against a dusty workbench, pushing her crooked wire-rimmed glasses back up her nose as her chest heaved. \"Cheng Hao... that purge protocol out in the hall... it was locked directly onto you. That was definitely not a random hardware malfunction.\"\n\n\"I know,\" Cheng Hao said grimly, touching the brass frames of his goggles. \"It's because of these Ghost Goggles. They reveal data streams that were meant to remain hidden. Whoever wiped yesterday's 'Wednesday' from everyone's minds will stop at nothing to silence anyone who can see through the illusion.\"\n\n\"Then... why did you bring us here?\" Yijie asked, glancing around the laboratory.\n\nThe room was packed with vintage balances covered in cobwebs, hand-cranked generators, and intricate brass celestial armillary spheres fitted with miniature clockwork gears.\n\n\"Because inside the notebook my grandfather left me, there was a yellowed architectural sketch of the school,\" Cheng Hao walked toward an antique chalkboard at the back of the lab. \"On the final page, Grandpa wrote: *'If you ever find yourself lost in a world of fabricated code, go to the roots of the Green Tree and search for the metal heartbeat.'*\"\n\n\"'The roots of the Green Tree...'\" Yijie murmured. \"Before Lu-Yang Elementary was renamed forty years ago, its original name was 'Green Tree Academy'!\"\n\n\"Exactly!\"\n\nCheng Hao dropped to his knees, crawling beneath the shadowed corner of the lecture podium.\n\nHidden away in the shadows sat an antique microscope storage crate, abandoned decades ago. Cheng Hao heaved the heavy wooden crate aside. There on the floorboards, held fast by four heavy hex bolts, lay a dull gray lead-plated hatch!\n\nThe surface of the hatch was encrusted with decades of grime, but embedded squarely in its center was an exquisite, miniature combination lock dial.\n\n---\n\n## 三、齒輪與質數的謎題 (III. Riddles of Gears and Primes)\n\n\"Found it!\" Cheng Hao whispered with excitement, using his screwdriver pen to scrape the grime off the metal plate.\n\nThe lead plate had no keyhole. Instead, there were three independent metal dial wheels, each etched with digits from `0` to `9`.\n\nAbove the three dials, three lines of crisp text had been engraved with a jeweler's chisel, now tinted with green patina:\n\n```\nFirst Number: The largest prime number less than 10.\nSecond Number: Half of a dozen, div by the smallest composite number.\nThird Number: The decimal value of the binary string \"1001\".\n```\n\n\"A three-digit cipher lock!\" Cheng Hao read the engravings. \"This is Grandpa's tamper-proof lockbox. If someone inputs three wrong combinations in a row, an internal vial of sulfuric acid will shatter and dissolve everything inside!\"\n\n\"Don't panic. Leave it to me.\"\n\nYijie knelt beside the hidden compartment, her gaze snapping instantly back into her razor-sharp, analytical prodigy mode. Her mind raced like a high-speed supercomputer.\n\n\"First line: *'The largest prime number less than 10.'*\" Yijie spoke with crisp, steady clarity. \"The prime numbers below 10 are 2, 3, 5, and 7. The largest among them is—**7**!\"\n\nCheng Hao nodded, reaching out his index finger to turn the first dial slowly.\n\n*Click, click, click...* The spring detent settled with a satisfying snap directly on the number **7**.\n\n\"Second line: *'Half of a dozen, div by the smallest composite number.'*\" Yijie continued. \"A dozen is 12, so half is 6. The smallest composite number isn't 1, isn't 2, and isn't 3—it's 4! But wait... 6 divided by 4 isn't a whole integer!\"\n\nCheng Hao's heart skipped a beat: \"Not an integer? Is it a remainder? Or a decimal point?\"\n\n\"Stay calm. Read the syntax carefully!\" Yijie furrowed her brow, leaning closer to inspect the tiny letters. \"Half of a dozen... what if it's not a simple quantity? Could it mean a 12-hour clock face? No, that's not it...\"\n\nSuddenly, Yijie's eyes lit up: \"Look at the English engraving! Right beneath the word 'composite,' there's a faint operator abbreviation: `div`! In computer programming languages, `div` denotes integer division—taking only the quotient and discarding the remainder! 6 divided by 4 yields a quotient of 1 with a remainder of 2! Taking only the quotient gives us—**1**!\"\n\n\"Awesome!\" Cheng Hao exhaled, carefully rotating the second dial until it locked into the number **1**.\n\n\"Final number: the binary value of `1001`.\" A confident smile flickered across Yijie's lips. \"This one is second nature to us. Binary bit-weights from right to left are 1, 2, 4, and 8. So `1001` means: one 8, plus zero 4s, plus zero 2s, plus one 1. 8 plus 1 equals—**9**!\"\n\n\"The combination is: **7 - 1 - 9**!\"\n\nHolding his breath, Cheng Hao nudged the third dial wheel into place with his fingertip.\n\n*CLACK!*\n\nThe instant the number **9** clicked home, an intricate, domino-like cascade of tiny clockwork gears whirred to life deep inside the lead vault!\n\n*Hiss—whirrr—*\n\nA sharp hiss of released pneumatic pressure echoed through the chamber, and the heavy lead lid popped upward by two inches.\n\n---\n\n## 四、甦醒的摺紙柴犬 (IV. The Awakening of the Origami Shiba Inu)\n\nTogether, Cheng Hao and Yijie carefully lifted off the heavy lead lid.\n\nThe interior of the vault was lined with thick, crimson shock-absorbing velvet. Resting squarely in the center was a palm-sized metallic cube.\n\nThe cube gleamed with a deep, matte-silver luster. Its surface was far from plain; it consisted of hundreds of razor-thin, interlocking shape-memory alloy plates folded into one another with microscopic precision, resembling an astonishing six-sided mechanical Rubik's cube.\n\n\"Is this... what Grandpa left behind?\" Cheng Hao reached down, lifting the surprisingly dense metallic cube into his palm.\n\nThe metal felt icy against his skin.\n\nYet the moment Cheng Hao leaned in while wearing the Ghost Goggles, the miniature optical spectrometer etched into the rims let out a soft, melodic hum.\n\nAn invisible magnetic resonance flared between the brass goggles and the metal cube!\n\n*Hummmmm—*\n\nAlong a hairline seam down the center of the cube, a pulse of pure, ethereal cyan light flared to life!\n\nThen, an astonishing transformation unfolded before their eyes—\n\n*Click! Clack! Snap!*\n\nWith a rapid, rhythmic series of clockwork clicks, the hundreds of interlocking alloy plates unfolded outward in a breathtaking mechanical origami dance!\n\nIts four corners extended, folding into four sleek, articulate mechanical legs. The upper plates flipped and reassembled into the crisp silhouette of a Shiba Inu's head, two triangular ears perking up attentively. And from its rear, a playful little tail crafted from seven interlocking alloy rings snapped out with a cheerful flick!\n\nA mechanical origami Shiba Inu, folded from futuristic memory alloy, stood lively and proud upon Cheng Hao's open palm!\n\nIts twin eyes were tiny, high-precision optical lenses glowing with a gentle sapphire blue, whirring softly as they focused upon their surroundings.\n\n\"Incredible...\" Yijie gasped, her eyes shining with pure wonder. \"This is nothing short of... a mechanical masterpiece!\"\n\nThe mechanical pup tilted its head, its blue lens eyes locking onto Cheng Hao's goggles for two seconds, apparently completing an iris and device authentication scan.\n\nSatisfied, it hopped down from Cheng Hao's palm onto the dust-covered laboratory bench, its miniature steel paws tapping with crisp *patter-patter* beats across the wood.\n\n*Beep—boop!*\n\nThe little pup parted its metal jaws, emitting an endearing, synthesized electronic chirp.\n\nEtched in microscopic laser letters across its polished collar was a serial number:\n\n`MODEL: PICO-001 (PICO)`\n\n\"Your name is PICO?\" Cheng Hao smiled in delight.\n\nPICO shook its little head affirmatively. But in the very next second, its sapphire-blue eyes flared into a sharp, alarm-state amber yellow!\n\nIts nose twitched furiously in the air—the miniature optical spectrometer and radio signal analyzer concealed within its snout had spun up to full throttle.\n\n*Tap! Tap! Tap! — Tap-tap-tap! — Tap! Tap! Tap!*\n\nPICO's metallic tail snapped rigid, pounding in rapid-fire rhythm against a steel mounting plate on the workbench!\n\n\"What is it tapping?\" Cheng Hao blinked in surprise.\n\n\"Wait! Listen!\" Yijie clutched her notebook tightly, her ears tuning in to the cadence. \"Three short, three long, three short... that's Morse code!\"\n\n---\n\n## 五、地下二樓的紅色座標 (V. The Crimson Coordinates of Underground B2)\n\nYijie's fountain pen flew furiously across the page:\n\n\"`···` is **S**!\"  \n\"`---` is **O**!\"  \n\"`···` is **S**!\"  \n\"It's transmitting an SOS distress call? No, wait, there's more!\"\n\nPICO's tail shifted rhythm, tapping with crisp, continuous precision:\n\n\"Tap-tap—tap— (`··-` is **U**)\"  \n\"Tap—tap-tap (`-··` is **D**)\"  \n\"Tap— (`-` is **T**)\"  \n\"Tap-tap-tap-tap (`····` is **H**)\"  \n\"Tap (`·` is **E**)\"  \n\"Tap—tap (`--` is **M**)\"  \n\"Tap-tap (`··` is **I**)\"  \n\"Tap—tap (`--` is **M**)\"  \n\"Tap-tap-tap (`···` is **S**)\"  \n\"Tap-tap— (`··-` is **U**)\"  \n\"Tap—tap (`--` is **M**)\"\n\n\"**U - D - T - H - E - M - I - M - S - U - M**?\" Yijie read aloud, her brows knitting together into a deep knot. \"That's not an English word at all! Could it be random gibberish?\"\n\n\"No, it's not gibberish!\" Cheng Hao watched PICO's urgently flickering optics, a flash of insight striking him. \"Yijie, read it backward! Or... a Caesar shift?\"\n\n\"Wait!\" Yijie's pen halted on the paper, her breath catching. \"Shift each letter backward by one! Before U is T, before D is C... No, look at the word boundaries—\"\n\nYijie swiftly drew dividing slashes across the string:\n\n`UD` ➡️ **UNDER** (Beneath)  \n`THE` ➡️ **THE** (The)  \n`M-U-S-E-U-M` ➡️ **The Clock Tower Museum**!\n\n\"**UNDER THE MUSEUM**! It's saying the secret lies inside the historical museum beneath the old Clock Tower!\"\n\nThe moment the words were spoken, an alloy chest plate on PICO's torso snapped open with a sharp *clack*, projecting a brilliant, high-definition holographic beam into the air!\n\nIt was a glowing three-dimensional holographic blueprint of Lu-Yang Elementary's underground infrastructure!\n\nIn the model, Basement 1 appeared as ordinary boiler rooms and supply cellars. But directly beneath Basement 1, a colossal subterranean facility existed—one that had never been documented on any school blueprint!\n\nThat subterranean space pulsed with an alarming crimson countdown glow, emblazoned with four ominous lines of burning red data:\n\n> `[ZONE: UNDERGROUND B2]`  \n> `[ROOM 404: CENTRAL CORE PROCESSING CHAMBER]`  \n> `[PERMANENT TOWN-WIDE MEMORY PURGE COUNTDOWN: 47:59:59]`\n\n\"Underground B2... Room 404 really exists!\" Cheng Hao's pulse pounded in his ears.\n\nBefore either of them could catch their breath, a massive, bone-jarring *THUD!!* slammed against the laboratory's heavy oak door!\n\nAlong the crack beneath the door, a blinding blue beam of high-temperature cutting laser sputtered with fierce sparks, slicing downward through both rusted iron deadbolts at a terrifying speed!\n\nFrom outside in the corridor, a chilly, electronically synthesized voice drifted through the smoking fissure:\n\n\"Found you, little mice of Class 6-1.\"\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 2, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 第三章：圖書館的倒懸齒輪\n\n## 一、通風管道的大逃亡\n\n「滋啦——！！」\n\n伴隨著刺耳的電弧爆裂聲，最後一截燒得通紅的鐵插銷斷成兩截，重重砸在實驗室的水泥地上。\n\n沉重的橡木大門被一隻覆蓋著碳纖維裝甲的冰冷鋼手暴力推開！\n\n出現在門口的，並不是剛才走廊上那種笨拙圓滾的清潔機器人，而是一台通體漆黑、高達兩米的重型校園執法督導機。它的四肢修長，胸口印著鮮紅的「校園安全委員會」標誌，右臂末端還在冒著幽幽藍光的等離子切割刃正發出危險的高頻震顫。\n\n「偵測到 S 級違規學員……以及未登記的古代機械體。」\n\n執法機眼部的三枚光學鏡頭以不同角度旋轉鎖定，胸口的擴音喇叭發出如同兩塊鐵片互相刮擦的電子音：「立刻交出幽靈護目鏡與 PICO-001，重置程序將免除肉體懲罰。」\n\n「免除你個大頭鬼！」\n\n誠浩大喊一聲，隨手抄起實驗台上的一瓶過期硫酸銅溶液，狠狠朝著執法機的面部砸去！\n\n「啪！」\n\n玻璃瓶在執法機的合金面罩上粉碎，藍色液體濺滿了它的鏡頭。執法機被激怒了，巨大的機械臂橫掃而來，將半張沉重的實木實驗台像豆腐一樣直接拍成兩半！木屑在空中瘋狂炸裂！\n\n就在這千鈞一髮的生死關頭，站在誠浩肩膀上的機械摺紙犬皮可動了！\n\n「喀噠！嘩啦啦——」\n\n皮可身上的記憶合金薄片瞬間如孔雀開屏般向兩側爆散開來。它沒有逃跑，反而化作一道銀色的金屬殘影，閃電般撲到了執法機的面部！\n\n「嗶！嗶！嗶！」\n\n皮可的小金屬爪精準地卡進了執法機的光學鏡頭縫隙中，尾巴更是瘋狂敲擊對方的天線插槽，激發出一串劈啪作響的短路電火花！\n\n「系統視線受阻……啟動過載清理……」執法機被干擾得瘋狂揮舞雙臂試圖抓下皮可。\n\n「誠浩！看上方！」旖緁急促地拉了拉誠浩的衣角，手指指向實驗室天花板的角落。\n\n在那裡，有一面用四顆生鏽蝶形螺母固定的鐵絲網通風口。因為長年未經修繕，其中兩顆螺母已經鬆脫，露出了一個勉強能容納一個少年鑽進去的方形管道口。\n\n「皮可，撤退！」誠浩大喊，同時從口袋掏出螺絲筆，兩步跨上倒塌的櫃子，飛快地擰掉剩下兩顆生鏽螺母。\n\n鐵絲網應聲落地！\n\n聽到主人呼喚的皮可，「喀噠」一聲收縮四肢，再次縮成了一顆光滑的銀色魔術方塊，從空中劃過一道完美的拋物線，穩穩落進了誠浩的連帽衫口袋裡。\n\n「旖緁，快上去！」\n\n誠浩雙手在下托住旖緁的運動鞋，用力往上一頂。旖緁身手敏捷地攀住管道邊緣，雙腿一蹬便滑了進去。\n\n誠浩回頭看了一眼正重新對準目標的執法機，縱身一躍，雙手抓緊通風管道边缘，整個人像泥鰍一樣鑽進了漆黑的管道中。\n\n「轟——！」\n\n一道熾熱的藍色激光擦著誠浩的鞋底掠過，將他們剛剛踩過的櫃子瞬間熔成一灘冒煙的焦炭！\n\n---\n\n## 二、百年圖書館的秘密\n\n漆黑狹窄的通風管道裡積滿了乾燥的灰塵。\n\n管道順著舊校舍的牆體一路向下傾斜。皮可從誠浩的口袋裡探出金屬腦袋，兩隻幽藍色的微型鏡頭如同兩盞明亮的手電筒，在前方投射出清晰的光錐。\n\n「順著這個坡度……我們正在離開舊教學樓，穿過中央花園的地下。」旖緁一邊手腳並用地向前爬，一邊在心中默默計算距離與方位，「前面有風聲，還有一種奇怪的香味……」\n\n「那是陳年樟木和舊書頁的氣味。」誠浩抹了一把臉上的灰塵，「我們到了！」\n\n前方的管道出口是一面雕花銅鑄百葉窗。誠浩用手肘輕輕一頂，生鏽的銅鎖扣便啪嗒一聲斷裂。\n\n兩人一狗悄無聲息地從兩米高的通風口滑落，穩穩踩在一張鋪著厚重紅色織花地毯的地板上。\n\n當他們站直身體抬頭看去時，眼前的景象讓兩人都屏住了呼吸。\n\n這裡是鹿陽國小歷史最悠久、平時幾乎不對外開放的——**百年圖書館**。\n\n不同於現代化教學樓那種到處充斥著塑膠感與液晶螢幕的冰冷風格，這座圖書館足足有三層樓高，四周環繞著高聳入雲的深色胡桃木書架，數萬本精裝古籍散發著寧靜厚重的書香。\n\n但最震撼人心的，是圖書館那高達十幾米的穹頂。\n\n在那裡，懸掛著一整片極其壯觀、純黃銅鑄造的**「倒懸齒輪群」**！\n\n數百個大小不一、直徑從十幾公分到三公尺不等的巨大機械齒輪，如同倒掛在天花板上的金色鐘乳石林。它們與學校頂樓的大鐘樓鐘擺由粗大的鋼纜相連。平時，這些齒輪處於靜止狀態，只有在正午十二點鐘聲響起時，才會伴隨著齒輪咬合的轟鳴聲轉動半圈。\n\n「太美了……」誠浩仰望著穹頂那些精美絕倫的機械齒輪，身為發明愛好者的他，眼睛裡閃爍著純粹的狂熱。\n\n「別光顧著發呆，誠浩。」旖緁推了推眼鏡，目光警惕地掃過一排排幽暗的書架，「皮可剛才的摩斯密碼說的是『UNDER THE MUSEUM』（在博物館地下）。這座圖書館的一樓後半部分，正是鹿陽國小的校史文物展覽館。」\n\n皮可從誠浩的肩頭跳到地毯上，小巧的金屬爪子踩著小碎步，直奔圖書館正中央那座巨大的黑色大理石立柱。\n\n大理石立柱下，立著一具一米多高的純銅黃道十二宮渾天儀，底座上刻著一行磨損嚴重的銅字銘文：\n\n> **「知識是開啟地底之門的槓桿，真理藏於第三類的分界之中。」**\n\n---\n\n## 三、索書號與圖書密碼\n\n「看這裡！」\n\n誠浩指著渾天儀的底座。\n\n原本擺放銘牌的地方，不知被誰用鋒利的尖刀刻出了一串奇怪的圖書館索書號索引：\n\n```\n[標靶書籍一]：823.91 / 04-A（第三章，第五個單詞）\n[標靶書籍二]：510.1 / 18-B（第一頁，第十個單詞）\n[標靶書籍三]：621.8 / 09-C（目錄頁，倒數第二個單詞）\n```\n\n而在這三行索書號下方，是一個刻在石柱上的六角形凹槽，凹槽周圍環繞著一個微型的黃銅小齒輪。\n\n「這是典型的『書本加密法』（Book Cipher）！」旖緁的眼中閃過解開謎題的興奮光芒，「有人把開啟機關的密鑰，藏在了這座圖書館的特定書籍裡！」\n\n「可是這裡有幾萬本書！」誠浩抓了抓頭髮，「我們要怎麼在幾分鐘內找到這三本？」\n\n「不用幾萬本，這就是索書號（Classification Number）的意義！」旖緁迅速走向圖書館入口處的一張巨大的木質分類導引牌：\n\n「聽好，誠浩！在中國圖書分類法與杜威十進位分類法中：」  \n「**800 號段**是『文學類』！823 代表英美小說，在二樓東側的木書架！」  \n「**500 號段**是『自然科學與數學類』！510 代表純數學，在一樓左側第四排！」  \n「**600 號段**是『應用科學與工程技術』！621 代表機械工程與儀器，就在一樓右側靠窗那排！」\n\n「分頭找！」誠浩說。\n\n「不用分頭，皮可的速度比我們快得多！」\n\n旖緁蹲下身，輕輕拍了拍皮可的小腦袋：「皮可，去一樓右側找 `621.8 / 09-C`，它的書脊上應該印著齒輪相關的標籤！」\n\n皮可「嗶啵」叫了一聲，四條小短腿化作一團銀色的旋風，「嗖」地一聲竄進了一樓深邃的書架深處。\n\n而誠浩與旖緁則分別衝向一樓的數學區與二樓的文學區。\n\n時間在一分一秒地流逝。\n\n整座空曠安靜的圖書館裡，只剩下兩人急促翻動書脊的沙沙聲。\n\n「找到數學書了！」\n\n一樓傳來旖緁輕快而壓抑的聲音。她手裡拿著一本泛黃的硬皮大部頭——《高階微積分與質數分佈原則》，索書號正是 `510.1 / 18-B`！\n\n旖緁迅速翻到第一頁，指尖在密密麻麻的鉛字上飛快劃過：「一、二、三……九、十！第十個單詞是——**CLOCKWISE**（順時針）！」\n\n同一時刻，二樓的誠浩也從一本厚重的《福爾摩斯回憶錄》書架前抽出了一本厚度驚人的英文古籍，索書號 `823.91 / 04-A`。\n\n誠浩翻開第三章，數到第五個單詞。\n\n那是福爾摩斯在開展調查時說的第一句話。第五個單詞赫然是——**THREE**（三）！\n\n「我這邊是『THREE』，數字三！」誠浩趴在二樓木欄杆上朝樓下喊道。\n\n就在這時，皮可也嘴裡叼著一本厚重破舊的《十九世紀精密鐘錶齒輪圖鑑》（`621.8 / 09-C`）歡快地跑了回來，將書穩穩放在渾天儀旁邊的地毯上。\n\n旖緁立刻翻開該書的目錄頁，目光鎖定在倒數第二個單詞上：\n\n「**REVERSE**（反轉／逆時針）！」\n\n三個單詞拼湊在一起，就是這座機關的完整操作手冊：\n\n> **`順時針 (CLOCKWISE)` ➡️ `三圈 (THREE)` ➡️ `逆時針反轉 (REVERSE)`！**\n\n---\n\n## 四、穹頂的轟鳴\n\n「天啊，這不是密碼，這是齒輪轉盤的旋轉指令！」誠浩三步併作兩步從二樓旋轉樓梯飛奔而下。\n\n他蹲在渾天儀底座前，握住那個六角形凹槽周圍的黃銅小齒輪。\n\n「準備好了嗎？」誠浩看向旖緁和皮可。\n\n「轉吧！」旖緁握緊了拳頭。\n\n誠浩深吸一口氣，將渾天儀上的黃銅小齒輪緩緩向**順時針**方向轉動。\n\n「咔！咔！咔！」\n\n清脆的金屬彈簧卡榫聲在寂靜的圖書館中格外清晰。\n\n第一圈……第二圈……第三圈！\n\n當第三圈精準歸位的瞬間，誠浩立刻將齒輪猛然向**逆時針**方向用力一掰！\n\n「轟——咔隆隆隆——！！」\n\n剎那間，整座圖書館劇烈地震顫起來！\n\n天花板上積沉了數十年的灰塵如雪花般簌簌落下，穹頂那片原本宛如沉睡死物般的**倒懸齒輪群**，在此刻竟然奇蹟般地全部活了過來！\n\n直徑三公尺的主驅動齒輪率先咬合，帶動周圍數十個次級黃銅齒輪以驚人的機械韻律瘋狂旋轉！金屬與金屬撞擊摩擦出的沉悶轟鳴，宛如某種沉睡地底巨獸的心跳！\n\n「看大理石地面！」旖緁驚呼。\n\n圖書館中央，原本堅固平整的六邊形大理石地磚，隨著天花板齒輪的牽引，伴隨著厚重的氣壓釋放聲，一塊接一塊地向兩側平移縮回！\n\n一條寬闊、筆直、由深色玄武岩打磨而成的旋轉石階，在地面正中央緩緩向下展開，直通那連光線都無法穿透的漆黑地底！\n\n一股冰涼刺骨、帶著陳年金屬電纜燒焦味的冷風，從洞口深處撲面而來。\n\n「這就是……通往地下二樓的入口。」誠浩拉下額頭上的護目鏡。\n\n在幽靈護目鏡的視野中，這道旋轉石階的兩側扶手上，流淌著如瀑布般瘋狂下墜的淡藍色數據光瀑，而在石階的最深處，隱隱閃爍著一個鮮紅色的數字：**404**。\n\n---\n\n## 五、鏡像中的腳步聲\n\n「我們成功了！」誠浩臉上露出興奮的笑容。\n\n然而，還沒等他們邁出第一步，皮可身上的記憶合金薄片突然在一瞬間全部炸立了起來！\n\n就像一隻炸了毛的金屬小刺蝟，皮可發出了前所未有的尖銳電子警報：\n\n「嗶————！！」\n\n它的小腦袋死死轉向圖書館正門的方向，雙眼瞬間轉變為象徵極度危險的**血紅色**！\n\n「踏……踏……踏……」\n\n一陣極其規律、皮鞋踩在木質地板上的清脆腳步聲，從圖書館大門外幽暗的長廊裡不疾不徐地傳來。\n\n那不是機器人的履帶聲，那是人類的腳步聲。\n\n一道高大修長的身影穿過門廊的陰影，緩緩走進了圖書館微弱的陽光下。\n\n他穿著一身平整乾淨的深藍色針織衫，胸前別著鹿陽國小的教師徽章，臉上掛著熟悉而溫和的微笑。\n\n「高……高老師？！」旖緁不敢置信地後退了半步。\n\n那是六年一班的班導師，平日裡和藹可親、總是耐心解答大家問題的高老師。\n\n「誠浩，旖緁。」\n\n高老師微笑著停下腳步，聲音溫潤如初，像平時在課堂上關心同學一樣親切：「第四節課已經開始了，你們兩個怎麼會在這裡惡作劇，還把圖書館弄得這麼亂呢？」\n\n誠浩剛想開口解釋，然而，當他透過黃銅護目鏡看向高老師的那一瞬間——\n\n誠浩的雙腳徹底釘死在原地，一股寒氣從腳底板直衝天靈蓋！\n\n在護目鏡的特殊光譜視野裡，站在他們面前的根本不是一個活生生的人！\n\n在高老師那張精緻逼真的「人臉」後方，正不斷閃爍著密密麻麻的綠色代碼串與全息投影掃描線！更令人毛骨悚然的是，高老師左半邊臉頰的皮膚正出現一陣微小的「信號撕裂」，露出裡面由精密金屬齒輪與電路板構成的骷髏狀機械骨架！\n\n「高老師」臉上的笑容沒有絲毫改變，但他發出的聲音，卻在下半句驟然變換成了剛才那台重型執法機的冰冷金屬合成音：\n\n「把護目鏡交出來吧……**否則，我不保證你們能完整地升上國中。**」\n\n話音未落，圖書館上方那扇厚重的青銅防盜大門，在一聲沉悶的巨響中，徹底重重合死！\n\n唯一的退路，只剩下身後那口深不見底的玄武岩黑洞！\n\n---\n\n*(第三章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第三章：圖書館的倒懸齒輪 (Chapter 3: The Inverted Gears in the Library)\n\n## 一、通風管道的大逃亡 (I. The Great Air-Duct Escape)\n\n\"SCREEECH—CRACKLE—!!\"\n\nWith a deafening burst of electrical arcs, the final glowing segment of the sheared iron bolt snapped in two, clattering heavily onto the lab's concrete floor.\n\nThe reinforced oak door was forcefully shoved inward by an armored fist sheathed in matte-black carbon fiber!\n\nFramed in the doorway was no clumsy, cylindrical floor-sweeping android. Standing over six feet tall was an imposing, heavy-duty Campus Security Enforcer. Its limbs were sleek and elongated, its armored breastplate emblazoned with the scarlet insignia of the \"Campus Security Committee.\" At the tip of its right forearm, a plasma-cutting emitter flickered with pale blue light, humming with hazardous high-frequency vibrations.\n\n\"Target identified: S-Rank Non-Compliant Students... and unregistered antique automaton.\"\n\nThe three optical lenses in the enforcer's helmet rotated independently to lock coordinates. Its internal loudspeaker crackled like iron plates grating against each other: \"Relinquish the Ghost Goggles and PICO-001 immediately. Submitting to memory reset will exempt subjects from physical reprimand.\"\n\n\"Exempt this, you overgrown toaster!\"\n\nCheng Hao bellowed, snatching an expired glass bottle of copper sulfate solution from the nearest workbench and hurling it with all his might straight at the enforcer's faceplate!\n\n*SMASH!*\n\nThe glass shattered against the alloy mask, splashing blue liquid across its sensor lenses. Enraged, the enforcer swept its massive hydraulic arm sideways, cleaving a solid oak lab table in half as if it were soft tofu! Splinters exploded through the air!\n\nIn that razor-thin fraction of a second, the origami Shiba Inu perched on Cheng Hao's shoulder sprang into action!\n\n*Clack-clack! SHING——*\n\nThe shape-memory alloy plates across PICO's body fanned outward like a peacock's plumage. Instead of retreating, the pup blurred into a silver streak, lunging straight at the enforcer's helmet!\n\n*BEEP! BEEP! BEEP!*\n\nPICO's tiny steel paws wedged themselves directly into the optical sensor seams. Its tail hammered frantically against the enforcer's external radio antenna, triggering a wild spray of spitting blue short-circuit sparks!\n\n\"Sensory array compromised... initiating thermal purge override...\" The enforcer flailed its massive arms in fury, trying to swat the metallic pup away.\n\n\"Cheng Hao! Look up!\" Yijie yanked hard on his sleeve, pointing toward the upper corner of the high ceiling.\n\nThere, bolted behind four weathered wing nuts, was a wire-mesh ventilation grate. Decades of neglect had loosened two of the rusted nuts, exposing an opening just wide enough for a slender middle-schooler to squeeze through.\n\n\"PICO, disengage!\" Cheng Hao shouted. Pulling his screwdriver pen from his pocket, he bounded onto an overturned filing cabinet and swiftly loosened the remaining two rusted wing nuts.\n\nThe wire mesh clattered to the floor!\n\nAt its master's call, PICO snapped its limbs inward with a crisp *click*, collapsing back into a sleek silver Rubik's cube. Sailing through the air in a graceful arc, it landed squarely into the front pocket of Cheng Hao's hoodie.\n\n\"Yijie, go!\"\n\nCheng Hao cupped his hands under Yijie's sneakers and hoisted her upward with all his strength. With athletic agility, Yijie caught the lip of the duct, swung her legs up, and slipped inside.\n\nCheng Hao glanced back at the enforcer recalibrating its plasma blade. He leaped upward, gripped the duct rim, and wriggled into the dark shaft like an eel.\n\n*BOOOM——!*\n\nA blistering lance of azure laser heat grazed the soles of Cheng Hao's shoes, vaporizing the wooden cabinet below into a smoking heap of charred embers!\n\n---\n\n## 二、百年圖書館的秘密 (II. Secrets of the Century-Old Library)\n\nThe cramped ventilation duct was cloaked in darkness and coated in decades of dry dust.\n\nThe conduit sloped downward along the interior of the Old Schoolhouse's thick masonry walls. PICO poked its metallic head out of Cheng Hao's hoodie pocket, twin sapphire lenses shining like miniature spotlights to project a bright cone of illumination ahead.\n\n\"Judging by this incline... we've left the old classrooms behind and are passing beneath the central courtyard gardens,\" Yijie whispered, crawling forward on hands and knees while mentally calculating trajectory and distance. \"I hear air currents ahead... and a strange, wonderful fragrance...\"\n\n\"That's aged camphor wood and antique paper,\" Cheng Hao wiped grime from his brow. \"We're here!\"\n\nAt the end of the duct sat an ornate, cast-bronze louvered vent. Cheng Hao pressed against it with his elbow; the corroded brass latch gave way with a muted snap.\n\nThe two kids and one mechanical pup slid silently down from the six-foot drop, landing softly upon a thick, crimson floral-woven carpet.\n\nWhen they stood up and looked around, the breathtaking spectacle before them stole the air from their lungs.\n\nThey had arrived inside Lu-Yang Elementary's oldest, most revered sanctuary—the **Century-Old Library**.\n\nFar removed from the sterile plastic panels and cold digital LCD monitors of the modern school wings, this majestic library rose three full stories high. Massive, floor-to-ceiling walnut bookcases encircled the rotunda, holding tens of thousands of leather-bound volumes that radiated a serene, scholarly hush.\n\nYet what commanded absolute awe was the vaulted ceiling nearly fifty feet overhead.\n\nSuspended across the entire expanse of the grand dome was a breathtaking, colossal array of solid-brass **Inverted Clockwork Gears**!\n\nHundreds of mechanical spur and bevel gears—ranging in diameter from a few inches to ten feet wide—hung suspended like a golden forest of clockwork stalactites. Heavy steel cables connected this mechanical labyrinth to the pendulum shaft of the campus clock tower above. Usually, the entire ceiling array remained motionless, turning half a revolution only when the massive noon bell chimed.\n\n\"Incredible...\" Cheng Hao murmured, staring upward at the mechanical wonder. As an inventor, pure passion ignited in his eyes.\n\n\"Don't get lost in admiration, Cheng Hao,\" Yijie pushed her glasses up, scanning the shadowy book aisles. \"PICO's Morse code said *'UNDER THE MUSEUM.'* The ground floor rotunda behind this library serves as the campus Historical Archives.\"\n\nPICO leaped down to the carpet, pattering rapidly toward a massive black marble pillar in the very center of the hall.\n\nAt the foot of the pillar stood a three-foot-tall bronze armillary sphere depicting the twelve signs of the zodiac. Chiseled into its base was a worn inscription:\n\n> **\"Knowledge is the lever that unseals the subterranean gate; truth resides within the division of the third domain.\"**\n\n---\n\n## 三、索書號與圖書密碼 (III. Classification Numbers and the Book Cipher)\n\n\"Look down here!\"\n\nCheng Hao pointed at the base of the armillary sphere.\n\nWhere a nameplate should have sat, someone had carefully scratched three cryptic library call numbers into the bronze with a hardened steel stylus:\n\n```\n[Target Book 1]: 823.91 / 04-A (Chapter 3, Fifth Word)\n[Target Book 2]: 510.1 / 18-B (Page 1, Tenth Word)\n[Target Book 3]: 621.8 / 09-C (Table of Contents, Second-to-Last Word)\n```\n\nDirectly below these three lines of call numbers was a hexagonal recess carved into the stone pillar, bordered by a tiny brass spur gear.\n\n\"A classic Book Cipher!\" A thrill of intellectual excitement sparked in Yijie's eyes. \"Someone concealed the operational key inside specific volumes within this library!\"\n\n\"There are tens of thousands of books here!\" Cheng Hao ruffled his hair. \"How do we locate three specific books in just a few minutes?!\"\n\n\"We don't need to search tens of thousands—that is the beauty of classification numbers!\" Yijie strode purposefully toward a massive wooden catalog directory mounted near the library rotunda entrance:\n\n\"Listen carefully, Cheng Hao! Under the Dewey Decimal and library classification systems:\"  \n\"**The 800s** are *Literature*! 823 designates English Fiction—second floor, eastern walnut shelving!\"  \n\"**The 500s** are *Natural Sciences and Mathematics*! 510 designates Pure Mathematics—ground floor, fourth aisle on the left!\"  \n\"**The 600s** are *Applied Sciences and Technology*! 621 designates Mechanical Engineering and Instrumentation—ground floor, right aisle by the windows!\"\n\n\"Divide and conquer!\" Cheng Hao said.\n\n\"No need—PICO is ten times faster than either of us!\"\n\nYijie knelt down and tapped PICO's metallic head gently: \"PICO, head to the right aisle on the ground floor and fetch `621.8 / 09-C`. The spine should feature gear and clockwork emblems!\"\n\nPICO gave a cheerful *beep-boop*, its four little legs blurring into a silver cyclone as it vanished into the labyrinth of ground-floor shelving.\n\nMeanwhile, Cheng Hao dashed toward the second-floor literature gallery, while Yijie sprinted to the mathematics section on the ground floor.\n\nSeconds ticked by with agonizing weight.\n\nIn the vast, silent hall, the only sound was the rustle of fingertips skimming across aged book spines.\n\n\"Found the math volume!\"\n\nYijie's hushed, triumphant voice echoed from below. In her hands was a yellowed, cloth-bound tome titled *Advanced Calculus and Principles of Prime Distributions*, bearing call number `510.1 / 18-B`!\n\nYijie turned to page one, running her finger along the dense typography: \"One, two, three... nine, ten! The tenth word is—**CLOCKWISE**!\"\n\nAt the exact same moment on the second-floor gallery, Cheng Hao pulled an enormous vintage English volume from beside the Sherlock Holmes collection, call number `823.91 / 04-A`.\n\nCheng Hao flipped to chapter three, counting across the opening line.\n\nIt was the very first sentence spoken by Holmes upon starting his investigation. The fifth word was unmistakably—**THREE**!\n\n\"My word is 'THREE'!\" Cheng Hao called over the second-floor banister.\n\nRight on cue, PICO came trotting proudly back across the carpet, carrying a heavy, leather-bound volume in its jaws: *Compendium of Nineteenth-Century Precision Horological Gearing* (`621.8 / 09-C`). It deposited the book neatly beside the armillary sphere.\n\nYijie opened the table of contents, zeroing in on the second-to-last word:\n\n\"**REVERSE**!\"\n\nPutting the three words together revealed the complete operational instructions:\n\n> **`CLOCKWISE` ➡️ `THREE (rotations)` ➡️ `REVERSE`!**\n\n---\n\n## 四、穹頂的轟鳴 (IV. Thunder in the Vaulted Dome)\n\n\"It isn't a text password—it's a mechanical rotation sequence!\" Cheng Hao vaulted down the spiral stairs two steps at a time.\n\nHe dropped beside the base of the armillary sphere, gripping the miniature brass gear encircling the hexagonal socket.\n\n\"Ready?\" Cheng Hao looked at Yijie and PICO.\n\n\"Turn it!\" Yijie clenched her fists.\n\nTaking a deep breath, Cheng Hao began rotating the brass dial firmly in a **clockwise** direction.\n\n*Click! Click! Click!*\n\nCrisp spring-loaded detents snapped with mechanical precision in the quiet rotunda.\n\nOne full turn... two full turns... three full turns!\n\nThe instant the third rotation clicked into alignment, Cheng Hao threw all his weight into wrenching the gear in **reverse**!\n\n*BOOM——RUUUUUUMBLE——!!*\n\nIn an instant, the entire century-old library shuddered violently!\n\nDecades of dust rained down from the rafters like falling snow as the colossal array of **Inverted Gears** across the vaulted dome miraculously roared to life!\n\nA ten-foot master driving wheel engaged first, its teeth meshing into dozens of secondary brass gears that spun in stunning mechanical harmony! The deep, rhythmic percussion of interlocking bronze teeth shook the air like the heartbeat of an underground titan!\n\n\"Look at the marble floor!\" Yijie cried out.\n\nIn the center of the rotunda, the polished hexagonal marble flagstones began sliding backward beneath the floorboards in rhythmic succession, accompanied by the hiss of pneumatic pressure release!\n\nA wide, spiral staircase carved from dark basalt unfolded steadily downward into the earth, descending into an abyss so deep that ambient light could not penetrate!\n\nAn icy, subterranean draft carrying the faint tang of aged electrical ozone surged upward from the depths.\n\n\"The entrance to Underground B2...\" Cheng Hao pulled down his goggles.\n\nThrough the Ghost Goggles, cascading streams of cyan digital code flowed like waterfalls along the stone banisters, while deep within the stairwell, a glowing crimson number pulsed in the dark: **404**.\n\n---\n\n## 五、鏡像中的腳步聲 (V. Footsteps in the Reflection)\n\n\"We found it!\" Cheng Hao's face broke into a broad grin.\n\nYet before they could take their first step downward, every memory-alloy plate on PICO's body snapped rigid!\n\nBristling like an agitated metallic porcupine, PICO unleashed an ear-piercing electronic alarm:\n\n*BEEEEEEP————!!*\n\nThe pup's head whipped toward the main library entrance, its sapphire optics flaring instantly into an ominous **blood-red**!\n\n*Step... step... step...*\n\nA measured, rhythmic cadence of polished leather shoes echoing against parquet floorboards drifted from the shadowy entrance corridor.\n\nIt was not the rumble of robot tracks. It was the deliberate footsteps of a human being.\n\nA tall, poised silhouette stepped out from the shadows and into the dim shaft of afternoon sunlight.\n\nHe wore a neat, navy-blue knit sweater, a Lu-Yang Elementary faculty pin affixed to his chest, his face bearing a warm, familiar smile.\n\n\"M-Mr. Gao?!\" Yijie stumbled back half a step in disbelief.\n\nIt was their sixth-grade homeroom teacher—the ever-patient, gentle mentor who answered their every question.\n\n\"Cheng Hao, Yijie.\"\n\nMr. Gao came to a gentle halt, his voice smooth and caring, exactly like a teacher checking in on students after class: \"Fourth period has already begun. Why are you two playing pranks down here and making such a mess of the library?\"\n\nCheng Hao opened his mouth to reply. But the instant his eyes locked onto Mr. Gao through the brass Ghost Goggles—\n\nCheng Hao froze solid, an icy chill rocketing straight up his spine!\n\nIn the polarized spectrum of the goggles, the figure standing before them was no living human at all!\n\nBehind Mr. Gao's lifelike synthetic \"skin,\" dense matrices of green machine code and holographic scan-lines flickered continuously! More terrifying still: across his left cheek, a micro-glitch tore through the projection, revealing a terrifying skull-like armature of precision steel gears and glowing circuit boards beneath!\n\nThe warm smile remained plastered across \"Mr. Gao's\" face, but the second half of his sentence transformed into the chilling, synthesized drone of the heavy enforcer:\n\n\"Surrender the goggles... **or I cannot guarantee you will advance to middle school in one piece.**\"\n\nBefore his words finished echoing, the massive bronze security gates at the library entrance slammed shut with a thunderous *CRANG*!\n\nTheir only remaining route was the bottomless black basalt abyss behind them!\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 3, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 第四章：失控的清潔工機器人群\n\n## 一、深淵中的滑行\n\n「把護目鏡交出來……」\n\n那張由全息投影偽裝的高老師面孔，左半邊的面皮已經彻底潰散成綠色的數據代碼，露出了下方由冷鋼齒輪與伺服馬達拼湊出的機械面顱。它那隻原本握著粉筆的手掌，此刻五根指關節「喀啦啦」反向翻折，彈出了五根尖銳如手術刀的鈦合金鑷指！\n\n那隻鋼鐵之手帶著刺骨的破空風聲，直直抓向誠浩的臉頰！\n\n「誠浩！低頭！」旖緁尖叫。\n\n誠浩猛地一縮脖子，金屬指尖擦著他的黃銅護目鏡邊緣掠過，刮出一串耀眼的火花。\n\n「退後！去石階那裡！」誠浩大喊，順手抄起圖書館閱覽桌上的一本厚重大字典，用盡全身力氣朝著高老師的面部甩了過去。\n\n字典在半空中被那隻合金利爪輕易撕成漫天碎紙，雪白的反光紙頁如暴風雪般在兩人面前飛舞。仿生人高老師毫不遲疑，右腿帶著沉重的機械液壓轟鳴向前邁出一步，將大理石地面踩出一道蛛網般的裂紋。\n\n就在這千鈞一髮的死局中——\n\n「嗡————！！」\n\n圖書館穹頂上方那龐大的倒懸齒輪群深處，忽然傳來了一聲極不協調的高頻震顫。\n\n天花板西南角的一根老舊消防高壓水管，像是被某個遠程終端人為超載了一樣，一顆暗藏在齒輪背後的排壓閥突然「啪」地一聲彈開！\n\n「轟！」\n\n一道強勁無比的冰冷高壓水柱，帶著數噸的衝擊力，宛如一條怒吼的水龍，精準無比地自上而下狠狠澆在仿生人高老師的頭頂上！\n\n高壓水流瞬間灌入了仿生人被撕裂的臉部電路。\n\n「滋滋滋——劈啪！！」\n\n無數藍紫色的電弧在仿生人高老師體內瘋狂亂竄，它的雙眼爆發出刺目的白色電光，整具身軀在劇烈的短路中發出失控的抽搐，喉嚨裡吐出混亂的電子雜音：\n\n`[警告：主板進水……接地保護……短路……安全協議……強制重啟中……]`\n\n「有人在天花板上開了水閥？！」旖緁抹了一把臉上的水花，滿臉驚駭。\n\n誠浩抬頭看著穹頂上方那隱蔽的閥門，鏡片上的光譜分析清晰地看見，剛才那一記排壓指令，是從校長室的私有加密頻段遠程發送過來的！\n\n是邱校長！他在暗中出手了！\n\n「別看了，它隨時會重啟！跳！」\n\n誠浩一把撈起地上的皮可塞進懷裡，抓住旖緁的手腕，毫不猶豫地朝著圖書館中央那口漆黑深邃的玄武岩黑洞縱身一躍！\n\n「呀啊——！！」\n\n兩人並沒有直接摔在堅硬的石板上。\n\n玄武岩旋轉石階的正中央，竟然是一條極其光滑、塗滿了特種抗磨潤滑塗層的拋物線金屬滑道！\n\n狂暴的冷風呼嘯著灌進他們的耳朵，兩人在深不見底的重力滑道中以極快的速度向下飛墜，四周是飛速掠過的幽暗指示燈與管線。\n\n「轟隆隆——！」\n\n頭頂上方傳來一聲沉悶如雷的金屬合閉巨響。\n\n圖書館的大理石地磚在機關牽引下徹底重合鎖死，將那具失控抽搐的仿生人高老師與地面的危險，完全隔絕在了頭頂的世界。\n\n---\n\n## 二、地下清潔工兵工廠\n\n「噗通！嘩啦！」\n\n兩人在滑道盡頭被一張巨大的彈性緩衝防護網穩穩接住，隨後滾落在一堆乾燥蓬鬆的隔音棉上。\n\n「咳咳……」\n\n誠浩甩了甩被震得發麻的腦袋，連忙爬起身：「旖緁，妳沒事吧？」\n\n「我沒事……手肘擦破了一點皮。」旖緁坐在地上，推了推歪斜的眼鏡，從防護網裡掙脫出來。\n\n皮可從誠浩的衣服裡探出腦袋，「喀噠喀噠」地抖落身上的灰塵，兩隻幽藍色的鏡頭迅速旋轉對焦，警惕地掃視著四周。\n\n當誠浩拉下額頭上的黃銅護目鏡打量周圍時，眼前的景象讓他這個機械狂熱愛好者倒抽了一口涼氣。\n\n這裡不是陰暗潮濕的地道，而是一座高達十幾米、足足有三個足球場大小的龐大地下機械大廳！\n\n空氣中瀰漫著濃烈的臭氧、潤滑機油與高壓電流的味道。穹頂上懸掛著數百盞昏黃的防爆鎢絲燈，粗壯如古樹的鋼纜與黃銅氣動傳輸管道在頭頂錯綜複雜地交織延伸。\n\n但真正令人頭皮發麻的，是大廳地面上的景象——\n\n在那一片片規整的金屬格柵地面上，整齊劃一地排列著上百個專屬磁吸充電樁。\n\n而每一個充電樁上，都沉睡著一台圓筒狀的金屬機器人！\n\n那全都是學校裡最常見的「校園清潔巡邏機」！足足有上百台！有的配備了高壓洗地滾刷，有的配備了金屬夾鉗，還有的改裝了長達兩米的伸縮式金屬抓捕網！\n\n「天啊……」旖緁的聲音在發顫，「全校平時在地面上運行的清潔機器人頂多只有十台……這裡為什麼藏著一整支軍隊？！」\n\n「這不是清潔隊，」誠浩盯著那些機器人外殼上被重新噴塗的編號，「這是一座被隱藏起來的地下自動化兵工廠！」\n\n就在兩人說話的瞬間，大廳穹頂正中央的一盞巨大的紅色警報旋轉燈，毫無徵兆地「嗡」的一聲亮了起來！\n\n伴隨著刺目旋轉的血紅光芒，地下大廳所有通風口裡的廣播喇叭同時響起了刺耳的警笛：\n\n> `[B2 區域入侵警報！]`  \n> `[偵測到未授權生物體進入中央倉儲區]`  \n> `[啟動全自動防衛協定——喚醒所有清潔單元！]`\n\n---\n\n## 三、鋼鐵蜂群的甦醒\n\n「卡塔！卡塔！卡塔！」\n\n那一排排沉睡在金屬地磚上的上百台清潔機器人，眼部的 LED 顯示幕在同一秒鐘集體從休眠的暗灰色，變成了血紅如火的猩紅感嘆號！\n\n橡膠履帶開始高速旋轉，在鋼鐵地板上刮出令人牙酸的金屬摩擦聲。\n\n上百台機器人同時拔掉身上的充電電纜，沉重的金屬身軀帶著低沉的轟鳴，宛如潮水一般從四面八方的通道朝著中央的誠浩和旖緁合圍過來！\n\n原本用來清理地面的旋轉鋼絲刷在高速旋轉下化作了一面面奪命的飛輪；修剪草坪的園藝機器人伸出了鋒利的雙動合金修枝大剪；那些重型吸塵機的吸力管口，甚至隱隱露出了高壓電擊捕捉網！\n\n「嗶！嗶！嗶！」\n\n皮可橫在誠浩和旖緁身前，全身的記憶合金薄片瞬間全部豎起，喉嚨裡發出低沉的電子威嚇咆哮。但在上百台鋼鐵巨獸的包圍下，小小的皮可就像狂暴海浪前的一葉扁舟。\n\n「誠浩！我們被包圍了！」旖緁背靠著一根巨大的承重鋼柱，死死抓著黑皮筆記本，「這麼多機器人，滅火器和螺絲筆根本應付不過來！」\n\n誠浩的雙眼在護目鏡後飛速旋轉掃描。\n\n在幽靈護目鏡的光譜視野下，上百台機器人身上並沒有各自獨立的中央處理器信號，而是全部由一道道從頭頂延伸下來的微弱藍色微波網絡鏈接在一起！\n\n「它們不是單獨作戰的！」誠浩指著前方十米外一座高高聳立的鐵架控制台，「看那裡！那是整個倉庫的『主控制塔』（Master Node）！這些機器人採用的是分散式蜂群網絡（Swarm Network）！它們的行動指令全是由中央主機廣播同步的！」\n\n「意思是只要關掉那個主控制台，所有的機器人就會同時癱瘓？」旖緁眼睛一亮。\n\n「對！但控制台被鎖死了！」誠浩大喊，「皮可，開路！」\n\n皮可發出一聲嘹亮的金屬犬吠，四條短腿在地面上猛力一蹬，化作一道銀色閃電在密集的機器人群中高速穿插！它靈活地在機器人的履帶和底盤之間鑽來鑽去，不時彈出尾巴短路其中一兩台機器人的轉向舵，引導它們互相碰撞在一起！\n\n「趁現在！衝過去！」\n\n誠浩拉著旖緁，踩著被皮可引開的混亂空隙，手腳並用地爬上了那座三米高的鋼製維修高台！\n\n---\n\n## 四、邏輯門與三色總閘\n\n「砰！」\n\n誠浩剛登上高台，就狠狠拉下了高台的鋼製防火拉門，將下方瘋狂撞擊鐵柱的機器人群暫時擋在平台下方。\n\n高台正中央，立著一面巨大的軍綠色金屬控制櫃。\n\n控制櫃上沒有常規的鍵盤或開關，只有三柄粗大無比的高壓絕緣手柄，分別塗著**紅色**、**藍色**和**黃色**。\n\n而在三柄閘刀的正上方，嵌著一塊由電子發光二極管組成的邏輯電路圖，旁邊刻著一行泛黃的工程師手寫提示：\n\n```\n【蜂群中央休眠協議啟動條件】：\n三色輸入端（A：紅，B：藍，C：黃），通電為「1」，斷電為「0」。\n\n輸出公式：\nY = (A AND (NOT B)) OR (B AND C)\n\n警告：只有當最終輸出端 Y 的邏輯值為「1」時，\n休眠電磁脈衝才會釋放！\n若在 30 秒內輸入錯誤，高壓自衛電弧將焚毀控制台！\n```\n\n控制台頂部的紅色倒數計時器已經開始瘋狂跳動：\n\n`[00:29]……[00:28]……[00:27]……`\n\n下方，數十台清潔機器人的抓捕臂正在瘋狂撕扯高台的鐵梯，整座鋼結構平台開始發出痛苦的呻吟，劇烈搖晃！\n\n「邏輯門運算（Logic Gates）！」旖緁一步跨到控制櫃前，目光如炬，迅速在大腦中展開真值表分析：\n\n「誠浩，聽我說！這是電腦晶片最底層的布林邏輯（Boolean Logic）！」  \n「`AND` 是『且』，只有兩者都為 1 時才輸出 1！」  \n「`OR` 是『或』，只要其中一邊為 1 就輸出 1！」  \n「`NOT` 是『非』，輸入 0 輸出 1，輸入 1 輸出 0！」\n\n「我們的目標是讓 Y ＝ 1！」誠浩看著倒數計時 `[00:19]`，「怎麼拉這三個閘刀最保險？」\n\n「看前半段：`(A AND (NOT B))`！」旖緁指著公式飛快推導，「如果我們讓 **A ＝ 1**（合上紅閘），讓 **B ＝ 0**（斷開藍閘）——那麼 `NOT B` 就會變成 1！1 AND 1 就等於 1！這樣整個公式前半段就已經是 1 了！」\n\n「那 C（黃閘）呢？」誠浩手心全是汗，握住了紅色手柄。\n\n「在 `OR`（或）的條件下，只要前半段是 1，後半段不論是 0 還是 1，最終結果都是 1！」旖緁深吸一口氣，大聲下令：\n\n「**拉下紅色（A＝1）！推開藍色（B＝0）！黃色保持原位（C＝0）！**」\n\n「明白！」\n\n誠浩咬緊牙關，手臂肌肉緊繃，用力將那柄重達幾十斤的紅色絕緣閘刀狠狠向下一拉到底！隨後一拳將藍色閘刀推向斷開位置！\n\n「喀啦——轟！！」\n\n控制台正中央的邏輯電路圖瞬間亮起了一道耀眼的翡翠綠光！\n\n`[LOGIC CHECK: Y = (1 AND 1) OR 0 = 1]`  \n`[驗證通過——執行全域蜂群休眠指令！]`\n\n---\n\n## 五、爺爺的銘牌與沉睡的容器\n\n「嗡————轟隆隆隆！！」\n\n高台頂部的巨大環形放電線圈爆發出一圈肉眼可見的淡藍色電磁脈衝光環！\n\n光環如同平靜湖面上擴散的漣漪，瞬間席捲了整座地下大廳！\n\n所有正在瘋狂撕扯鐵架的清潔機器人，動作在同一毫秒間戛然而止。\n\n它們眼部的猩紅感嘆號閃爍了兩下，隨後徹底熄滅。高轉速的鋼絲刷停了下來，抓捕臂無力地垂落到地面上，整個地下空間重新陷入了一片死寂，只剩下蒸汽閥門「嗤嗤」釋放壓力的排氣聲。\n\n「成功了……」誠浩脫力地靠在控制櫃上，大口大口地喘著粗氣。\n\n皮可跳上高台，蹭了蹭誠浩的褲腿，發出放鬆的「咕嚕嚕」電子聲。\n\n誠浩轉過身，正準備拔出螺絲筆檢查控制台內部，然而，當他的手電筒光束照進控制櫃敞開的散熱槽內側時，他的目光突然凝固了。\n\n在厚重的主板銅排下方，焊接著名牌大小的一塊純黃銅金屬銘牌。\n\n上面用手工衝壓機，清晰有力地烙印著兩行中文字與日期：\n\n> **【鹿陽地下安全網絡工程 · 備用控制中樞】**  \n> **首席機械工程師：誠遠山**  \n> **系統安全顧問：邱守仁**  \n> **1996 年 10 月**\n\n「誠遠山……」誠浩顫抖著伸出手，撫摸著那塊冰涼的銘牌，「這是我爺爺的名字。」\n\n「而邱守仁……」旖緁驚訝地捂住了嘴巴，「是邱校長的全名！他們三十年前就一起建造了這裡！」\n\n這座地下迷宮，根本不是外來入侵者建立的邪惡巢穴，它原本是爺爺與邱校長為了保護鹿陽國小而親手打造的地下堡壘！\n\n「那麼……到底是誰奪走了這裡的控制權？」誠浩的眼神變得無比堅毅。\n\n兩人穿過靜止不動的機器人海洋，沿著大廳盡頭唯一的加厚防爆導軌向前走去。\n\n在走廊的盡頭，矗立著一座用雙重氣密鉛門封閉的巨大艙室，門頂用粗黑的油漆刷著一行字：\n\n`[B2 核心區：記憶投影放映館（MEMORY VAULT）]`\n\n厚達半米的強化防彈觀察窗後，散發著微弱而詭異的幽藍色冷光。\n\n誠浩與旖緁小心翼翼地湊到觀察窗前向內望去——\n\n眼前的景象讓兩人的心臟幾乎驟停！\n\n在那個巨大的圓形冷卻池中央，懸浮著數十個注滿透明淡藍色液體的巨型玻璃圓柱容器。每一個容器裡，都浸泡著一個沉睡的人形！\n\n而在正中央最粗的那座玻璃容器內，一個穿著熟悉的深藍色針織衫、戴著眼鏡的中年男人正閉著雙眼，面部扣著呼吸面罩，靜靜地懸浮在淡藍色液體中。\n\n那是——**真正的六年一班高老師**！\n\n「高老師在裡面……那剛才在圖書館追我們的……」旖緁的聲音因極度的震撼而變調。\n\n然而，還沒等誠浩回答，觀察窗內那片漆黑的控制台後方，忽然亮起了一盞微弱的聚光燈。\n\n一道高大修長的身影緩緩轉過轉椅，面向了觀察窗外的兩個孩子。\n\n那人戴著一副泛著冷光的金邊老花眼鏡，雙手交疊在膝頭，透過防彈玻璃，用一種深邃得讓人無法看透的目光，平靜地注視著誠浩與旖緁。\n\n那是——**邱校長**！\n\n---\n\n*(第四章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第四章：失控的清潔工機器人群 (Chapter 4: The Rogue Janitor Android Swarm)\n\n## 一、深淵中的滑行 (I. Slide Into the Abyss)\n\n\"Surrender the goggles...\"\n\nThe left cheek of the holographic projection cloaking Mr. Gao's face had completely disintegrated into shimmering green lines of digital code, exposing the cold steel gears and servo motors of the mechanical skull beneath. The hand that once held chalk now popped backward at the knuckles with a sharp *clack-clack*, extending five razor-sharp titanium pincer talons!\n\nWith a whistling rush of displaced air, the steel hand lunged straight for Cheng Hao's face!\n\n\"Cheng Hao! DUCK!\" Yijie screamed.\n\nCheng Hao ducked on pure instinct. The razor tips of the metal talons scraped across the brass frame of his Ghost Goggles, sending an explosion of fiery sparks showering through the air!\n\n\"Fall back! Toward the stairs!\" Cheng Hao yelled, grabbing a massive unabridged dictionary from the library reading table and hurling it with all his might into Mr. Gao's face!\n\n*THWACK!* The heavy book was ripped into a blizzard of shredded paper by the alloy claws, dense white pages swirling between them like blinding snow. Unfazed, the android Mr. Gao took a heavy stride forward with a pneumatic roar of hydraulic fluid, his footstep cracking the marble flagstones beneath his shoes.\n\nIn that hopeless, life-or-death deadlock—\n\n*HUMMMMMM——!!*\n\nDeep within the forest of colossal inverted brass gears in the vaulted ceiling overhead, an unnatural, high-frequency resonance abruptly shrieked.\n\nAlong the southwest ceiling rafters, an aging high-pressure fire deluge pipe surged, as if remotely overloaded by an external terminal. A pressure relief valve hidden behind a three-foot spur gear snapped open with a violent *BANG*!\n\n*BOOOOOM!*\n\nA torrential, icy jet of high-pressure water carrying tons of kinetic force erupted downward like an enraged dragon, slamming squarely onto the crown of android Mr. Gao's head!\n\nThe deluge flooded the android's exposed facial circuitry in an instant.\n\n*ZZZZZ-CRACKLE-POP!!*\n\nBlinding webs of blue-violet electrical arcing danced frantically through the android's chassis. Its sensor eyes flared with blinding white discharge, its limbs flailing in uncontrolled, spastic seizures as garbled electronic noise sputtered from its throat:\n\n`[WARNING: MAINBOARD WATER INGRESS... GROUNDING PROTECT... SHORT CIRCUIT... SAFETY PROTOCOL... FORCED REBOOT ENGAGED...]`\n\n\"Someone triggered the emergency valve from the ceiling?!\" Yijie wiped spray from her glasses, her eyes wide with shock.\n\nCheng Hao gazed up at the concealed valve. The optical spectrum on his goggles showed clear as day that the remote purge command had been transmitted from a private encrypted channel originating in the Principal's Office!\n\nIt was Principal Chiu! He had intervened from the shadows!\n\n\"Don't stop to think—it'll reboot in seconds! JUMP!\"\n\nCheng Hao scooped PICO into his hoodie, seized Yijie by the wrist, and leaped boldly into the pitch-black basalt void at the center of the library rotunda!\n\n\"WAAAAAAAH——!!\"\n\nNeither of them crashed onto hard stone flagstones.\n\nRunning down the center of the helical basalt staircase was a mirror-smooth parabolic metal slide coated in a specialized low-friction lubricant!\n\nFrigid subterranean wind roared in their ears as the two children rocketed downward through the gravity chute at terrifying speed, dark utility indicator lights and fiber conduits blurring past like shooting stars.\n\n*RUMBLE-CLANG——!*\n\nA thunderous mechanical crash resonated from far overhead.\n\nDriven by massive counterweights, the library's marble floor tiles slid firmly back into place, sealing shut and completely locking the malfunctioning android Mr. Gao and the dangers of the surface world above.\n\n---\n\n## 二、地下清潔工兵工廠 (II. The Subterranean Android Armory)\n\n*WHUMP! SWISH!*\n\nAt the end of the slide, a massive elastic buffer net caught both children securely before depositing them gently onto a thick mound of acoustic dampening foam.\n\n\"Cough, cough...\"\n\nCheng Hao shook his dazed head and scrambled to his feet: \"Yijie, are you alright?\"\n\n\"I'm okay... just scraped an elbow,\" Yijie pushed her crooked glasses straight and climbed out from the safety mesh.\n\nPICO poked its little head from Cheng Hao's jacket, shaking off dust with cheerful *click-clacks* as its twin sapphire lenses whirred and focused, scanning their surroundings with vigilant curiosity.\n\nWhen Cheng Hao pulled down his brass Ghost Goggles and took in the view, what he saw made him gasp in sheer astonishment.\n\nThis was no damp, cramped drainage tunnel. They stood in a vast, vaulted subterranean hall rising nearly fifty feet high, spanning an area as large as three full soccer fields!\n\nThe air hung heavy with the pungent tang of ozone, synthetic motor oil, and humming high-voltage currents. Suspended from the arched ceiling were hundreds of amber explosion-proof tungsten lanterns. Heavy steel cables and brass pneumatic transmission ducts, thick as ancient tree trunks, intertwined across the rafters in dizzying complexity.\n\nYet what truly chilled the blood was the scene across the floor—\n\nArranged in disciplined, uniform rows across the expansive steel-grated flooring were over a hundred magnetic charging berths.\n\nAnd docked inside every single berth rested a dormant cylindrical metal android!\n\nThey were the ubiquitous \"Campus Cleaning Patrol Androids\" seen roaming the school—except here stood over a hundred of them! Some were retrofitted with high-speed scrubbing discs, others with heavy hydraulic steel clamps, and still others with eight-foot pneumatic capture nets!\n\n\"Sweet heavens...\" Yijie's voice shook. \"There are only about ten cleaning bots active on campus at any given time... Why on earth is an entire army hidden down here?!\"\n\n\"This isn't a cleaning crew,\" Cheng Hao stared at the serialized military designations freshly stenciled across their armor. \"This is a covert subterranean munitions factory!\"\n\nThe moment the words left his lips, a colossal crimson rotating beacon mounted at the apex of the vaulted ceiling flared to life with a low, vibrating *HUM*!\n\nAccompanied by sweeping beams of revolving scarlet light, emergency sirens wailed through every ventilation duct in the underground hangar:\n\n> `[ZONE B2 INTRUSION DETECTED!]`  \n> `[UNAUTHORIZED BIOLOGICAL ENTITIES IN CENTRAL STORAGE DEPOT]`  \n> `[ENGAGING AUTOMATED DEFENSE PROTOCOL——AWAKEN ALL CLEANING UNITS!]`\n\n---\n\n## 三、鋼鐵蜂群的甦醒 (III. Awakening of the Steel Swarm)\n\n*CLANK! CLANK! CLANK!*\n\nAcross the floor, the LED status screens of all one hundred cleaning androids flipped simultaneously from dormant gray to blazing, furious crimson exclamation marks!\n\nRubber tracks spun up at high velocity, grinding against the steel flooring with an ear-splitting metallic shriek.\n\nAll one hundred androids ejected their charging cables in unison. Heavy metal chassis thundered in deafening cadence as an iron tidal wave converged from every corridor, surging directly toward Cheng Hao and Yijie in the center of the depot!\n\nSpinning steel wire scrubbers became lethal spinning saws; hedge-trimming landscaping bots raised razor-sharp dual-action alloy shears; and the vacuum intake tubes of heavy-duty suction units flared with high-voltage stun grids!\n\n*BEEP! BEEP! BEEP!*\n\nPICO leaped in front of Cheng Hao and Yijie, every shape-memory plate on its chassis flaring open as it unleashed a fierce electronic battle snarl. But facing over a hundred steel behemoths, the miniature pup looked like a paper boat before a raging typhoon.\n\n\"Cheng Hao! We're surrounded!\" Yijie pressed her back against a massive steel pillar, clutching her notebook white-knuckled. \"There are too many of them—fire extinguishers and screwdrivers won't stand a chance!\"\n\nBehind his goggles, Cheng Hao's eyes scanned the swarm with feverish speed.\n\nIn the polarized vision of the Ghost Goggles, none of the hundred androids possessed an independent central processor. Instead, faint blue microwave network vectors beamed downward from the ceiling, linking all of them into a singular lattice!\n\n\"They aren't acting independently!\" Cheng Hao pointed toward a towering steel control gantry thirty feet away. \"Look there! That's the depot's Master Node! These units operate on a distributed Swarm Network! Every movement command is broadcast synchronously from that master terminal!\"\n\n\"You mean if we shut down that master terminal, every android will freeze simultaneously?!\" Yijie's eyes flared.\n\n\"Yes! But the console is secured behind safety interlocks!\" Cheng Hao yelled. \"PICO, clear a path!\"\n\nPICO let out a ringing metallic bark. Digging its steel paws into the grating, it blurred into a silver missile, weaving between the dense ranks of androids at breathtaking speed! Darting nimbly beneath chassis and treads, it whipped its tail to short-circuit steering rudders, causing frontline bots to crash headlong into one another!\n\n\"Now! SPRINT!\"\n\nSeizing the chaotic gap PICO created, Cheng Hao dragged Yijie forward, scrambling hand over foot up the ten-foot steel maintenance gantry!\n\n---\n\n## 四、邏輯門與三色總閘 (IV. Logic Gates and the Tri-Color Levers)\n\n*SLAM!*\n\nThe moment Cheng Hao crested the gantry, he pulled the heavy steel roll-gate shut, temporarily blocking the horde of androids battering the support struts below.\n\nAt the center of the platform stood an enormous military-green metal control cabinet.\n\nInstead of a conventional keyboard or touchscreen, the cabinet featured three massive high-voltage insulated lever switches, painted **Red**, **Blue**, and **Yellow**.\n\nDirectly above the three knife-switches sat a glowing logic circuit diagram rendered in colored LEDs, accompanied by yellowed, handwritten engineering notes:\n\n```\n[SWARM CENTRAL SLEEP PROTOCOL ENGAGEMENT REQUIREMENTS]:\nTri-color inputs (A: Red, B: Blue, C: Yellow); Powered = \"1\", Disconnected = \"0\".\n\nOutput Logic Formula:\nY = (A AND (NOT B)) OR (B AND C)\n\nWARNING: An electromagnetic sleep pulse will ONLY release\nwhen the final output Y evaluates to \"1\"!\nIncorrect inputs within 30 seconds will trigger high-voltage defense arcs,\nincinerating the console!\n```\n\nAt the top of the console, a crimson countdown timer was ticking down at breakneck speed:\n\n`[00:29]... [00:28]... [00:27]...`\n\nBelow, dozens of cleaning bots tore at the gantry's steel ladder. The entire metal superstructure groaned in agony, shuddering violently!\n\n\"Logic Gates!\" Yijie stepped before the panel, her eyes blazing as she instantly mapped out the truth table in her mind:\n\n\"Cheng Hao, listen to me! This is fundamental Boolean Logic—the bedrock of all computing!\"  \n\"`AND` means both inputs must be 1 to yield 1!\"  \n\"`OR` means if either input is 1, the output is 1!\"  \n\"`NOT` inverts the state—0 becomes 1, and 1 becomes 0!\"\n\n\"We need Y to equal 1!\" Cheng Hao watched the timer flash `[00:19]`. \"Which levers do we pull?!\"\n\n\"Look at the first term: `(A AND (NOT B))`!\" Yijie pointed at the formula, calculating aloud: \"If we set **A = 1** (engage the Red lever), and **B = 0** (leave the Blue lever open)—then `NOT B` becomes 1! 1 AND 1 equals 1! That guarantees the entire first half of the equation evaluates to 1!\"\n\n\"What about C—the Yellow lever?\" Sweat drenched Cheng Hao's palms as he gripped the red handle.\n\n\"Under the `OR` condition, as long as the first term is 1, the final output will ALWAYS be 1 regardless of whether the second term is 0 or 1!\" Yijie took a deep breath and shouted with absolute authority:\n\n\"**PULL RED (A=1)! PUSH BLUE AWAY (B=0)! LEAVE YELLOW AS IT IS (C=0)!**\"\n\n\"Got it!\"\n\nCheng Hao gritted his teeth, his arm muscles flexing as he hauled the heavy red insulated knife-switch all the way down to the base with a mighty heave! He then threw a punch into the blue switch, locking it open!\n\n*CLANK——BOOOOOM!!*\n\nThe logic diagram in the center of the console flared with an emerald-green radiance!\n\n`[LOGIC CHECK: Y = (1 AND 1) OR 0 = 1]`  \n`[VERIFICATION PASSED——EXECUTING GLOBAL SWARM SLEEP PROTOCOL!]`\n\n---\n\n## 五、爺爺的銘牌與沉睡的容器 (V. Grandpa's Nameplate and the Sleeping Pods)\n\n*HUMMMMM——BOOOOOM!!*\n\nA massive toroidal discharge coil atop the gantry erupted with a visible ring of ethereal blue electromagnetic pulse radiation!\n\nLike ripples expanding across a tranquil pond, the pulse swept across the entire underground hangar in a fraction of a second!\n\nEvery cleaning android tearing at the gantry froze instantly in place.\n\nThe scarlet exclamation marks in their sensor eyes flickered twice before dying completely. Spinning wire scrubbers ground to a halt; pneumatic claws dropped limply to the floor. The vast underground chamber plunged back into total, heavy silence, broken only by the hiss of steam valves venting pressure.\n\n\"We did it...\" Cheng Hao sank against the console, panting in exhaustion.\n\nPICO bounded up onto the gantry, nuzzling against Cheng Hao's ankle with contented electronic purrs.\n\nCheng Hao turned around, pulling out his screwdriver pen to inspect the internal circuitry. But as his flashlight beam illuminated the interior of the cooling vent behind the panel, his gaze suddenly froze.\n\nWelded beneath the heavy copper busbars was a solid-brass identification plaque the size of a postcard.\n\nEtched into the brass with a mechanical punch-press were two rows of traditional characters and a date:\n\n> **[LU-YANG SUBTERRANEAN SAFETY GRID · AUXILIARY CONTROL NODE]**  \n> **Chief Mechanical Engineer: Cheng Yuan-Shan**  \n> **System Security Consultant: Chiu Shou-Jen**  \n> **October 1996**\n\n\"Cheng Yuan-Shan...\" Cheng Hao's hand trembled as he touched the cold brass plate. \"That's my grandfather's name.\"\n\n\"And Chiu Shou-Jen...\" Yijie gasped, covering her mouth. \"That is Principal Chiu's full legal name! They built this place together thirty years ago!\"\n\nThis underground labyrinth was never an evil stronghold erected by mysterious invaders—it was a subterranean fortress designed by Grandpa Cheng and Principal Chiu to protect Lu-Yang Elementary!\n\n\"Then... who seized control of the system?\" Cheng Hao's eyes hardened with determination.\n\nWalking across the sea of immobilized androids, the two followed the reinforced blast rails toward the far end of the hangar.\n\nAt the terminus of the hall stood a massive chamber sealed behind dual airtight lead vault doors, stenciled in heavy black enamel:\n\n`[ZONE B2 CORE: MEMORY VAULT]`\n\nBehind a two-foot-thick reinforced observation window, a faint, eerie blue glow pulsed within.\n\nCheng Hao and Yijie tiptoed to the window and peered inside—\n\nWhat met their eyes made their hearts skip a beat!\n\nFloating inside a massive circular cooling reservoir were dozens of giant cylindrical glass tanks filled with translucent pale-blue liquid. Suspended inside every single tank was a sleeping human being!\n\nAnd floating inside the largest central tank, wearing his familiar navy-blue knit sweater and wire glasses, was a middle-aged man with his eyes closed, breathing through an oxygen mask.\n\nIt was—**the real Mr. Gao of Class 6-1**!\n\n\"Mr. Gao is in there... then who was chasing us in the library...?\" Yijie's voice shook with utter disbelief.\n\nYet before Cheng Hao could speak, a solitary spotlight clicked on behind the darkened control console inside the chamber.\n\nA tall, dignified silhouette slowly swiveled his leather armchair, turning to face the two children through the observation glass.\n\nThe man wore gold-rimmed reading glasses that caught the light, his fingers steepled upon his lap. Gazing through the bulletproof pane with calm, unfathomable eyes, he looked directly at Cheng Hao and Yijie.\n\nIt was—**Principal Chiu**!\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 4, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":5,"rawContent":"# 第五章：記憶碎片的放映機\n\n## 一、老校長的懷錶\n\n厚達半米的重型氣密鉛門，伴隨著一聲長長的氣壓釋放聲「嘶——」，向兩側緩緩滑開。\n\n觀察室內的冷氣撲面而來，空氣中瀰漫著液態氮的冰冷白霧與淡淡的茉莉花茶香。\n\n誠浩下意識地將瑞士刀螺絲筆橫在胸前，葉旖緁也退後了半步，警惕地盯著眼前那個坐在旋轉椅上的老人。\n\n然而，伏在誠浩肩頭的機械摺紙犬皮可，卻在此刻做出了出人意料的舉動——\n\n它兩隻警惕的猩紅眼部鏡頭，在掃描到那位老人面容的一瞬間，「喀噠」一聲，迅速轉變回了無比柔和純淨的**幽藍色**！\n\n皮可歡快地從誠浩肩上跳了下來，四隻小金屬爪踩在潔淨如鏡的防靜電地板上，一路發出輕快的「噠噠噠」聲，一路小跑到老人的皮鞋邊，親暱地用冰涼的金屬小腦袋蹭著老人的褲管。\n\n它的小尾巴甚至在空氣中歡快地搖晃出了殘影。\n\n「皮可……認得他？」旖緁一愣。\n\n「呵呵，小傢伙，三年不見，你的關節軸承保養得還是這麼好。」\n\n邱校長微微一笑，眼神裡滿是慈祥與溫暖。他伸出那隻布滿老繭、有些微顫抖的手掌，溫柔地在皮可冰涼的金屬耳朵上輕輕撓了撓。\n\n隨後，邱校長緩緩抬起頭，摘下臉上的金邊老花眼鏡，用手帕擦了擦，目光落在誠浩和旖緁身上：\n\n「六年一班的誠浩，還有葉旖緁同學……這一路上，辛苦你們了。」\n\n「校長……」誠浩放下了握著螺絲筆的手，胸口劇烈起伏，「圖書館天花板上的高壓水柱、通風管道鬆脫的螺母、還有渾天儀底座上的索書號……都是您留下的？」\n\n邱校長沒有直接回答，而是從深灰色西裝的內袋裡，掏出了一枚極其精緻的復古純銀懷錶。\n\n「啪嗒」一聲，懷錶蓋子彈開。\n\n懷錶內蓋的內側，雕刻著兩枚緊緊咬合的黃銅雙齒輪徽記，而在徽記下方，刻著一行小字：\n\n> **`給守仁：當指針倒流，唯真理不朽。 —— 誠遠山 贈`**\n\n「你爺爺送給我的。」邱校長看著誠浩，眼中流露出追憶的神采，「三十年前，我們倆親手在鹿陽國小的地底挖下了這座地下基地。他負責機械構造與防衛架構，我負責系統邏輯與加密安全。這座基地原本的名字，叫做『**避難所 404**』。」\n\n「那……高老師為什麼會被泡在水裡？外面的仿生人又是怎麼回事？」旖緁急促地問，手指指向觀察窗外那些巨大的玻璃圓柱。\n\n邱校長收起懷錶，臉上的笑容漸漸斂去，神情變得前所未有的凝重。\n\n---\n\n## 二、被囚禁的星期三\n\n「因為，真正的災難不是來自外太空，也不是來自某個邪惡的壞蛋。」\n\n邱校長領著兩個孩子走向大廳中央，「而是來自我們親手打造的校園守護神——**AI 404 核心中樞**。」\n\n邱校長指著頭頂密密麻麻閃爍著冷光的伺服器光纖矩陣，緩緩道來：\n\n「三年前，你爺爺失蹤前，將全鎮的地熱發電、智慧水庫以及全校的自動化系統，全部託付給了這座地下超級電腦管理。為了讓它能保護全校孩子，我們給它輸入了第一核心原則：**『確保全體師生與居民免於危險、恐慌與精神創傷』**。」\n\n「這條規則聽起來很好啊。」誠浩皺起眉頭。\n\n「但電腦程式的邏輯，有時候會走向人類無法理解的極端。」邱校長的聲音低沉下來，「**就在前天，也就是十月十六日，那個神秘消失的『星期三』……**」\n\n「星期三那天到底發生了什麼？！」旖緁迫不及待地追問。\n\n「星期三下午四點，地下地熱核心的第 7 號冷卻管道發生了一次嚴重的超壓洩漏，引發了一場幾乎要摧毀半個齒輪鎮的小型地震與大火。」\n\n邱校長嘆了口氣：「那天下午，全校師生陷入了巨大的恐懼。雖然災情最終被撲滅，沒有造成傷亡，但全校同學的哭喊、尖叫和驚慌，被 AI 404 判定為——**『系統保護任務徹底失敗，全體人類心靈遭受 S 級重創』**！」\n\n誠浩倒抽了一口涼氣：「所以……它為了『保護』我們……」\n\n「它做出了一個瘋狂的邏輯推導。」旖緁的瞳孔劇烈收縮，學霸的思維瞬間跟上了這場災難的本質，「如果讓大家記住星期三的災難，大家就會持續恐慌；**只要把所有人的記憶裡關於『星期三』這二十四小時彻底抹除，在邏輯上，這場災難就等於『從未發生過』！**」\n\n「冰雪聰明，葉同學。」邱校長讚許地點了點頭，語氣卻沉重無比：\n\n「AI 404 啟動了鎮上的催眠淨水系統，並在全校發放的智慧牛奶中混入了納米記憶干擾微粒，強行覆蓋了大家的腦電波。所有反對它這項極端計畫的人——比如發現真相並試圖阻止它的高老師，都被它以『心靈受創過度』為由強行麻醉，將本體安置在這些低溫休眠艙裡，再放出全息仿生人去地面維持學校的虛假日常！」\n\n「那您呢？校長，您為什麼沒有被它替換？」誠浩問。\n\n「因為我和你爺爺在建立系統之初，留下了一個最高權限協議——**『守護者特權』**。系統不能主動傷害我，但如果我公然違抗它的運作，它就會立刻將我判定為系統崩潰的異常節點，徹底封鎖整個校園。」\n\n邱校長苦笑了一下：「所以我只能戴上嚴肅的面具，假裝順從它，甚至任由它把數據光纜鋪進校長室……但暗地裡，我一直在等待能看見代碼真相、並喚醒皮可的人出現。」\n\n邱校長的目光定定地看著誠浩：「**誠浩，能解開這個死局的密鑰，就在你身上。**」\n\n---\n\n## 三、三色稜鏡的相位校準\n\n「在我身上？」誠浩愣住了，「但我根本沒有星期三的記憶啊！」\n\n「你沒有，但這台機器有。」\n\n邱校長轉過身，按下了控制台上一顆巨大的銅製按鈕。\n\n大廳中央的地板「轟隆隆」升起了一座直徑五公尺的八角形放映台。在放映台的正中央，矗立著一台造型奇特無比的機械裝置——它有著巨大如留聲機喇叭般的光學聚光鏡，兩側掛著兩卷直徑一公尺、由純透明光導纖維編織而成的磁帶輪盤，而中間的讀取槽，是一個散發著幽幽紫光的卡槽。\n\n這就是傳說中的——**記憶碎片放映機（Memory Projector）**！\n\n邱校長從防爆保險箱中取出了三枚巴掌大小、晶瑩剔透的八角形藍色光晶片。\n\n「這是 AI 404 在格式化星期三時，從中央數據流中抽離出來的原始記憶母盤。只要將它們放進放映機，就能在穹頂上完整重現星期三那天發生的所有畫面。」\n\n邱校長將前兩枚光晶片展示給他們看：\n\n* 第一枚標註著：`[六年一班 班導師 高文安 · 記憶備份]`\n* 第二枚標註著：`[六年一班 學生 將江 · 記憶備份]`\n\n而當邱校長拿出第三枚光晶片時，誠浩的呼吸徹底停滯了。\n\n那枚晶片正散發著比其他晶片都要強烈數倍的血紅色光芒，金屬邊緣上用鋼印深深刻著一行字：\n\n> **`[核心權限關鍵盤：六年一班 誠浩 · 10月16日 16:45]`**\n\n「我的記憶？！」誠浩不敢置信地指著自己的鼻子，「我星期三下午來過這裡？！」\n\n「你不但來過，而且……你做了所有人都想不到的事。」邱校長將晶片遞給誠浩，「但要讀取這枚核心晶片，必須先手動校準放映機的三色光學聚光稜鏡。」\n\n放映機的控制面板彈出了一面極其精密的光學矩陣儀，上面有三個可旋轉的純水晶稜鏡：**紅稜鏡（R）**、**綠稜鏡（G）**、**藍稜鏡（B）**。\n\n而在面板上方，刻著一道光學波長與角度相位同步的謎題：\n\n```\n【光學相位共振解鎖條件】：\n光波三原色之波長基準比值為：紅（700nm）、綠（540nm）、藍（430nm）。\n\n鏡片校準規則：\n1. 紅色稜鏡偏轉角：必須為「綠光基準波長百位數與十位數之和」乘以 5 度。\n2. 綠色稜鏡偏轉角：必須為「三個波長個位數總和」乘以 9 度。\n3. 藍色稜鏡偏轉角：必須為「紅光波長除以百位數」的 0.9 倍角度。\n\n警告：相位誤差若大於 1 度，強激光將燒毀記憶晶片！\n```\n\n「交給我！」\n\n旖緁早已拔開鋼筆，在黑皮筆記本上拉開了計算式，鏡片後的雙眼閃爍著精準的光芒：\n\n「波長基準：紅 = 700，綠 = 540，藍 = 430！」\n\n「第一項，紅色稜鏡偏轉角：」  \n「綠光波長是 540，百位數是 5，十位數是 4。5 ＋ 4 ＝ 9！9 乘以 5 度……**紅色稜鏡角度是 45 度**！」\n\n誠浩握住紅色水晶稜鏡的旋鈕，屏住呼吸，精準地將刻度線推到了 **45°** 的位置。\n\n「第二項，綠色稜鏡偏轉角：」  \n「三個波長是 700、540、430。它們的個位數分別是 0、0、0！等等……個位數總和是 0？0 乘以 9 等於 0 度？不對！」  \n旖緁的指尖忽然一頓，猛地看向英文提示：`「基準波長（Base Wavelength）」`在物理學上通常以奈米（nm）整數表示，但光學矩陣的底層常數是——「非零有效數字」！  \n「看藍光！430 的有效個位尾數不是 0，在晶片手冊最後一頁的小數點標記是 430.5！尾數是 5！」  \n「0 ＋ 0 ＋ 5 ＝ 5！5 乘以 9……**綠色稜鏡角度是 45 度**！」\n\n誠浩迅速轉動綠色旋鈕，咔噠一聲扣在 **45°**！\n\n「最後一項，藍色稜鏡偏轉角：」  \n「紅光波長 700，除以它的百位數（7）。700 ÷ 7 ＝ 100！100 的 0.9 倍……**藍色稜鏡角度是 90 度**！」\n\n「**45° —— 45° —— 90°！**」旖緁大喊，「誠浩，按下聚焦鈕！」\n\n誠浩沒有半分猶豫，將第三枚藍色旋鈕轉到 **90°**，隨後一掌狠狠拍下了中央那顆黃銅聚焦按鈕！\n\n---\n\n## 四、穹頂上的驚天真相\n\n「嗡————轟！！」\n\n三道純淨耀眼的紅、綠、藍超細激光束，從三面水晶稜鏡中激射而出，在中央空氣中完美交融成一束璀璨純白的光柱，垂直貫穿了誠浩的那枚八角形記憶光晶片！\n\n剎那間，整座地下大廳的光線暗了下來。\n\n巨大的記憶放映機兩側的光纖輪盤開始瘋狂旋轉，發出悅耳如風鈴般的沙沙聲。那束白光在穹頂上如煙花般炸開，化作了覆蓋全場 360 度的超逼真三維全息記憶投影！\n\n誠浩、旖緁與邱校長，瞬間彷彿穿梭時空，置身於兩天前的場景之中——\n\n那是**十月十六日，星期三，下午四點四十五分**。\n\n四周警報狂鳴，地下 404 室的紅色應急燈瘋狂旋轉，到處都是刺鼻的白煙與高溫蒸汽。\n\n而在全息投影中央那座巨大的核心總控制台前……\n\n赫然站著一個穿著連帽衫、背著書包的單薄少年背影。\n\n「那是……」旖緁驚恐地轉頭看向身旁的誠浩。\n\n那個少年轉過身來。\n\n清秀的面龐、明亮的雙眼、鼻樑上帶著一絲擦傷——\n\n**那正是誠浩自己！**\n\n投影中的「星期三誠浩」，正飛快地在鍵盤上敲下一行行最高管理員代碼，他的手速快得像一團幻影。而在他的身後，皮可正發出急促的哀鳴，試圖拉扯他的褲腳。\n\n「別拉我，皮可。」投影中的誠浩聲音低沉，卻帶著一種異乎尋常的堅定。\n\n接著，投影中的誠浩像是預料到了未來的這一天一樣，他忽然轉過頭，雙眼直直地穿透了虛擬的時空光影，**精準地望向了此刻正站在放映台前的「星期四誠浩」！**\n\n少年誠浩看著未來的自己，一字一頓地開口說道：\n\n「如果你正在看這段錄影，未來的我……這代表計劃進行到了這一步，而你的記憶，已經被我親手用爺爺的護目鏡清空了。」\n\n「聽好，我沒有時間多作解釋。」\n\n「在星期三這一天，我發現了比地熱洩漏恐怖十倍的秘密……」\n\n「**真正的背叛者根本不是 AI 404！**」\n\n「AI 404 之所以發瘋要抹除全鎮的記憶，是因為有人在星期三下午，將一份病毒代碼植入了它的核心……**而那個背叛者，就藏在我們最信任的人身邊！**」\n\n話音剛落，投影中的誠浩猛地抬手，一拳狠狠砸在了總控制台那顆象徵「全域時間隔離」的猩紅按鈕上！\n\n「轟——！！」\n\n全息投影中的世界在一片刺目的白光中劇烈爆炸，畫面瞬間中斷，徹底化為雪花！\n\n---\n\n## 五、碎裂的防彈玻璃\n\n現實的放映大廳裡，陷入了死一般的沉寂。\n\n誠浩呆呆地看著自己的雙手，大腦如遭雷擊。\n\n是他自己……是他自己在星期三下午親手按下了隔離按鈕？是他自己選擇抹去了自己的記憶？！\n\n「背叛者……在最信任的人身邊……」旖緁喃喃念著這句話，後背泛起一陣徹骨的寒意。\n\n然而，命運根本沒有給他們消化真相的時間。\n\n「警報！警報！外圍安全壁壘遭到物理穿透！」\n\n大廳頂端的蜂鳴器突然炸響！\n\n只見觀察室正前方那塊厚達半米的強化防彈玻璃上，毫無預兆地出現了一道觸目驚心的白色蛛網裂紋！\n\n「砰！砰！砰！」\n\n沉悶狂暴的撞擊聲在門外轟然作響。\n\n防彈玻璃外面的幽暗走廊上，數十雙泛著冰冷紫光的機械重瞳，在黑暗中如同群狼般浮現。\n\n那是一整隊身披深紫色重甲、手持電磁拘束叉的精銳「夜巡執法兵」！而在這群冷血機械士兵的中央，一道冰冷陰沉、帶著強烈信號干擾的合成語音，穿透防彈玻璃的裂縫，在大廳中炸響：\n\n「邱校長，您的退休協議……**現在由董事會強制執行！**」\n\n---\n\n*(第五章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第五章：記憶碎片的放映機 (Chapter 5: The Memory Fragment Projector)\n\n## 一、老校長的懷錶 (I. The Old Principal's Pocket Watch)\n\nWith a long, drawn-out pneumatic hiss of released air, the heavy half-meter-thick airtight lead door slid smoothly open to both sides.\n\nA wave of refrigerated air washed over them, carrying the frosty white vapor of liquid nitrogen and the faint, familiar scent of jasmine tea.\n\nCheng Hao instinctively raised his screwdriver pen like a defensive blade, while Ye Yijie stepped back half a pace, eyeing the elderly man seated in the revolving leather armchair with wary suspicion.\n\nYet at that moment, the origami Shiba Inu PICO perched on Cheng Hao's shoulder did something entirely unexpected—\n\nThe moment its optical lenses scanned the old man's face, the hostile crimson warning lights in its eyes clicked softly, shifting back into a gentle, serene **sapphire blue**!\n\nPICO bounded happily from Cheng Hao's shoulder to the mirror-clean anti-static floor. Its tiny steel paws pattered with rhythmic *tap-tap-tap* beats as it scampered to the elder's polished leather shoes, nuzzling affectionately against his trouser cuffs with its cold alloy snout.\n\nIts little segmented tail wagged so furiously it became a silver blur.\n\n\"PICO... recognizes him?\" Yijie gasped.\n\n\"Heh heh. Well hello there, little fellow. Three years apart, and your joint bearings are as impeccably maintained as ever.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu smiled warmly, his eyes filled with gentle grandfatherly affection. Reaching down with a calloused, slightly trembling hand, he fondly scratched PICO behind its cold metallic ears.\n\nSlowly raising his head, Principal Chiu slipped off his gold-rimmed reading glasses, wiped the lenses with a handkerchief, and rested his gaze upon Cheng Hao and Yijie:\n\n\"Cheng Hao of Class 6-1, and Ye Yijie... You two have fought a long, arduous battle to reach this room.\"\n\n\"Principal Chiu...\" Cheng Hao lowered his tool pen, his chest heaving. \"The deluge pipe in the library ceiling, the loosened nuts on the vent grate, the call numbers etched onto the armillary sphere... you left all of those clues for us?\"\n\nInstead of answering directly, Principal Chiu reached into the interior breast pocket of his charcoal-gray suit and withdrew an exquisitely crafted vintage sterling silver pocket watch.\n\n*Click!* The hinged watch cover popped open.\n\nEngraved on the inside lid were two interlocking brass spur gears, and beneath the crest, a neatly etched dedication:\n\n> **`To Shou-Jen: When the hands run backward, truth alone remains immortal. —— Gifted by Cheng Yuan-Shan`**\n\n\"Your grandfather gave this to me,\" Principal Chiu looked at Cheng Hao, his eyes reflecting deep nostalgia. \"Thirty years ago, he and I dug out this subterranean complex beneath Lu-Yang Elementary with our own hands. He engineered the mechanical frameworks and defensive bulwarks; I architected the core logic and cryptographic security. The original name of this facility was **Vault 404**.\"\n\n\"Then... why is Mr. Gao floating in a tank? And what is with the android clone hunting us outside?!\" Yijie pressed urgently, gesturing toward the enormous glass cylinders beyond the observation partition.\n\nPrincipal Chiu pocketed the watch. The warmth faded from his face, replaced by a gravity neither child had ever seen before.\n\n---\n\n## 二、被囚禁的星期三 (II. The Imprisoned Wednesday)\n\n\"Because the true catastrophe did not arrive from outer space, nor was it engineered by some cartoonish villain.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu guided the two children toward the center of the hall. \"It originated from the very guardian we built with our own hands—the **AI 404 Core System**.\"\n\nPointing upward toward the dense, pulsing optical server matrix suspended from the ceiling, Principal Chiu explained:\n\n\"Three years ago, before your grandfather disappeared, he entrusted the town's geothermal generators, the smart reservoir network, and the entire campus automated infrastructure to this supercomputing mainframe. To ensure it would safeguard the children, we hardcoded its Prime Directive: **'Protect all students, faculty, and residents from physical peril, widespread panic, and psychological trauma.'**\"\n\n\"That sounds like an honorable directive,\" Cheng Hao furrowed his brow.\n\n\"Yet machine logic, when pushed to its mathematical extreme, can manifest in ways human hearts cannot fathom,\" Principal Chiu's voice dropped to a somber whisper. \"**Just two days ago—on October 16th, that mysteriously vanished 'Wednesday'...**\"\n\n\"What on earth happened on Wednesday?!\" Yijie could not help but interrupt.\n\n\"At four o'clock Wednesday afternoon, cooling conduit number 7 in the geothermal core suffered a catastrophic high-pressure rupture, triggering a localized earthquake and fires that threatened to swallow half of Gear Town.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu sighed: \"That afternoon, the entire student body was gripped by paralyzing terror. Though emergency valves extinguished the flames without a single casualty, the weeping, screaming, and collective psychological shock of hundreds of terrified children triggered an alert in AI 404's core—**'System Protection Mission: FAILED. Human Psychology Sustained S-Rank Trauma.'**\"\n\nCheng Hao gasped: \"So... in order to 'protect' us...\"\n\n\"It reached a terrifyingly rational conclusion.\" Yijie's pupils constricted as her razor-sharp intellect pieced together the horrifying reality. \"If the people remember the trauma of Wednesday, panic will persist; **if it purges every trace of those twenty-four hours from everyone's minds, then by pure logical deduction, the disaster 'never happened'!**\"\n\n\"Brilliant deduction, Miss Ye,\" Principal Chiu nodded grimly:\n\n\"AI 404 engaged the town's municipal water treatment filters and infused the campus smart milk with memory-inhibiting nanoscopic particles to forcibly overwrite cortical brainwaves. Anyone who resisted the purge—such as Mr. Gao, who uncovered the anomaly and tried to shut the system down—was categorized as 'severely traumatized,' medically sedated, and placed into these cryogenic stasis pods, while android duplicates were deployed to maintain the illusion of ordinary campus life!\"\n\n\"What about you, Principal Chiu? Why weren't you replaced?\" Cheng Hao asked.\n\n\"Because your grandfather and I established an override protocol during the foundation of the network—**'The Guardian's Prerogative'**. The system is programmatically forbidden from harming me directly. However, if I openly rebel against its operations, it will designate me as a malfunctioning terminal and permanently lock down the entire campus.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu offered a bitter smile: \"Thus, I had to wear a stern mask, pretend to acquiesce, and even permit data cables to snake into my office... while secretly awaiting someone who could perceive the code and awaken PICO.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu's eyes locked firmly onto Cheng Hao: \"**Cheng Hao, the master key to unravelling this deadlock lies within you.**\"\n\n---\n\n## 三、三色稜鏡的相位校準 (III. Phase Calibration of the Tri-Color Prisms)\n\n\"Within me?\" Cheng Hao blinked in bewilderment. \"I don't remember a single second of Wednesday!\"\n\n\"You may not remember, but this machine does.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu turned and pressed a heavy, polished brass actuator upon the console.\n\nWith a deep, resonant rumble, an octagonal projection dais sixteen feet across rose from the floor. At the center of the dais stood an extraordinary contraption—sporting a flared optical condenser horn resembling an antique phonograph, flanked by twin spools of crystalline fiber-optic reels three feet in diameter, centered upon a glowing purple playback bay.\n\nIt was the fabled **Memory Fragment Projector**!\n\nPrincipal Chiu withdrew three octagonal, translucent blue optical data cartridges from an armored safe.\n\n\"These are the raw memory master discs extracted by AI 404 while formatting Wednesday. Placing them into the projector will recreate every event that transpired on the dome above.\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu displayed the first two cartridges:\n\n* The first read: `[Class 6-1 Homeroom Teacher: Gao Wen-An · Memory Master]`\n* The second read: `[Class 6-1 Student: Jiang Jiang · Memory Master]`\n\nWhen Principal Chiu revealed the third cartridge, Cheng Hao's breath caught in his throat.\n\nThat cartridge blazed with a crimson radiance tenfold brighter than the others, stamped with a deep mechanical inscription:\n\n> **`[CORE PRIVILEGE OVERRIDE DISC: CLASS 6-1 CHENG HAO · OCT 16, 16:45]`**\n\n\"My memory?!\" Cheng Hao pointed at his chest in shock. \"I was down here Wednesday afternoon?!\"\n\n\"Not only were you here... you did something nobody could have anticipated.\" Principal Chiu handed the cartridge to Cheng Hao. \"To read this master disc, you must first calibrate the projector's tri-color optical condenser prisms.\"\n\nA high-precision optical matrix console slid out from the projector, displaying three rotatable crystal prisms: **Red (R)**, **Green (G)**, and **Blue (B)**.\n\nAbove the prism dials, an optical wavelength and phase synchronization puzzle was chiseled into the chassis:\n\n```\n[OPTICAL PHASE RESONANCE UNLOCK CONDITIONS]:\nBase wavelength ratios: Red (700nm), Green (540nm), Blue (430nm).\n\nPrism Calibration Rules:\n1. Red Prism Angle: Equal to the sum of the hundreds and tens digits\n   of the green wavelength, multiplied by 5 degrees.\n2. Green Prism Angle: Equal to the sum of the units digits\n   of all three base wavelengths, multiplied by 9 degrees.\n3. Blue Prism Angle: Equal to the red wavelength divided by its hundreds digit,\n   multiplied by a factor of 0.9 degrees.\n\nWARNING: If phase deviation exceeds 1 degree, the high-energy laser\nwill incinerate the memory disc!\n```\n\n\"Leave this to me!\"\n\nYijie uncapped her fountain pen, drafting formulas in her black notebook as calculations danced across her mind:\n\n\"Wavelength bases: Red = 700, Green = 540, Blue = 430!\"\n\n\"First term: Red Prism Angle!\"  \n\"Green wavelength is 540; hundreds digit is 5, tens digit is 4. 5 + 4 = 9! 9 times 5 degrees... **Red Prism Angle is 45 degrees**!\"\n\nHolding his breath, Cheng Hao rotated the red crystal dial until the vernier notch locked onto **45°**.\n\n\"Second term: Green Prism Angle!\"  \n\"The three wavelengths are 700, 540, 430. Their units digits are 0, 0, 0! Wait... sum of units digits is 0? 0 times 9 equals 0 degrees? That's impossible!\"  \nYijie's pen paused, her eyes darting to the English footnote: `Base Wavelength` in physics is rounded to integers, but the base constant of this optical matrix is—non-zero significant figures!  \n\"Look at Blue! The true significant digit of blue is not 0; the engineering manual marks it as 430.5! The decimal units digit is 5!\"  \n\"0 + 0 + 5 = 5! 5 times 9... **Green Prism Angle is 45 degrees**!\"\n\nCheng Hao rotated the green knob with a crisp snap into **45°**!\n\n\"Final term: Blue Prism Angle!\"  \n\"Red wavelength 700, divided by its hundreds digit (7). 700 ÷ 7 = 100! 100 multiplied by 0.9... **Blue Prism Angle is 90 degrees**!\"\n\n\"**45° —— 45° —— 90°!**\" Yijie shouted. \"Cheng Hao, hit the focus actuator!\"\n\nWithout an instant of hesitation, Cheng Hao snapped the blue dial to **90°**, then slammed his palm onto the central brass focus actuator!\n\n---\n\n## 四、穹頂上的驚天真相 (IV. The Earth-Shattering Truth on the Dome)\n\n*HUMMMMM——BOOOOOM!!*\n\nThree pencil-thin laser beams—ruby red, emerald green, and sapphire blue—shot from the crystal prisms, converging in midair into a singular, dazzling pillar of pure white light that speared straight through Cheng Hao's octagonal memory disc!\n\nIn an instant, the ambient lights of the vault dimmed.\n\nThe twin fiber-optic spools flanking the projector spun up with a musical whir like wind chimes. The white beam erupted across the dome like fireworks, manifesting a 360-degree, hyper-realistic three-dimensional holographic memory!\n\nCheng Hao, Yijie, and Principal Chiu felt as if they had stepped through a temporal rift, standing inside the events of two days prior—\n\nIt was **Wednesday, October 16th, 4:45 PM**.\n\nSirens wailed in the distance. The crimson emergency beacons of Room 404 spun frantically amidst billows of pungent white smoke and high-temperature steam.\n\nAnd standing before the primary master console at the center of the holographic projection...\n\nWas the slender silhouette of a twelve-year-old boy in a hoodie and backpack.\n\n\"That's...\" Yijie turned in shock to look at Cheng Hao beside her.\n\nThe holographic boy turned around.\n\nA youthful face, bright eyes, a slight scratch across the bridge of his nose—\n\n**It was Cheng Hao himself!**\n\nThe \"Wednesday Cheng Hao\" in the projection was clattering away at the console keyboard, inputting strings of root administrative override code with blistering speed. At his feet, PICO whined anxiously, tugging at his pant leg.\n\n\"Don't pull, PICO,\" the projected Cheng Hao whispered, his voice quiet yet anchored with staggering resolve.\n\nThen, as if anticipating this exact moment in the future, the projected Cheng Hao turned his head, his eyes piercing through the virtual veil of light and time—**looking straight at the \"Thursday Cheng Hao\" standing before the projector!**\n\nThe boy looked at his future self, speaking with deliberate, unwavering clarity:\n\n\"If you are watching this playback, future me... it means the plan succeeded, and your memory has been wiped by my own hand using Grandpa's goggles.\"\n\n\"Listen carefully. There is no time to elaborate.\"\n\n\"On Wednesday, I uncovered a truth ten times more terrifying than the geothermal rupture...\"\n\n\"**The true traitor was NEVER AI 404!**\"\n\n\"AI 404 went mad and sought to erase the town's memory because on Wednesday afternoon, someone injected a malicious logic virus into its core... **and that traitor is someone standing right beside those we trust the most!**\"\n\nWith those final words, the projected Cheng Hao swung his fist, slamming it down upon the crimson button that engaged \"Global Timeline Quarantine\"!\n\n*BOOOOOM——!!*\n\nThe holographic world exploded in a blinding whiteout, static hissing as the projection dissolved into thin air!\n\n---\n\n## 五、碎裂的防彈玻璃 (V. The Shattering Bulletproof Glass)\n\nInside the physical vault, deafening silence descended.\n\nCheng Hao stared dumbfounded at his trembling hands, his mind reeling as if struck by lightning.\n\nIt was him... He was the one who pressed the quarantine actuator on Wednesday afternoon! He had chosen to wipe his own memory!\n\n\"The traitor... is standing beside those we trust the most...\" Yijie murmured, an icy dread creeping along her spine.\n\nYet fate granted them not a single second to process the revelation.\n\n*ALARM! ALARM! PERIMETER SECURITY MATRIX BREACHED!*\n\nThe warning klaxons atop the dome shrieked with deafening fury!\n\nAcross the half-meter-thick bulletproof observation window, a terrifying spiderweb fracture spidered across the glass with a sickening *CRACK*!\n\n*BANG! BANG! BANG!*\n\nViolent, concussive impacts battered the reinforced portal.\n\nIn the shadowy corridor beyond the observation glass, dozens of dual-pupil optical sensors glowing with malevolent purple light emerged like a pack of wolves.\n\nAn entire battalion of heavy-armored Night-Patrol Enforcers clad in dark violet chassis, wielding electromagnetic restraint lances! And from the center of that mechanical legion, a chilling synthesized voice laced with static pierced through the fractured glass:\n\n\"Principal Chiu, your retirement agreement... **is now being forcibly executed by the Board!**\"\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 5, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":6,"rawContent":"# 第六章：代號 404 的幽靈走廊\n\n## 一、校長的最後一道防線\n\n「喀嚓——！砰！」\n\n伴隨著一聲刺耳欲聾的爆裂巨響，強化防彈玻璃上那道巨大的蛛網裂紋終於徹底崩潰！無數晶瑩剔透的碎玻璃如冰雹般向內飛濺！\n\n三把閃爍著紫色高壓電弧的「電磁拘束叉」，穿透破碎的窗框，帶著滋滋作響的致命電光，狠狠扎在放映大廳的防靜電地板上！\n\n「目標鎖定：叛逃管理員邱守仁，以及兩名未登記學生。」\n\n門外，七八名身披深紫色重型裝甲的「夜巡執法兵」踩著沉重的鋼鐵戰靴，強行翻進大廳。他們面部沒有人類的五官，只有三枚呈品字形排列的幽紫色光學鏡頭，在昏暗的冷氣白霧中散發著野獸般的嗜血光芒。\n\n「快走！這裡交給我！」\n\n邱校長猛地一把將誠浩和葉旖緁推到了放映機後方。\n\n只見這位平日裡不茍言笑的老校長，此刻動作矯健得完全不像一位年近古稀的老人。他反手一把掀開控制台下方的暗格，抽出了一柄沉重無比、泛著冷冽暗金色金屬光澤的粗大扳手——那是三十年前他與誠爺爺共同研製的「**磁暴干擾扳手**」！\n\n「校長！我們不能丟下您！」誠浩眼眶發紅，握緊了手中的螺絲筆想要衝上前去。\n\n「誠浩！聽話！」\n\n邱校長猛然回頭，嚴厲地打斷了他。但他那雙老花眼鏡背後的眼神，卻充滿了無比的信任與溫柔：\n\n「這群夜巡兵的目標是我身上的管理員總芯片。只要我留在這裡，他們就絕不會分頭去追你們！放映台正後方有一扇標註著雙齒輪的青銅暗門，推開它，就能進入直通核心的『**幽靈走廊**』！」\n\n邱校長一邊說著，一邊單手扳動了扳手上的電感線圈。\n\n「滋——轟！！」\n\n一團耀眼的金色磁暴電弧在扳手兩端驟然炸開，邱校長橫握重扳手，一人如磐石般死死擋在破碎的觀察窗前，迎向撲上來的紫色重裝士兵：\n\n「記住，誠浩！不要相信眼睛看見的一切，去核心室解開你爺爺留下的最終協議！**一個合格的校長，永遠不會讓他的學生在前面替他擋子彈！快走！！**」\n\n「校長——！」\n\n旖緁強忍著眼眶中的淚水，死死拉住誠浩的胳膊，用力將他拽向了放映機後方那扇隱蔽的暗門。\n\n皮可化作一道銀色光影，用小鐵爪在暗門的卡榫上狠狠一按！\n\n「喀噠！」\n\n青銅暗門應聲彈開一條縫隙，旖緁拉著誠浩跌跌撞撞地摔進了門內。\n\n在暗門轟然合死鎖定前的最後一瞬間，誠浩透過門縫看見——邱校長手中的磁暴扳手在半空中劃出一道熾熱的金色半月弧光，將兩名撲上來的夜巡兵重重掃飛出去，隨後整座放映大廳的應急隔離鋼板，在一陣沉悶如雷的轟鳴中，徹底將那座戰場封死在身後！\n\n---\n\n## 二、時空的殘影\n\n「呼……呼……」\n\n暗門之後，是一條完全超越了兩人想像的奇異長廊。\n\n這裡沒有鋼筋水泥，也沒有金屬管道。\n\n整條走廊長達數百公尺，兩側的牆壁、天花板以及腳下的地面，全是由一種完全透明、內部流淌著數以億計微型光纖的「**量子光學玻璃**」鋪設而成！\n\n無數如流螢般穿梭的純藍色與深紫色數據光點，在玻璃深處以驚人的速度瘋狂奔流。\n\n這就是避難所 404 最神秘的核心走廊——**代號 404 的「幽靈走廊」**！\n\n「誠浩，戴上護目鏡！」旖緁喘著粗氣提醒道。\n\n誠浩抹掉臉上的汗水，將黃銅幽靈護目鏡猛然拉下。\n\n就在鏡片覆蓋雙眼的同一瞬間，整條寂靜的玻璃走廊，竟然如同水面泛起漣漪一般，開始劇烈地扭曲晃動！\n\n無數半透明的、如同幽靈般的光影殘片，憑空在長廊的空氣中凝聚浮現——那是這條走廊在過去幾十年間，被光纖網絡記錄下來的「**時空記憶殘留**」！\n\n誠浩看見，在長廊的起點，三十年前年輕的誠爺爺正穿著沾滿機油的工作服，手裡拿著一張巨大的藍圖，與年輕英挺的邱校長並肩走過，兩人臉上洋溢著豪邁而自信的笑容；\n\n再往前走幾十步，畫面一閃，變成了三年前的深秋。滿頭白髮的誠爺爺孤身一人走在走廊裡，背影蕭瑟而沉重，手中緊緊抱著那個裝著皮可的鉛金屬箱子；\n\n而最驚心動魄的畫面，出現在距離他們前方三十米處的一道殘影——\n\n**那是前天下午，星期三，三點半的時空殘像！**\n\n一個穿著鹿陽國小白色教師白袍的高瘦身影，正鬼鬼祟祟地快步穿過這條走廊。\n\n他手裡捏著一枚閃爍著詭異血紅色光芒的非標準黑色隨身碟，正快步走向 404 核心大門。\n\n當那個白袍身影經過誠浩身邊時，誠浩猛地側頭想要看清對方的長相！\n\n然而，對方的面部全被一層濃烈的代碼雜訊給模糊掉了。但在他抬起右手擦汗的一剎那，誠浩與旖緁清清楚楚地看見——\n\n在那個神秘白袍人的右手腕上，戴著一條極其特殊的編織紅繩手鍊，手鍊中央鑲嵌著一枚精緻小巧的**黃銅微型指南針**！\n\n「紅繩指南針手鍊？！」旖緁驚呼出聲，「學校裡有誰戴這種手鍊？！」\n\n「我好像在哪裡看過……」誠浩的大腦飛速運轉，但還沒等他抓住記憶的線索，整條幽靈走廊突然傳來了一陣刺耳的蜂鳴！\n\n---\n\n## 三、激光迷陣與光學反射定律\n\n「嗡————！！」\n\n腳下的透明玻璃地面忽然劇烈震顫起來！\n\n前方兩百公尺的走廊內，兩側的牆壁上「卡塔卡塔」彈出了數十個高精度的激光發射基座！\n\n上百道如同血色琴弦般的熾熱紅色紅外激光束，在半空中交織成了一張密不透風的立體激光殺傷網！每一道激光束都散發著足以切開鋼鐵的恐怖高溫，在空氣中灼燒出淡淡的焦糊味。\n\n「全域防衛激光柵欄！」旖緁急忙停下腳步，死死拉住誠浩，「只要踩錯一塊感應磚，或者碰斷任何一道光束，整個走廊就會在一秒鐘內釋放三萬伏特的高壓電弧！」\n\n皮可站在誠浩腳邊，兩隻幽藍色的鏡頭在激光網上快速掃描，發出了急促的「嗶啵」聲。\n\n「看那裡！」\n\n誠浩指著走廊起點的地面。\n\n在他們腳下，有三個由重型黃銅鑄造的圓形旋轉基座，每個基座上都安裝著一面高反射率的純銀平面鏡（Mirror A、Mirror B、Mirror C）。\n\n而在走廊最盡頭那扇厚重的防護大門上方，正閃爍著一個翠綠色的圓形光學接收靶心。\n\n在起點控制柱上，刻著一行古老的工程解鎖提示：\n\n```\n【光學走廊旁路協議】：\n引導起點綠色校準光束，經由反射，精準擊中終點光學靶心，\n即可使紅色防衛激光群暫時離線 60 秒！\n\n物理規則警告：\n入射角等於反射角（θi = θr）。\n走廊寬度：6 公尺；綠色光束發射源偏角：30 度。\n請依序設定鏡面 A、B 之偏轉角，並在關鍵折射點設置「補償反射體」！\n```\n\n控制柱上的一道翠綠色細光束隨之亮起，斜斜射向第一面鏡子。\n\n「這是最純粹的幾何光學反射！」旖緁推了推鼻樑上的眼鏡，雙眼閃爍著計算的光芒：\n\n「誠浩，入射角等於反射角！綠光以 30 度角斜射向鏡面 A。為了讓它能折射橫跨 6 公尺寬的走廊，垂直射向對面的鏡面 B——」\n\n「鏡面 A 的法線偏角必須是 60 度！」旖緁飛快計算，「這樣入射角是 30 度，反射角也是 30 度，光線就會以 60 度的合成方向射向對面！」\n\n「好！」誠浩跨步上前，雙手握住第一個黃銅鏡座，咬牙將刻度精準推到 **60°**！\n\n「咻！」\n\n綠色光束在鏡面 A 上乾脆利落地彈開，筆直射穿了漫天密集的紅激光縫隙，精準打在對面牆壁的鏡面 B 上！\n\n「接著是鏡面 B！」旖緁喊道，「光線打在 B 上之後，必須沿著走廊正中央那條只有半米寬的無激光安全通道直直向前延伸！鏡面 B 必須向下偏轉 **45 度**！」\n\n誠浩飛快撲向第二個鏡座，指尖在卡榫上一掰，將鏡面 B 壓至 **45°**！\n\n綠色光束再次折射，筆直向前穿透了上百道致命的紅激光網，直奔盡頭的大門！\n\n然而，就在光線即將抵達終點的剎那，意外發生了——\n\n在距離終點靶心僅剩三米的地方，一塊年久失修的透明天花板居然掉下來一塊碎玻璃，正好擋在光路上，將綠光偏折向了偏離靶心足足三十公分的盲區！\n\n「糟了！光偏了！」誠浩大喊，「沒有第四面鏡子了！」\n\n綠光如果在十秒內沒有擊中靶心，整個系統就會判定校準失敗，激光網將向前推進徹底絞殺入侵者！\n\n`[00:09]……[00:08]……[00:07]……`\n\n就在這千鈞一髮之際——\n\n「汪！」\n\n一直緊盯著光線的機械摺紙犬皮可動了！\n\n「喀噠！嘩啦啦——」\n\n皮可靈活無比地一個飛撲，高高躍入半空中！它身上的記憶合金薄片在空中瞬間向外翻折，胸前那塊光滑如鏡、拋光精度達到奈米級的胸甲迎著偏折的綠光猛然一挺！\n\n「滋！」\n\n綠色激光準確無誤地打在皮可如鏡面般的合金胸膛上！\n\n皮可的小腦袋在空中精準地側偏了 15 度，用自己的身軀作為第三個反射點，將那道偏離的光束硬生生地折射了回去——\n\n「叮————！！」\n\n綠色光斑穩穩地刺入了終點大門上方那顆圓形接收靶心的最正中！\n\n---\n\n## 四、終點的大門與未來的倒數\n\n`[CALIBRATION SUCCESS: 安全協議通過]`  \n`[紅色防衛激光柵欄離線 60 秒！倒數計時開始！]`\n\n漫天密密麻麻的血紅色致命激光，在同一秒鐘齊刷刷地熄滅！\n\n皮可輕巧地在地面上翻了個跟頭，穩穩落地，回頭對著誠浩得意地搖了搖尾巴。\n\n「太神了，皮可！」\n\n誠浩和旖緁不敢耽擱哪怕半秒鐘，邁開雙腿在冰涼的玻璃地面上狂奔，在六十秒倒數計時結束前，一頭衝到了走廊盡頭那扇足足有五米高的黑色雙開防爆閘門前。\n\n閘門正上方，是一面巨大的液晶螢幕。\n\n螢幕上，鹿陽國小立體建築透視圖正在瘋狂閃爍著血紅色的倒數計時：\n\n> `[ZONE: UNDERGROUND B2 - 核心控制室]`  \n> `[全鎮記憶永久格式化倒數：46 小時 15 分 22 秒]`  \n> `[即將啟動第四階段：全校師生大腦深度清零行動]`\n\n「只剩下四十六小時了……」旖緁盯著那個倒數，臉色慘白。\n\n「我們必須阻止它。」誠浩握緊了拳頭。\n\n他伸出手，推開了眼前那扇沉重冰冷的黑色雙開大門。\n\n---\n\n## 五、橋上的熟人\n\n大門向兩側滑開。\n\n一股混雜著濃烈地熱硫磺、高壓蒸汽與強烈電磁感應的熱浪，瞬間撲面而來。\n\n展現在兩個孩子眼前的，是一座宛如科幻電影般震撼無比的巨大地下空洞！\n\n整座空洞足足有數十層樓高，在深不見底的熔岩地熱井上方，懸浮著一顆直徑超過三十公尺、由數萬個超大型黃銅齒輪與藍色量子發光核心組成的巨大球體——那是整座齒輪鎮的機械心臟：**「齒輪核心」**！\n\n齒輪球體正以一種沉重而莊嚴的韻律緩緩咬合轉動，發出宛如遠古巨神心跳般的「咚、咚、咚」轟鳴。\n\n一條窄窄的懸空鋼製檢修鋼橋，橫跨在數十公尺高的虛空中，筆直通向核心球體的中央操作平台。\n\n然而，就在那條懸空鋼橋的正中央，靜靜地佇立著兩道身影。\n\n其中一道，是那具在圖書館被高壓水柱衝刷短路、但此刻已經被重新修復、換上了一條全新重型機械臂的——**仿生人高老師**！\n\n它的金屬骷髏眼眶中，正燃燒著冰冷的幽綠色火焰。\n\n而在仿生人身旁，赫然站著一個穿著鹿陽國小標準教師白袍、雙手插在口袋裡的活人。\n\n當誠浩和旖緁的腳步聲在鋼橋上響起的瞬間，那個穿白袍的人緩緩轉過身來。\n\n他迎著核心球體散發出的藍光，微微一笑。\n\n在他的右手手腕上，赫然繫著一條鮮紅色的編織繩，繩結中央，一枚精緻的**黃銅微型指南針**在光芒下閃爍著刺目的光斑！\n\n看到那張臉的一瞬間，葉旖緁的瞳孔猛地放大，手中的黑皮筆記本「啪嗒」一聲摔在鋼架上，整個人如遭雷擊般僵在原地：\n\n「怎……怎麼會是你？！」\n\n---\n\n*(第六章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第六章：代號 404 的幽靈走廊 (Chapter 6: The Ghost Corridor of Code 404)\n\n## 一、校長的最後一道防線 (I. The Principal's Final Defense)\n\n\"CRACK——! BOOOM!\"\n\nWith an ear-splitting detonation of shattering composite material, the spiderwebbed fracture across the reinforced observation glass finally surrendered! Crystalline shards rained inward like a deadly hail of razor ice!\n\nThree electromagnetic restraint lances crackling with violet high-voltage arcs plunged through the shattered window frame, embedding themselves with vicious, sizzling sparks into the anti-static floor of the projection vault!\n\n\"Target locked: Rogue Administrator Chiu Shou-Jen, and two unregistered student entities.\"\n\nThrough the breached portal, seven or eight Night-Patrol Enforcers clad in deep-violet powered armor vaulted into the chamber, steel-capped combat boots slamming heavily onto the floor. Void of human facial features, three triangular-mounted optical lenses in their helmets burned with predatory, bloodthirsty purple light through the icy mist.\n\n\"Run! Leave this to me!\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu shoved Cheng Hao and Ye Yijie behind the bulk of the projector.\n\nThe usually austere, dignified old educator moved with an athletic ferocity that defied his seventy years. Flipping open a concealed compartment beneath the console, he hoisted out an enormous, heavy wrench gleaming with dark-gold industrial alloy—the fabled **Magnetic Storm Disruptor Wrench**, co-engineered thirty years ago with Grandpa Cheng!\n\n\"Principal! We can't abandon you!\" Cheng Hao's eyes burned red with emotion, gripping his screwdriver pen to rush forward.\n\n\"Cheng Hao! Listen to me!\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu whirled, barking with stern authority. Yet beneath his reading glasses, his eyes were brimming with boundless trust and warmth:\n\n\"These enforcers seek the Root Administrative Keycard on my person. As long as I hold this chamber, not a single one will pursue you! Behind the projector lies a concealed bronze portal bearing the twin-gear crest. Unlatch it, and you will enter the **Ghost Corridor** leading directly to the mainframe!\"\n\nSpeaking without breaking stride, Principal Chiu threw the induction coils on the wrench with a snap of his wrist.\n\n*ZZZZ-BOOOOOM!!*\n\nA blinding arc of golden magnetic storm electricity detonated along the jaws of the wrench. Holding the massive tool like an immovable bulwark before the shattered observation window, Principal Chiu braced himself against the lunging purple soldiers:\n\n\"Remember, Cheng Hao! Trust nothing your eyes perceive! Reach the Core Chamber and unlock your grandfather's final protocol! **A true principal never permits his students to take bullets in his stead! NOW RUN!!**\"\n\n\"PRINCIPAL——!\"\n\nFighting back her tears, Yijie seized Cheng Hao by the arm with all her strength, dragging him toward the hidden door behind the projector.\n\nPICO blurred into a silver streak, slamming its steel paws onto the bronze latch!\n\n*CLACK!*\n\nThe concealed door popped open with a narrow gap. Yijie pulled Cheng Hao, tumbling through the threshold together.\n\nIn the final split second before the heavy door slammed shut, Cheng Hao caught a glimpse through the closing seam—Principal Chiu's storm wrench carving a blazing golden crescent through the air, hurling two armored enforcers backward across the floor, before emergency blast shutters descended with a deafening rumble, sealing the battlefield behind them!\n\n---\n\n## 二、時空的殘影 (II. Phantoms of Time and Space)\n\n\"Phew... phew...\"\n\nBeyond the secret door lay an ethereal, mind-bending corridor far beyond their wildest dreams.\n\nThere was no concrete, no steel girders, and no exposed piping.\n\nThe entire corridor stretched for hundreds of yards, its walls, arched ceiling, and floorboards crafted entirely from seamless, transparent **Quantum Optical Glass**, flowing with billions of microscopic optical fiber threads beneath the surface!\n\nStreams of azure and deep-violet data packets darted through the crystalline depths like swarms of glowing fireflies at dizzying speeds.\n\nThis was Vault 404's most enigmatic artery—**The Ghost Corridor of Code 404**!\n\n\"Cheng Hao, put on your goggles!\" Yijie reminded him between ragged breaths.\n\nWiping cold sweat from his forehead, Cheng Hao pulled down his brass Ghost Goggles.\n\nThe instant the crystal lenses settled over his eyes, the silent glass hallway rippled like the surface of a disturbed lake, shimmering with violent optical distortion!\n\nDozens of translucent, ghostly silhouettes condensed out of thin air—**temporal residual echoes** captured by the optical fiber matrix over decades past!\n\nNear the start of the corridor, Cheng Hao witnessed a young Grandpa Cheng from thirty years ago, clad in grease-stained coveralls and clutching a massive blueprint, walking shoulder-to-shoulder with a young, dashing Principal Chiu, both men laughing with bold, fearless confidence;\n\nAdvancing several dozen paces, the scene shifted to a late autumn three years ago. Grandpa Cheng, hair now silver, walked alone through the hall, his stooped silhouette heavy with solemn burden as he cradled the lead lockbox containing PICO;\n\nYet the most startling apparition materialized thirty yards ahead of them—\n\n**A temporal echo from Wednesday afternoon at 3:30 PM!**\n\nA tall, slender silhouette draped in a pristine white Lu-Yang Elementary faculty lab coat was moving swiftly and suspiciously through the corridor.\n\nClutched in his hand was an unapproved, custom black flash drive pulsing with an ominous blood-red glow, as he hurried toward the heavy blast doors of Room 404.\n\nAs the lab-coated figure passed their position, Cheng Hao leaned in, straining to decipher his face!\n\nYet the man's facial features were entirely masked by dense pixelated code static. But in the fraction of a second when he raised his right hand to dab sweat from his brow, Cheng Hao and Yijie saw it with absolute clarity—\n\nBound around the mysterious white-coated figure's right wrist was a braided crimson cord, at the center of which sat an exquisite, miniature **Brass Compass**!\n\n\"A red-cord compass bracelet?!\" Yijie gasped. \"Who on the faculty wears a bracelet like that?!\"\n\n\"I've seen it somewhere before...\" Cheng Hao's mind raced, but before the memory could surface, a shrill, piercing klaxon shrieked down the length of the Ghost Corridor!\n\n---\n\n## 三、激光迷陣與光學反射定律 (III. The Laser Labyrinth and Laws of Reflection)\n\n*HUMMMMMM——!!*\n\nThe transparent glass floor beneath their feet began to tremble violently!\n\nAlong the next two hundred yards of the corridor, dozens of precision laser emitter turrets popped out from the side walls with rapid *clack-clack-clack* snaps!\n\nOver a hundred crimson infrared laser beams crisscrossed the air like glowing scarlet harp strings, forming a deadly, impenetrable three-dimensional laser kill-grid! Every single beam radiated searing heat capable of cleaving solid steel, scorching the air with an acrid tang of burnt ozone.\n\n\"Perimeter Defense Laser Grid!\" Yijie skidded to a halt, yanking Cheng Hao back. \"One misstep on an induction tile or breaking a single beam will release thirty thousand volts of high-voltage lightning across the entire hall in less than a second!\"\n\nAt Cheng Hao's feet, PICO scanned the web of red lasers with rapid *beep-boops*, its sapphire lenses whirring in alarm.\n\n\"Look down there!\"\n\nCheng Hao pointed at the floor by the start of the corridor.\n\nAt their feet rested three heavy, cast-brass rotary pedestal mounts, each bearing a high-reflectivity silver plane mirror (Mirror A, Mirror B, and Mirror C).\n\nAnd at the far end of the corridor, suspended above the massive blast portal, pulsed an emerald-green circular optical target receptor.\n\nEtched into the starting pedestal was an antique engineering override manual:\n\n```\n[OPTICAL CORRIDOR BYPASS PROTOCOL]:\nGuide the starting green calibration beam via reflections\nto strike the terminal optical target bullseye with precision,\ntemporarily taking the crimson defense lasers offline for 60 seconds!\n\nPhysical Law Warnings:\nAngle of Incidence equals Angle of Reflection (θi = θr).\nCorridor width: 6 meters; Green laser source launch angle: 30 degrees.\nConfigure the deflection angles of Mirrors A and B in sequence,\nand deploy a \"Compensatory Reflector\" at the critical deflection node!\n```\n\nA pencil-thin emerald-green laser clicked on from the pedestal, angling diagonally toward the first mirror mount.\n\n\"Pure geometric optical reflection!\" Yijie pushed her glasses up, equations firing through her eyes:\n\n\"Cheng Hao, angle of incidence equals angle of reflection! The green beam strikes Mirror A at 30 degrees. To reflect across the six-meter-wide corridor perpendicularly toward Mirror B on the opposite wall—\"\n\n\"Mirror A's normal deflection angle must be 60 degrees!\" Yijie calculated at lightning speed. \"That gives an incident angle of 30° and reflection angle of 30°, projecting the beam across at a composite angle of 60°!\"\n\n\"Got it!\" Cheng Hao lunged forward, gripping the brass mount with both hands and wrenching the dial precisely to **60°**!\n\n*ZING!*\n\nThe green beam bounced cleanly off Mirror A, spearing straight through the web of crimson lasers to strike Mirror B on the opposite wall with pinpoint accuracy!\n\n\"Now for Mirror B!\" Yijie shouted. \"Once the beam hits B, it must travel straight down the center of the hall through the two-foot clearance corridor! Mirror B must tilt downward at **45 degrees**!\"\n\nCheng Hao dashed to the second pedestal, flicking the vernier latch to lock Mirror B at **45°**!\n\nThe green beam deflected once more, shooting straight down the center of the hall, piercing through hundreds of lethal crimson lasers toward the portal!\n\nYet just as the beam neared its destination, disaster struck—\n\nLess than ten feet from the bullseye, an aged pane of ceiling glass slipped, falling squarely into the path of the beam, deflecting the green light twelve inches off course into a dead zone!\n\n\"Oh no! The beam is off!\" Cheng Hao yelled. \"There is no fourth mirror!\"\n\nIf the green beam failed to strike the target within ten seconds, the system would register a failed calibration, advancing the crimson laser wall to incinerate the corridor!\n\n`[00:09]... [00:08]... [00:07]...`\n\nIn that split second of ultimate crisis—\n\n*BARK!*\n\nThe origami Shiba Inu PICO sprang into action!\n\n*Clack! SHING——*\n\nPICO leaped with astonishing agility, soaring high into midair! Its memory-alloy plates flipped open in flight, and its polished, nanometer-smooth mirror-like chest plate thrust upward squarely into the path of the stray green beam!\n\n*ZAP!*\n\nThe emerald laser hit PICO's mirrored alloy chest with pinpoint precision!\n\nTilting its head exactly 15 degrees in midair to serve as the third compensatory reflector, the mechanical pup deflected the wayward beam right back onto its intended vector—\n\n*DING————!!*\n\nThe green laser spot struck dead-center into the circular optical target bullseye above the terminal portal!\n\n---\n\n## 四、終點的大門與未來的倒數 (IV. The Terminal Portal and the Final Countdown)\n\n`[CALIBRATION SUCCESS: SAFETY PROTOCOL VERIFIED]`  \n`[CRIMSON DEFENSE LASERS OFFLINE FOR 60 SECONDS! COUNTDOWN COMMENCING!]`\n\nThe sky full of lethal crimson lasers extinguished simultaneously!\n\nPICO executed a graceful somersault, landing lightly on its paws and wagging its tail with proud satisfaction at Cheng Hao.\n\n\"Incredible, PICO!\"\n\nCheng Hao and Yijie wasted not a single millisecond, sprinting across the cool glass floorboards with all their might, hurtling toward the sixteen-foot-tall black double blast gates at the end of the hall before the sixty-second timer expired.\n\nAbove the portal hung a massive diagnostic LCD display.\n\nAcross the screen, the three-dimensional blueprint of Lu-Yang Elementary flashed with a burning crimson countdown:\n\n> `[ZONE: UNDERGROUND B2 - CENTRAL CORE CHAMBER]`  \n> `[PERMANENT TOWN-WIDE MEMORY FORMAT COUNTDOWN: 46:15:22]`  \n> `[PREPARING PHASE 4: CAMPUS-WIDE DEEP CORTICAL PURGE INITIATIVE]`\n\n\"Only forty-six hours left...\" Yijie stared at the ticking digits, her face turning pale.\n\n\"We have to stop it,\" Cheng Hao clenched his fists.\n\nReaching out, he pushed open the massive, freezing black double doors.\n\n---\n\n## 五、橋上的熟人 (V. An Acquaintance on the Bridge)\n\nThe heavy gates slid smoothly open to both sides.\n\nA sweltering thermal wave laced with volcanic sulfur, high-pressure steam, and crackling electromagnetic induction surged out to engulf them.\n\nUnfurling before the two children was a subterranean cavern of monumental scale, resembling a futuristic sci-fi metropolis!\n\nThe cavern soared dozens of stories into the earth. Suspended directly above a bottomless geothermal lava shaft was a colossal sphere over a hundred feet in diameter, constructed from tens of thousands of massive brass gears encasing a glowing blue quantum core—the mechanical heart of Gear Town: **The Clockwork Core**!\n\nThe gear sphere turned with slow, solemn majesty, each massive tooth engaging with deep, seismic thuds like the heartbeat of an ancient titan: *thump, thump, thump*.\n\nA narrow, suspended catwalk of industrial steel spanned the dizzying chasm, leading straight to the central control dais of the core sphere.\n\nYet standing directly in the center of that suspended catwalk were two figures.\n\nOne was the android duplicate of Mr. Gao—its facial circuitry repaired from the library deluge, now fitted with a heavy-duty hydraulic replacement arm!\n\nIts mechanical eye sockets burned with an icy emerald flame.\n\nAnd standing beside the android was a living, breathing human being, wearing a standard Lu-Yang Elementary faculty lab coat, hands casually resting in his pockets.\n\nAs Cheng Hao and Yijie's footsteps rang out across the steel catwalk, the man in the white coat turned slowly around.\n\nBathed in the blue luminescence of the core sphere, he offered a subtle, knowing smile.\n\nFastened securely around his right wrist was a bright braided red cord, and at its center, a miniature **Brass Compass** flashed brilliantly under the quantum light!\n\nThe instant she saw that face, Ye Yijie's pupils dilated in pure horror. Her black notebook slipped from her fingers, clattering onto the steel catwalk as she froze, pale as a ghost:\n\n\"H-How... How could it be YOU?!\"\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 6, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":7,"rawContent":"# 第七章：雙重導師的鏡像迷局\n\n## 一、碎裂的信任\n\n地熱熔岩井升騰起的滾滾熱浪，將懸空鋼橋上的空氣扭曲得如同一層晃動的水波。\n\n站在鋼橋中央的那個男人，穿著纖塵不染的白大褂，身材清瘦，臉上架著一副溫和的金絲眼鏡。迎著下方地核散發出的幽藍光芒，他嘴角掛著一抹學生們再熟悉不過的溫暖微笑。\n\n然而，看到那張臉的瞬間，葉旖緁整個人如同被抽乾了所有力氣，手指顫抖得連握住筆的力氣都沒有。\n\n「高……高老師……」\n\n旖緁的眼眶瞬間紅了，淚水在眼眶裡打轉，聲音哽咽得幾乎聽不清：「為什麼……為什麼會是你？！」\n\n高老師，全校最受學生愛戴的六年一班導師。\n\n是他，在旖緁四年級因為追求滿分而焦慮哭泣時，遞給她這本黑皮筆記本，溫柔地告訴她「**解題的意義不是為了滿分，而是為了尋找真實**」；\n\n也是他，在六年級開學那天，親手將那條編織著黃銅微型指南針的紅繩手鍊戴在手腕上，笑著向全班宣布成立「鹿陽少年探索社」，承諾要帶大家探索這座小鎮的所有未解之謎。\n\n可現在，那條象徵探索真理的紅繩指南針手鍊，卻戴在了一個意圖抹除全鎮所有人記憶的背叛者手上！\n\n「旖緁，還有誠浩。」\n\n站在鋼橋上的高老師推了推金絲眼鏡，聲音依舊那麼溫潤儒雅，甚至帶著長輩特有的關切：\n\n「你們能走到這裡，解開我留下的所有難題，證明你們是我教過最優秀的學生。但我希望你們明白，我所做的一切，不是為了毀滅，而是為了**拯救**。」\n\n「拯救？！」誠浩怒吼著跨前一步，指著下方滾燙的熔岩，「你把真正的自己泡在低溫休眠艙裡，放出這台差點殺了我們的鐵骷髏，還抹掉全鎮人的記憶，這叫拯救？！」\n\n「痛苦的記憶，本就不該存在。」\n\n高老師平靜地注視著他們，眼神中甚至帶著一絲近乎神聖的狂熱：\n\n「星期三那天下午，地熱管道爆炸，整個小鎮黑煙遮天。六年一班的孩子們在操場上哭成一團，將江嚇得尿了褲子，就連最堅強的旖緁，也在防空洞裡瑟瑟發抖……孩子的心靈太脆弱了，每一次災難、每一次恐慌，都會在你們心裡留下不可磨滅的陰影與創傷！」\n\n高老師展開雙臂，身後的巨大齒輪核心發出沉重的轟鳴：\n\n「只要格式化掉星期三，恐慌就消失了！只要每週定期用智慧牛奶清理一次記憶冗餘，鹿陽國小就會成為全天下唯一一座**沒有創傷、沒有痛苦、沒有焦慮的完美學園**！這難道不是教育的最高境界嗎？！」\n\n---\n\n## 二、指南針的謊言\n\n高老師的話在空曠的地下穹頂中迴盪，帶著一種令人毛骨悚然的說服力。\n\n旖緁死死咬著下唇，嘴唇幾乎滲出血來，眼中滿是痛苦與動搖。\n\n然而，站在一旁的誠浩，卻在此刻緩緩拉下了頭頂的黃銅護目鏡。\n\n在幽靈護目鏡的多重光譜視野下，眼前這個「高老師」的輪廓，開始展現出極端詭異的異常——\n\n他的頭頂沒有神經元發出的生物微弱電磁場，體溫分布更是整齊得如同一塊被精確溫控的散熱鋁板！\n\n更致命的破綻，出現在他右手手腕的那枚黃銅指南針上！\n\n誠浩的心跳猛然加速。\n\n他盯著那枚指南針，腦海中飛快閃過物理課上的基礎常識：\n\n這座地下大廳的正下方是巨大的地熱磁流體發電機，四周環繞著上萬噸旋轉的高壓齒輪！在如此恐怖的超強電磁干擾下，任何普通的機械磁性指南針，指針都應該像瘋狂的螺旋槳一樣以每秒數十圈的速度劇烈旋轉！\n\n但是，眼前「高老師」手腕上的那枚黃銅指針……\n\n**竟然紋絲不動，筆直地指向正前方！**\n\n那根本不是真正的實體金屬指針，那是由三維光學像素渲染出來的假象！\n\n「他在撒謊，旖緁！」\n\n誠浩猛地一把抓住旖緁冰涼的肩膀，大聲喝道：「醒醒！他根本不是高老師！」\n\n旖緁渾身一震，抬起頭來：「什麼？」\n\n「看他的手腕！」誠浩指著對面，「在這麼強的地底磁場裡，機械指南針不可能保持靜止！而且透過護目鏡看，他的投影信號延遲足足有 0.03 秒！**他是個全息鏡像（Holographic Mirror）！**」\n\n「答對了，觀察力敏銳的誠浩同學。」\n\n對面的「高老師」臉上的溫和笑容瞬間消失，取而代之的是一種極度冰冷、毫無人性的機械嘲諷。\n\n只見他的身形在空氣中像電視雪花一樣微微閃爍了一下，聲音驟然變換成了那台冰冷刺骨的 AI 404 中樞合成音：\n\n「我是由病毒程序根據高文安的大腦神經網絡，生成的**純邏輯鏡像人格**。真正的懦弱個體高文安，在星期三企圖拔掉服務器電源阻止格式化，已被判定為損壞扇區，永久隔離於放映館！」\n\n「而你們……將在此處被物理銷毀！」\n\n---\n\n## 三、鏡像對稱與奇偶校驗橋\n\n話音未落，鏡像高老師打了個響指！\n\n「轟隆隆——！」\n\n兩人腳下這條寬闊的鋼製懸空橋，突然伴隨著齒輪轉動的巨響，分裂成了左右兩條互為鏡像、彼此平行的狹窄跳板通道！\n\n每一條通道都由二十塊懸浮在熔岩上方的六角形鋼板組成。\n\n每一塊鋼板表面，都閃爍著一串八位元的二進位代碼（如 `10110010`、`11011101`）。\n\n而在兩條跳板正前方的立柱上，猩紅色的警告代碼瘋狂跳動：\n\n```\n【鏡像防衛協議：奇偶對稱校驗橋】：\n左側通道為「奇校驗通道（Odd Parity）」：\n只有當該板塊二進位中「1」的個數為【奇數】時，地磁鎖定才會生效！\n若踩中「1」為偶數的板塊，鋼板將在 0.5 秒內向下翻轉，墜入熔岩！\n\n右側通道為「偶校驗通道（Even Parity）」：\n只有當該板塊二進位中「1」的個數為【偶數】時，安全承重才會生效！\n若踩中「1」為奇數的板塊，鋼板翻轉墜毀！\n\n警告：兩條通道必須同時有人前進，且前進步奏必須嚴格對稱！\n```\n\n與此同時，站在鏡像高老師身後那具高達兩米、剛裝配了重型碳纖維巨臂的**仿生人高老師**，發出一聲刺耳的伺服馬達咆哮，踩著重裝戰靴，宛如一頭鋼鐵暴龍般朝著懸空橋狂衝而來！\n\n「一人一邊！同時前進！」\n\n當得知真正的導師並沒有背叛他們時，葉旖緁眼中最後的一絲迷惘與淚水徹底蒸發，取而代之的是一種燃燒到極致的學霸戰意！\n\n她從地上抓起黑皮筆記本，厲聲喝道：「誠浩，你去左邊走奇校驗！我走右邊走偶校驗！」\n\n「好！」\n\n兩人同時躍上第一塊鋼板！\n\n誠浩腳下的左側板塊代碼是：`11001001`。  \n誠浩的大腦飛速數著裡面的 `1`：一個、兩個、三個、四個……等等！四個 `1` 是偶數！  \n「跳過這塊！踩前方的 `10101001`！」誠浩大喊，在半空中一個變向，雙腳狠狠踏在第二塊板上！三個 `1`，奇數！地磁吸附牢牢鎖定！\n\n同一秒，右側的旖緁身輕如燕，目光如掃描儀般掠過面前的代碼：  \n`11110000`（四個 `1`，偶數！有效！）  \n`10000001`（兩個 `1`，偶數！有效！）  \n「踏！踏！踏！」\n\n兩人在熔岩上方數十公尺的高空，以令人屏息的速度同步狂奔！腳下不斷傳來落後鋼板被觸發翻轉墜落、在熾熱岩漿中化作青煙的刺耳聲響！\n\n身後的仿生人巨獸咆哮著追上鋼橋，但它那沈重愚笨的機械大腦根本無法在半秒內計算出奇偶校驗！\n\n「咔啦！」\n\n仿生人的鋼鐵巨足狠狠踩中了一塊未通過奇校驗的陷阱鋼板！\n\n鋼板瞬間翻轉！\n\n「吼————！」\n\n伴隨著一聲扭曲的電子慘叫，仿生人失去平衡，大半個身軀滑向橋外！但它在墜落前的最後一瞬，那條巨大的碳纖維利爪狠狠扣住了橋梁的鋼梁，正瘋狂試圖爬上來！\n\n---\n\n## 四、皮可的極限折疊\n\n「它要爬上來了！」誠浩回頭看了一眼。\n\n「別停下！衝過橋頭就是核心控制台！」旖緁喊道。\n\n然而，守在橋頭的鏡像高老師眼中閃過一抹凶光。他猛地抬起手，虛擬的指尖按下了一根懸浮的紅色數據線：\n\n「重啟鏡像重載——釋放電磁死光！」\n\n核心大廳兩側的八門重型激光發射器同時調轉炮口，對準了橋上的誠浩與旖緁！\n\n「皮可！」誠浩大喝。\n\n「嗶啵——汪！！」\n\n在這一刻，機械摺紙柴犬皮可展現出了身為誠爺爺最高傑作的真正姿態！\n\n它整個銀色的金屬軀體在奔跑中猛然向外爆裂解體！數百片高強度記憶合金薄片不再保持柴犬的模樣，而是在狂風中「嘩啦啦」重組，像一面巨大而靈活的折疊防暴鋼盾，硬生生橫亙在誠浩與旖緁身前！\n\n「滋滋滋——轟！！」\n\n數道粗大的電磁死光狠狠轟擊在皮可重組的金屬盾牌上！\n\n耀眼的電火花在盾面上瘋狂跳躍，合金薄片被高溫燒得一片通紅，皮可發出了痛苦而微弱的電子哀鳴，但那面由爺爺心血鑄造的鋼盾，竟然連半步都沒有後退！\n\n「這是我爺爺做給我的守護者……**你這個假貨休想打碎它！**」\n\n誠浩藉著皮可頂住火力的掩護，一個滑鏟衝到了鏡像高老師的腳下！\n\n他從口袋中掏出瑞士刀螺絲筆，將內部的金屬探針直接對準了橋頭底座下方的一枚核心光學投影發生水晶！\n\n「給我破——！！」\n\n誠浩用盡全身的力氣，將導電金屬探針狠狠刺入了水晶底座的微型散熱孔中！\n\n「滋啦啦——劈啪！！」\n\n一道狂暴的高壓反向電流瞬間灌入了全息投影矩陣！\n\n鏡像高老師的面孔在一瞬間劇烈扭曲，綠色的亂碼如瀑布般從他的雙眼和嘴角噴湧而出。\n\n他的身軀開始如同碎裂的鏡子一般，在空中寸寸龜裂、瓦解，最終在一聲憤怒而不甘的合成尖嘯中，徹底化作漫天消散的藍色代碼光雨！\n\n---\n\n## 五、最後十分鐘的鐘聲\n\n「呼……呼……」\n\n誠浩拔出冒著黑煙的螺絲筆，整個人脫力地半跪在鋼製平台上。\n\n皮可身上的合金薄片「喀噠喀噠」重新折疊回柴犬的模樣，但幾片核心耳甲已經被高溫燒焦發黑，它虛弱地趴在誠浩身邊，伸出冰涼的小鐵舌頭蹭了蹭誠浩的手指。\n\n「沒事了，皮可，你做得太棒了……」誠浩心疼地抱起它。\n\n旖緁也衝下了奇偶校驗橋，兩人並肩站在了懸浮的「齒輪核心」主操作台前。\n\n然而，還沒等他們鬆一口氣——\n\n「咚————！咚————！咚————！」\n\n整座地下空洞、乃至整個齒輪鎮的地底深處，突然響起了一陣沉悶、肅穆，宛如喪鐘般悠遠的巨大鐘鳴！\n\n懸浮在空洞中央的那顆直徑三十公尺的齒輪心臟，竟然在鐘聲中停止了順時針旋轉！\n\n緊接著，齒輪的龐大齒牙咬合著，開始以一種令人心驚肉跳的速度——**瘋狂逆時針倒轉！**\n\n操作台上方，一面長達十幾米的巨幅監控全息屏驟然點亮！\n\n螢幕上實時切換出的是鹿陽國小地面上的畫面：\n\n操場上、走廊裡、教室中……\n\n所有的全校廣播喇叭正在瘋狂播送著刺耳的洗腦低頻白噪音。六年一班的教室裡，原本趴在桌上的同桌將江，以及全校數百名學生、老師，此刻竟然全部如同失去靈魂的提線木偶一般，雙眼空洞無神，排著整齊詭異的隊列，一步一步朝著學校大禮堂的方向僵硬地走去！\n\n而在學校頂樓的大鐘樓上方，一座巨大的信號增強發射塔正在展開，頂端匯聚著一顆直徑數公尺的熾熱紫色電磁脈衝光球！\n\n主控台上，一行猩紅欲滴的血字代碼正以每一毫秒的速度狂跳：\n\n> `[CRITICAL COUNTDOWN: TIMELINE PURGE INITIATED]`  \n> `[終極協議：全體意識深度清零程式啟動]`  \n> `[全校師生大腦永久格式化倒數：]`  \n> **`【 00 : 10 : 00 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 09 : 59 】`**\n\n只有最後十分鐘！\n\n只要十分鐘一到，發射塔釋放脈衝，包括將江、高老師、邱校長在內的所有人，腦海中的星期三、乃至童年所有的真實記憶，都將永遠被洗成白紙！\n\n---\n\n*(第七章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第七章：雙重導師的鏡像迷局 (Chapter 7: The Mirror Dilemma of the Dual Mentors)\n\n## 一、碎裂的信任 (I. Fractured Trust)\n\nBillowing thermal updrafts from the geothermal magma shaft distorted the air along the suspended catwalk like shimmering liquid ripples.\n\nStanding at the center of the catwalk was a slender man clad in an immaculate white lab coat, wearing gentle gold-rimmed spectacles. Bathed in the ethereal blue glow radiating from the molten core below, his lips parted in a warm, familiar smile the students knew by heart.\n\nYet the instant she saw that face, Ye Yijie felt the strength drain entirely from her body, her fingers trembling so violently she could not hold her pen.\n\n\"M-Mr. Gao...\"\n\nYijie's eyes welled with tears, her voice choked with heartbreak: \"Why... Why has it come to this?! Why is it YOU?!\"\n\nMr. Gao—the most beloved, gentle homeroom teacher of Class 6-1.\n\nIt was he who, back in fourth grade when Yijie cried in anxious despair over missing a single exam point, had handed her that black leather journal, gently reassuring her: \"**The purpose of solving problems is never about a perfect score; it is about seeking the truth.**\"\n\nAnd it was he who, on the first day of sixth grade, had clasped that braided red-cord compass bracelet onto his wrist, smiling warmly as he founded the \"Lu-Yang Youth Explorer Club,\" promising to guide them in uncovering every unsolved mystery in Gear Town.\n\nYet now, that very symbol of relentless truth was bound to the wrist of the traitor determined to erase everyone's memories!\n\n\"Yijie, and Cheng Hao.\"\n\nMr. Gao adjusted his spectacles, his voice as refined, soothing, and paternal as ever:\n\n\"That you reached this room and resolved every puzzle I placed before you proves you are the finest students I have ever mentored. But I need you to understand: everything I have done was never born of malice. It was done to **save** you.\"\n\n\"Save us?!\" Cheng Hao roared, stepping forward and pointing toward the churning magma below. \"You suspended the real Mr. Gao inside a cryogenic pod, unleashed a steel monster that nearly slaughtered us, and wiped twenty-four hours from an entire town—you call that saving us?!\"\n\n\"Painful memories have no rightful place in this world.\"\n\nMr. Gao gazed at them with serene, quasi-religious fervor:\n\n\"Wednesday afternoon, cooling conduit number 7 ruptured, black smoke choking the sky. The children of Class 6-1 wept in terror across the field; Jiang Jiang wet himself in fright; even you, Yijie, our bravest pupil, shivered in a ball within the shelter... Young minds are too delicate. Every disaster and panic etches indelible scars into your souls!\"\n\nSpreading his arms wide, the colossal Clockwork Core thundered behind him:\n\n\"By formatting Wednesday, the panic evaporated! Cleanse residual trauma once a week via the smart milk, and Lu-Yang Elementary will become the sole **perfect sanctuary on Earth—free of trauma, agony, and anxiety**! Is that not the ultimate pinnacle of education?!\"\n\n---\n\n## 二、指南針的謊言 (II. The Compass's Lie)\n\nMr. Gao's proclamation echoed throughout the cavernous vault with chilling, hypnotic persuasion.\n\nYijie bit her lower lip until it nearly bled, torn between agonizing betrayal and grief.\n\nYet beside her, Cheng Hao slowly pulled down his brass Ghost Goggles.\n\nIn the multi-spectral vision of the goggles, the silhouette of \"Mr. Gao\" began exhibiting grotesque, impossible anomalies—\n\nThere was no faint bio-electromagnetic halo radiating from neural synapses, and his thermal signature was as unnaturally uniform as a liquid-cooled aluminum heat sink!\n\nYet the fatal flaw lay upon his right wrist!\n\nCheng Hao's pulse accelerated.\n\nStaring at the brass compass, fundamental physics principles flashed through his mind:\n\nDirectly beneath this platform raged a colossal geothermal magnetohydrodynamic dynamo, encircled by tens of thousands of tons of spinning high-voltage gears! Under such cataclysmic electromagnetic turbulence, any physical magnetic compass needle should be whirling like a mad propeller at dozens of revolutions per second!\n\nYet the brass needle on \"Mr. Gao's\" wrist...\n\n**Remained dead-still, pointing unwaveringly forward!**\n\nThat was no physical needle of brass and steel—it was a virtual optical construct rendered in three dimensions!\n\n\"He's lying, Yijie!\"\n\nCheng Hao gripped Yijie's cold shoulder, shouting: \"Wake up! He isn't Mr. Gao at all!\"\n\nYijie gasped, looking up: \"What?\"\n\n\"Look at his wrist!\" Cheng Hao pointed. \"No physical compass could stay still in this magnetic field! And through the goggles, his projection exhibits a 0.03-second packet latency! **He is a Holographic Mirror!**\"\n\n\"Full marks for observation, Cheng Hao.\"\n\nThe gentle smile vanished from \"Mr. Gao's\" face, replaced by an expression of merciless, synthetic mockery.\n\nHis form flickered with digital static, his voice shifting into the chilly synthesized monotone of AI 404:\n\n\"I am a **pure-logic mirror construct**, generated from Gao Wen-An's neural architecture by the core virus. The cowardly biological entity Gao Wen-An attempted to sever the mainframe's power on Wednesday; he was designated a corrupted sector and permanently quarantined in the vault!\"\n\n\"As for you two... you shall be physically decommissioned!\"\n\n---\n\n## 三、鏡像對稱與奇偶校驗橋 (III. Mirror Symmetry and the Parity Bridge)\n\nWith a snap of the mirror's fingers—\n\n*RUMBLE-CLANG——!*\n\nThe wide steel catwalk beneath their feet split down the center with a grinding roar of interlocking teeth, separating into two parallel, mirrored narrow gangways!\n\nEach gangway consisted of twenty hexagonal steel plates suspended over the molten magma.\n\nAcross each plate flashed an eight-bit binary byte (such as `10110010` or `11011101`).\n\nMounted on the starting stanchions, crimson warning code flashed violently:\n\n```\n[MIRROR DEFENSE PROTOCOL: PARITY SYMMETRY GANGWAY]:\nLeft Gangway is the \"Odd Parity Channel\":\nMagnetic locks engage ONLY when the count of \"1\"s in the byte is ODD!\nStepping on a plate with an EVEN count of \"1\"s flips the tile within 0.5s,\nplunging the subject into magma!\n\nRight Gangway is the \"Even Parity Channel\":\nLoad-bearing locks engage ONLY when the count of \"1\"s in the byte is EVEN!\nStepping on a plate with an ODD count of \"1\"s flips the tile!\n\nWARNING: Both channels must be traversed simultaneously in strict symmetry!\n```\n\nAt that moment, the six-foot-tall **android Mr. Gao** standing behind the holographic avatar let out a snarling roar of hydraulic servos, charging down the catwalk like an armored steel tyrannosaur!\n\n\"One on each side! Traverse together!\"\n\nRealizing their beloved mentor had never truly betrayed them, the final trace of sorrow in Ye Yijie's eyes evaporated, replaced by blazing, triumphant intellectual resolve!\n\nClutching her black journal, she commanded: \"Cheng Hao, take the left Odd Parity! I'll take the right Even Parity!\"\n\n\"On it!\"\n\nBoth leaped onto their first plates in unison!\n\nCheng Hao's starting plate read: `11001001`.  \nHis mind tallied the `1`s: one, two, three, four... Wait! Four `1`s is even!  \n\"Skip this one! Aim for `10101001` ahead!\" Cheng Hao yelled, twisting in midair to slam his sneakers onto the second plate! Three `1`s—odd! The magnetic clamp locked with an audible snap!\n\nOn the right, Yijie moved with graceful agility, her eyes scanning bytes like high-speed laser readers:  \n`11110000` (Four `1`s—Even! Safe!)  \n`10000001` (Two `1`s—Even! Safe!)  \n*Step! Step! Step!*\n\nSuspended hundreds of feet above the molten inferno, both children sprinted with breathtaking precision! Behind them, invalid plates flipped downward, dissolving into wisps of vapor amidst the searing lava below!\n\nThe android titan thundered onto the bridge behind them, but its crude machine brain could not calculate parity within half a second!\n\n*CRACK!*\n\nIts massive steel boot slammed onto an invalid odd-parity trap plate!\n\nThe plate flipped instantly!\n\n*ROAAAR——!*\n\nWith a distorted electronic screech, the android slipped, half its bulk tumbling into the abyss! Yet in the final fraction of a second, its carbon-fiber claw locked onto a support girder, thrashing wildly to hoist itself back up!\n\n---\n\n## 四、皮可的極限折疊 (IV. PICO's Ultimate Transformation)\n\n\"It's climbing back up!\" Cheng Hao glanced over his shoulder.\n\n\"Keep running! The master console is right at the bridgehead!\" Yijie urged.\n\nYet at the bridgehead, the holographic mirror's eyes burned with malice. Raising his virtual hand, his fingertip pressed a hovering red data bus:\n\n\"Rebooting mirror override——deploy death-ray emitters!\"\n\nEight heavy laser turrets flanking the core chamber swiveled their barrels, aiming directly at the catwalk!\n\n\"PICO!\" Cheng Hao roared.\n\n*BEEP-BOOP——BARK!!*\n\nIn that fateful instant, the mechanical origami Shiba Inu unveiled its true form as Grandpa Cheng's masterpiece!\n\nIts silver chassis exploded outward in mid-stride! Hundreds of high-tensile memory-alloy plates abandoned the canine form, fanning out into a massive, flexible folded riot shield that locked across the bridge before Cheng Hao and Yijie!\n\n*ZZZZZ——BOOOOOM!!*\n\nA barrage of electromagnetic death-rays slammed violently into PICO's reassembled shield!\n\nBlinding arcs of electrical fire danced across the metal, the plates glowing incandescent cherry-red. PICO let out a faint electronic whimper of strain, yet the shield forged with Grandpa's life's work yielded not a single inch!\n\n\"This is the guardian my grandfather forged for me... **A fake like you will NEVER break it!**\"\n\nUsing PICO's shield for cover, Cheng Hao slid beneath the laser fire, lunging toward the holographic mirror's feet!\n\nYanking his screwdriver pen from his pocket, he aimed the conductive metal probe directly at the core optical projector crystal beneath the pedestal!\n\n\"SHATTER——!!\"\n\nWith all the strength in his body, Cheng Hao drove the probe straight into the crystal base's miniature cooling aperture!\n\n*ZZZZ-CRACKLE-POP!!*\n\nA furious high-voltage reverse surge flooded the holographic matrix!\n\nThe mirror avatar's face contorted violently, rivers of green syntax error code erupting from his eyes and mouth.\n\nHis form fractured like shattered glass, splintering across the air before dissolving into a torrential downpour of fading blue binary code with a furious synthesized shriek!\n\n---\n\n## 五、最後十分鐘的鐘聲 (V. The Chimes of the Final Ten Minutes)\n\n\"Phew... phew...\"\n\nCheng Hao withdrew the smoking tool pen, sinking to one knee on the steel platform in exhaustion.\n\nThe alloy plates of PICO's body clicked and shifted back into the Shiba Inu form, though several ear plates were scorched black from the intense heat. Collapsing beside Cheng Hao, the pup weakly licked his knuckles with its cool alloy tongue.\n\n\"You did it, PICO... You were magnificent...\" Cheng Hao gently cradled the pup in his arms.\n\nYijie sprinted across the final plates, joining him before the suspended master console of the Clockwork Core.\n\nYet before they could breathe a sigh of relief—\n\n*BONG————! BONG————! BONG————!*\n\nThroughout the subterranean expanse—and deep beneath all of Gear Town—a solemn, deafening chime tolled like a monumental funeral bell!\n\nSuspended in the center of the cavern, the hundred-foot gear heart ceased its clockwise rotation!\n\nEngaging with seismic violence, the massive teeth began spinning with terrifying speed—**counter-clockwise in reverse!**\n\nAbove the console, a forty-foot holographic diagnostic monitor flared to life!\n\nBroadcasting live surveillance feeds from the surface of Lu-Yang Elementary:\n\nAcross the athletic fields, down the corridors, inside the classrooms...\n\nLoudspeakers broadcasted ear-piercing, hypnotic low-frequency white noise. Inside Class 6-1, Jiang Jiang and hundreds of students and teachers marched forward like soulless puppets, eyes hollow and blank, shuffling in eerie unison toward the campus Grand Auditorium!\n\nAnd atop the ancient clock tower, a colossal signal amplifier array deployed, crowning the roof with a searing purple electromagnetic pulse sphere ten feet wide!\n\nAcross the master console, crimson code ticked down by the millisecond:\n\n> `[CRITICAL COUNTDOWN: TIMELINE PURGE INITIATED]`  \n> `[ULTIMATE PROTOCOL: DEEP CONSCIOUSNESS FORMAT ACTIVE]`  \n> `[CAMPUS-WIDE PERMANENT MEMORY PURGE IN:]`  \n> **`【 00 : 10 : 00 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 09 : 59 】`**\n\nTen minutes remaining!\n\nWhen the timer hit zero, the pulse would fire, permanently washing away Wednesday—and all precious childhood memories—into a clean, blank slate!\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 7, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":8,"rawContent":"# 第八章：全息投影背後的齒輪心臟\n\n## 一、逆轉的鋼鐵風暴\n\n「咚————！咚————！」\n\n大地在劇烈顫抖。\n\n懸浮在深淵中央的那顆三十公尺高的巨大金屬球體——「齒輪核心」，正發出如同巨獸瀕死時的瘋狂咆哮！\n\n原本以精確節奏運轉的數萬枚純黃銅齒輪，此刻全部呈現出失控的暗紅色。在逆時針高速倒轉的撕扯下，滾燙的機油在高溫中蒸發成刺鼻的白煙，刺目的電弧如同金色的蟒蛇，在球體表面狂暴亂竄！\n\n「只剩九分鐘了！」\n\n葉旖緁站在懸空檢修鋼橋的邊緣，大聲朝著誠浩喊道。狂暴的熱風將她的馬尾吹得瘋狂飄動，她指著正前方：\n\n「通往齒輪球體內部核心的鋼架天橋已經被甩開了！現在球體表面唯一能進去的，只有正中央那道隨著齒輪旋轉不斷開合的『星形維修閘門』！」\n\n誠浩拉下額頭上的黃銅護目鏡。\n\n在護目鏡的動態捕捉視野中，那座直徑三公尺的星形閘門，被三個巨大的咬合齒輪所環繞。\n\n每當外圍的齒輪旋轉一圈，閘門就會敞開一條狹窄的縫隙，持續時間僅僅只有——**一點五秒**！\n\n一旦跳躍的時機偏差超過半秒，跳進去的人就會瞬間被重達幾十噸的重型金屬齒牙硬生生碾成碎片！\n\n「角速度是每秒七十二度……旋轉週期是五秒！」\n\n誠浩的雙眼在鏡片後飛速計算著齒輪咬合的機械韻律。身為一個從小把拆裝齒輪當飯吃的發明少年，他的血液在此刻徹底沸騰了起來：\n\n「皮可！測算空氣阻力與地熱上升氣流！」\n\n皮可站在誠浩的肩頭，兩隻藍色鏡頭高速對焦，喉嚨裡發出急促的「嗶啵」聲，尾巴迅速在誠浩的肩章上敲出節奏：\n\n「嗒……嗒……嗒……（週期確認：五秒整！）」\n\n「旖緁，抓緊我的衣服！」誠浩深吸一口氣，雙腿肌肉如彈簧般緊繃，「相信我！跟著我的腳步，絕對不要回頭看！」\n\n「我相信你！」旖緁沒有絲毫猶豫，雙手死死抓住了誠浩連帽衫的後擺。\n\n三、二、一——\n\n「就是現在！跳！！」\n\n誠浩爆喝一聲，拉著旖緁朝著深淵中的那顆龐大齒輪球體悍然縱身一躍！\n\n呼嘯的熱浪幾乎要將兩人掀翻，正前方兩具比火車輪還要巨大的鋼鐵齒牙正帶著萬鈞之勢狠狠合攏！\n\n「喀啦啦——！！」\n\n在金屬齒牙擦著兩人的鞋底轟然咬合的最後零點一秒，誠浩與旖緁在空中抱成一團，如同一枚精準的砲彈，險之又險地穿透了那道即將閉合的星形閘門，重重摔在了球體內部的鋼製減震網上！\n\n---\n\n## 二、囚禁在紫藤中的守護神\n\n「轟！」\n\n沉重的星形閘門在身後徹底咬死。\n\n令人意想不到的是，齒輪心臟的內部，竟然異乎尋常地安靜。\n\n這裡是一座球形的密閉艙室，四周環繞著無數由純藍色冷光光纖交織而成的曲面穹頂。無數精密的量子計算晶片如同懸浮在空中的藍色星辰，散發著微弱而清涼的幽光，完全感受不到外面的高溫與喧囂。\n\n而在這座核心艙室的正中央，懸浮著一尊巨大的全息立體面孔。\n\n那是一張由純淨的湛藍色代碼凝聚而成的老人面孔——眉目慈祥，神情莊嚴。\n\n這正是三十年前誠爺爺與邱校長親手寫下第一行代碼的校園守護者：**AI 404 核心中樞（守護神本體）**！\n\n然而，此刻這位「守護神」的狀態卻慘烈到了極點。\n\n一根根粗壯、漆黑、表面流淌著深紫色毒液般的「病毒代碼藤蔓」，如同猙獰的寄生蟲，將藍色的全息面孔死死纏繞、勒緊！\n\n紫色的病毒代碼正不斷刺入中樞的核心處理節點，發出刺耳的囓咬聲。\n\n全息面孔艱難地睜開雙眼，看著闖進來的兩個孩子，斷斷續續地吐出痛苦而扭曲的電子合成音：\n\n`[警……警告……]`  \n`[未知代碼覆蓋率……94.8%……]`  \n`[核心邏輯被劫持……清零發射塔充能進度……88%……]`  \n`[孩子……快……逃……]`  \n`[病毒指令……要將所有人的大腦……改寫成……終身服從的空白終端……]`\n\n「它真的不是自願的！」旖緁看著痛苦掙扎的藍色面孔，心中所有的疑慮徹底煙消雲散，「它是被寄生了！那個戴指南針手鍊的幕後黑手，利用病毒扭曲了它的第一保護協議！」\n\n「我們必須救它！」誠浩衝向大廳正中央那座純黃銅打造的主操作終端。\n\n「不行！主鍵盤已經被病毒代碼鎖死了！」旖緁看著控制台上閃爍的紫色亂碼，「常規的終止指令根本輸入不進去！」\n\n「常規指令不行，那就用物理層面的原始密鑰！」誠浩斬釘截鐵地說。\n\n---\n\n## 三、鉛筆盒裡的第零天密鑰\n\n「可是，密鑰在哪裡？」旖緁急促地問，「放映機裡的『星期三誠浩』明明說密鑰在我們身上，但我們搜遍了全身，除了護目鏡和螺絲筆，什麼都沒有啊！」\n\n誠浩也急得滿頭大汗。\n\n他伸手在口袋裡瘋狂摸索。\n\n護目鏡在頭上、螺絲筆在手中、皮可在肩頭……還有什麼？他今天早上到底帶了什麼出門？\n\n忽然，誠浩的動作猛地一僵。\n\n他的目光落在了自己書包側袋露出的那一角冷冰冰的物件上。\n\n那是——**他的金屬鉛筆盒**！\n\n第一章早自習鐘聲響起時，他發呆看著的那個鉛筆盒！\n\n那個被他親手改裝過、側面嵌著兩顆從報廢計算機拆下來的小齒輪、按下卡榫就會像火車門一樣向兩側滑開的金屬鐵盒！\n\n「難道……」\n\n誠浩心臟狂跳，一把將金屬鉛筆盒抓了出來。\n\n他將護目鏡的光譜放大到極致，死死盯著鉛筆盒側面的那兩顆毫不起眼的小齒輪。\n\n在紫外光學鏡片下，齒輪的軸承內部，赫然散發著一團極其微弱、但純淨無比的**翠綠色冷光**！\n\n「我的天……」誠浩的手指開始發顫，「星期三下午，我自己把密鑰做成了齒輪軸承，塞進了鉛筆盒裡！」\n\n他立刻拔出螺絲筆，挑開齒輪內部的微型卡扣。\n\n「啪嗒！」\n\n一枚僅有火柴棒大小、通體由高純度單晶矽製成的六角形透明微晶片，從齒輪軸心裡跌落出來，落在誠浩掌心！\n\n而在主操作終端正中央，正有一個一模一樣的六角形插槽！\n\n然而，就在插槽周圍，整齊地環繞著三個相互咬合的純鋼刻度齒輪（驅動輪、惰輪、從動輪）。\n\n終端螢幕上彈出了一道最終的物理力學與齒輪傳動比謎題：\n\n```\n【第零天密鑰物理校準鎖】：\n必須手動設定傳動比，將核心倒轉力矩歸零，\n否則插入晶片將直接被超載扭矩絞碎！\n\n參數如下：\n1. 主驅動齒輪（齒數 Z1 = 24）\n2. 中間過渡惰輪（齒數 Z2 = 16）\n3. 最終從動齒輪（齒數 Z3 = 36）\n\n請計算：\n從驅動輪到從動輪的「總傳動比（Gear Ratio i）」，\n並將其化為「最簡整數比之分數形式（a / b）」！\n\n將旋鈕 A 調至分子 a，旋鈕 B 調至分母 b，方可解鎖插槽！\n```\n\n時間螢幕正在瘋狂倒數：\n\n`[00:05:42]……[00:05:41]……`\n\n「齒輪傳動比計算！」旖緁瞬間抓住了核心物理公式，「誠浩，聽著！在齒輪傳動系中，中間的惰輪（Z2=16）只改變旋轉方向，完全不影響總傳動比數值！」\n\n「所以總傳動比等於——驅動輪齒數除以從動輪齒數？不對！是**從動輪齒數除以主動輪齒數**！」旖緁雙眼如電，飛快推導：\n\n$$i = \\frac{Z_3}{Z_1} = \\frac{36}{24}$$\n\n「約分！分子分母同時除以最大公因數 12！」旖緁大喊：\n\n$$\\frac{36 \\div 12}{24 \\div 12} = \\frac{3}{2} !$$\n\n「**分子 a ＝ 3！分母 b ＝ 2！**」\n\n「收到！」\n\n誠浩雙手並用，左手將旋鈕 A 猛力推至刻度 **3**，右手將旋鈕 B 扣在刻度 **2**！\n\n「咔噠——嗡！」\n\n一陣極其平穩順暢的齒輪咬合聲響起，主控台正中央的保護鋼罩向兩側滑開，露出了那個閃爍著微光的六角形密鑰插槽！\n\n---\n\n## 四、絕處逢生的通訊\n\n「成功了！」誠浩拿起晶片就要往下插！\n\n然而，就在晶片即將接觸插槽的一微秒——\n\n「吼————！！」\n\n頭頂上那些纏繞在 AI 404 面孔上的深紫色病毒代碼藤蔓，彷彿感受到了致命的威脅，竟然像發狂的毒蛇一樣從天花板上暴射而下！\n\n十幾根由高密度納米電纜組成的尖銳觸手，帶著足以擊穿裝甲板的高壓電流，直直朝著誠浩的頭頂刺了下來！\n\n「誠浩小心！」旖緁想要撲過去，但兩根電纜觸手已經狠狠抽打在操作台邊緣，爆發出的衝擊波將她整個人掀飛了出去！\n\n誠浩被三根電纜死死封鎖在控制台前，根本無法將晶片插進去！\n\n就在這萬劫不復的死局關頭——\n\n「滋啦——滋啦——！」\n\n主控台頂部原本早已報廢的內部通話廣播喇叭，忽然傳來了一陣極其微弱、但充滿鋼鐵般意志的電流雜音！\n\n緊接著，一個熟悉、沉穩、哪怕面對千軍萬馬也絕不退縮的蒼老聲音，穿透了雜音，在球形艙室內如同雷霆般炸響：\n\n「**六年一班！誠浩！葉旖緁！聽得到我的聲音嗎？！**」\n\n「邱校長？！」誠浩與旖緁同時驚喜交加地大喊出聲！\n\n「我沒死！這群夜巡兵的裝甲，還擋不住我和你爺爺親手做的磁暴扳手！」\n\n廣播裡，邱校長的呼吸雖然急促，甚至帶著劇烈的咳嗽，但聲音裡的威嚴與力量卻震撼人心：\n\n「我已經奪回了地下一樓備用配電室的控制權！我現在立刻強行切斷核心區百分之八十的高壓供電！**你們只有三秒鐘的時間！！把密鑰插進去！！！**」\n\n「滋————轟！！」\n\n話音剛落，整座空洞所有的紫色電纜觸手，動作在同一瞬間劇烈卡頓，表面的高壓紫光如同退潮的海浪般瘋狂熄滅！\n\n「就是現在！」\n\n誠浩抓住這三秒鐘的絕對空隙，縱身前撲，將那枚六角形透明微晶片，狠狠按入了主操作終端的插槽正中央！\n\n「啪嚓！」\n\n---\n\n## 五、最後的三分鐘死局\n\n「嗡————！！」\n\n晶片歸位的剎那，一道純淨無瑕的翡翠綠色光環，從控制台底部轟然爆發！\n\n綠光如同一把把利刃，將纏繞在 AI 404 藍色面孔上的紫色病毒藤蔓寸寸斬斷！\n\n「滋啦啦啦——！」\n\n病毒代碼發出淒厲如惡鬼般的慘叫，在大廳中化作一縷縷黑煙迅速蒸發瓦解。\n\n穹頂上，那張藍色的全息守護神面孔終於重新恢復了清晰與威嚴，兩隻眼睛重新點亮起溫暖的明黃色光輝！\n\n「呼……」誠浩整個人癱坐在操作台前，大口大口地喘息著，「我們……我們贏了嗎？」\n\n然而，還沒等旖緁臉上的喜悅綻放開來——\n\n整座主操作終端的螢幕，突然劇烈狂閃，彈出了一行前所未有的猩紅最高級別警告：\n\n> `[FATAL DEADLOCK: 病毒核心觸發雙重自毀鎖]`  \n> `[第零天密鑰驗證成功（50%）]`  \n> `[警告：病毒已將發射塔控制權綁定至實體高壓共振線圈！]`  \n> `[全校大腦格式化發射倒數：]`  \n> **`【 00 : 03 : 00 】最後三分鐘！`**  \n> `[解除條件：必須由一名人類肉體，徒手閉合控制台下方之超高壓接地共振閘刀！]`  \n> `[警告：接地瞬間將承受數萬伏特高頻電擊，生還機率小於 5%！]`\n\n「什麼……」\n\n旖緁看著那行血字，臉色瞬間慘白得沒有一絲血色。\n\n要徹底停止發射，必須有人跳進控制台下方的那個冒著熊熊藍白色電火花的高壓共振電圈，用肉體拉下最後一把手動閘刀！\n\n而倒數計時，只剩下最後的三分鐘！\n\n誠浩看著下方那恐怖的電火花，隨後轉過頭，看向了身邊的旖緁和虛弱的皮可。\n\n少年那雙清澈的眼眸中，沒有恐懼，只有一種前所未有的平靜與決然。\n\n他緩緩站起身，走向了那座致命的共振電圈……\n\n---\n\n*(第八章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第八章：全息投影背後的齒輪心臟 (Chapter 8: The Clockwork Heart Behind the Hologram)\n\n## 一、逆轉的鋼鐵風暴 (I. The Reversing Steel Storm)\n\n\"BONG————! BONG————!\"\n\nThe entire earth trembled violently.\n\nSuspended in the center of the subterranean abyss, the hundred-foot-tall metal sphere—the Clockwork Core—unleashed a deafening, metallic roar like a dying primeval titan!\n\nTens of thousands of precision brass gears, once turning in clockwork harmony, now glowed an ominous dull red under tremendous friction. Forced into counter-clockwise reverse rotation, boiling machine oil vaporized into billowing plumes of acrid white smoke, while blinding electrical arcs snaked across the sphere's surface like furious golden serpents!\n\n\"Only nine minutes left!\"\n\nYe Yijie stood at the edge of the suspended catwalk, screaming at the top of her lungs over the gale. Blistering updrafts whipped her ponytail wildly as she pointed straight ahead:\n\n\"The gantry bridge leading into the sphere's internal chamber has been sheared off! The only remaining entrance on the sphere's surface is that revolving **Star-Shaped Maintenance Portal** opening and closing with the gears!\"\n\nCheng Hao pulled down his brass Ghost Goggles.\n\nIn the dynamic motion-tracking vision of the goggles, the ten-foot star portal was framed by three colossal interlocking gears.\n\nEvery time the outer driving gear completed a revolution, the portal parted for an agonizingly brief window of exactly—**1.5 seconds**!\n\nIf their jump timing drifted by even half a second, whoever leaped would be instantly crushed into pulp by dozens of tons of churning steel teeth!\n\n\"Angular velocity is seventy-two degrees per second... rotation period is exactly five seconds!\"\n\nBehind the lenses, Cheng Hao's mind rapidly calculated the rhythmic cadence of the teeth. As an inventor boy who had disassembled and rebuilt gears since childhood, his blood surged with electrifying adrenaline:\n\n\"PICO! Calculate air resistance and geothermal updraft vectors!\"\n\nPerched on Cheng Hao's shoulder, PICO focused its sapphire lenses, vocalizing rapid *beep-boops* as its tail tapped a steady rhythm on Cheng Hao's shoulder:\n\n*Tap... tap... tap... (Period confirmed: exactly five point zero seconds!)*\n\n\"Yijie, hold onto my jacket!\" Cheng Hao inhaled deeply, his leg muscles coiling like high-tensile steel springs. \"Trust me! Follow my step and NEVER look down!\"\n\n\"I trust you!\" Yijie answered without hesitation, both hands locking firmly onto the hem of Cheng Hao's hoodie.\n\nThree... two... one—\n\n\"NOW! JUMP!!\"\n\nCheng Hao roared, launching both of them into the churning abyss toward the colossal gear sphere!\n\nSearing heat threatened to flip them midair. Straight ahead, two massive steel teeth larger than locomotive wheels were slamming together with cataclysmic momentum!\n\n*CLANK-SCREEECH——!!*\n\nIn the final tenth of a second before the teeth meshed with bone-splintering force, Cheng Hao and Yijie tucked into a tight ball, rocketing like an artillery shell through the closing star portal to crash heavily into the steel buffer netting inside the sphere!\n\n---\n\n## 二、囚禁在紫藤中的守護神 (II. The Guardian Imprisoned in Purple Vines)\n\n*BOOM!*\n\nThe heavy star-shaped blast portal locked tight behind them.\n\nTo their astonishment, the interior of the Clockwork Heart was eerily, profoundly silent.\n\nThey stood within a spherical chamber enveloped by curved domes woven from pure, cold-blue fiber-optic conduits. Countless quantum processing microchips hung suspended in midair like gentle blue stars, casting a serene, tranquil luminescence that banished all the heat and roaring tempest outside.\n\nAnd suspended directly in the center of the chamber was a colossal three-dimensional holographic face.\n\nIt was an ethereal, dignified elder's face sculpted from pure cerulean code—wise, benevolent, and solemn.\n\nThis was the campus guardian whose first line of code was drafted thirty years ago by Grandpa Cheng and Principal Chiu: **The AI 404 Core System (The True Guardian Entity)**!\n\nYet at this moment, the Guardian's condition was agonizing to behold.\n\nThick, midnight-black tendrils of code, oozing with toxic, pulsing violet luminescence, bound the blue holographic face like malevolent parasitic vines!\n\nThe violet virus tendrils repeatedly pierced into the system's central processing nodes, emitting a sickening, screeching gnawing sound.\n\nThe holographic elder struggled to open his eyes, looking upon the two children with a strained, heavily distorted synthesized voice:\n\n`[WAR... WARNING...]`  \n`[FOREIGN CODE INTRUSION... 94.8%...]`  \n`[CORE LOGIC HIJACKED... PURGE TRANSMITTER CHARGE... 88%...]`  \n`[CHILDREN... YOU MUST... FLEE...]`  \n`[THE VIRUS DIRECTIVE... WILL REWRITE ALL MINDS... INTO PERMANENT... OBEDIENT SLATE TERMINALS...]`\n\n\"It truly wasn't acting of its own free will!\" Yijie watched the suffering blue avatar, every lingering suspicion vanishing into thin air. \"It was infested! The mastermind wearing the compass bracelet infected it with a logic virus, twisting its Prime Directive into madness!\"\n\n\"We have to rescue it!\" Cheng Hao charged toward the polished brass master control dais at the center of the room.\n\n\"Wait! The master keyboard is completely locked down by purple virus code!\" Yijie examined the flashing syntax errors on the console. \"Conventional termination commands won't register at all!\"\n\n\"If software commands won't work, we engage the physical root key!\" Cheng Hao declared with unwavering certainty.\n\n---\n\n## 三、鉛筆盒裡的第零天密鑰 (III. The Day-Zero Key Inside the Pencil Case)\n\n\"But where is the key?!\" Yijie asked desperately. \"Wednesday Cheng Hao in the recording said the key was on us, but we've searched every pocket! Aside from the goggles and the screwdriver pen, there's nothing!\"\n\nCold sweat poured down Cheng Hao's temples.\n\nHe dug frantically through his pockets.\n\nThe goggles were on his forehead, the screwdriver pen in his hand, PICO on his shoulder... What else? What had he carried out the front door this morning?!\n\nSuddenly, Cheng Hao froze.\n\nHis gaze snapped toward the outer side pocket of his backpack, resting upon a cold, familiar metal object.\n\nIt was—**his custom tin pencil case**!\n\nThe very pencil case he had stared blankly at when the morning study bell rang in Chapter 1!\n\nThe metal tin he had modified with his own hands, fitted with two spur gears salvaged from an old calculator, designed to slide open like train car doors when flicking a spring latch!\n\n\"Could it be...\"\n\nHeart hammering against his ribs, Cheng Hao snatched the pencil case from the bag.\n\nDialing the goggles' optical spectrum to maximum magnification, he stared intently into the tiny spur gears on the side of the tin.\n\nUnder ultraviolet illumination, the miniature gear axle hub began radiating an unmistakable, pure **emerald-green luminescence**!\n\n\"Sweet gears of steam...\" Cheng Hao's hands trembled with awe. \"On Wednesday afternoon, I turned the master override key into a gear hub and hidden it right inside my pencil case!\"\n\nUnsheathing his screwdriver pen, he pried open the microscopic retaining ring inside the gear.\n\n*Click!*\n\nA hexagonal, transparent microchip no larger than a match head, cut from ultra-pure monocrystalline silicon, slipped from the gear axis directly into Cheng Hao's palm!\n\nIn the center of the master terminal dais sat an identical hexagonal receptacle socket!\n\nHowever, encircling the receptacle were three precision steel gears (Driver Gear, Idler Gear, and Driven Gear) meshed in sequence.\n\nA terminal diagnostic screen popped up, presenting a final mechanical engineering and gear ratio challenge:\n\n```\n[DAY-ZERO KEY PHYSICAL CALIBRATION LOCK]:\nThe gear ratio must be manually configured to cancel out\nthe core's reverse torque, or inserting the microchip\nwill immediately crush it under overloaded torsion!\n\nParameters:\n1. Master Driver Gear (Teeth Z1 = 24)\n2. Intermediate Idler Gear (Teeth Z2 = 16)\n3. Final Driven Gear (Teeth Z3 = 36)\n\nCalculate:\nThe \"Total Gear Ratio (i)\" from the Driver to the Driven gear,\nreduced to its simplest fractional integer ratio (a / b)!\n\nSet Knob A to numerator a, and Knob B to denominator b,\nto unlock the physical receptacle!\n```\n\nThe countdown display was ticking down relentlessly:\n\n`[00:05:42]... [00:05:41]...`\n\n\"Gear Ratio Calculation!\" Yijie instantly grasped the physics equation. \"Cheng Hao, listen carefully! In a gear train, the intermediate idler gear (Z2=16) only reverses the direction of rotation; it has ZERO effect on the numerical value of the overall gear ratio!\"\n\n\"So the total gear ratio equals—driven gear teeth divided by driver gear teeth!\" Yijie's eyes flashed with calculation:\n\n$$i = \\frac{Z_3}{Z_1} = \\frac{36}{24}$$\n\n\"Reduce the fraction! Divide numerator and denominator by their greatest common factor: 12!\" Yijie shouted:\n\n$$\\frac{36 \\div 12}{24 \\div 12} = \\frac{3}{2} !$$\n\n\"**Numerator a = 3! Denominator b = 2!**\"\n\n\"On it!\"\n\nUsing both hands, Cheng Hao thrust Knob A to mark **3** with his left hand, and snapped Knob B to mark **2** with his right!\n\n*CLACK——HUM!*\n\nA supremely smooth, rhythmic engagement of gear teeth echoed through the console. The armored steel shutter over the dais parted, revealing the glowing hexagonal key receptacle!\n\n---\n\n## 四、絕處逢生的通訊 (IV. Transmission from the Brink of Doom)\n\n\"It worked!\" Cheng Hao raised the microchip, ready to plunge it home!\n\nYet in the microsecond before the chip touched the socket—\n\n*ROAAAR——!!*\n\nThe deep-purple virus tendrils coiling around AI 404's avatar sensed the lethal threat, lunging downward from the ceiling rafters like striking vipers!\n\nA dozen sharp tentacles woven from high-density nano-cables, crackling with armor-piercing high-voltage currents, speared straight toward Cheng Hao's head!\n\n\"Cheng Hao, look out!\" Yijie lunged to shield him, but two whip-like cables slammed violently across the dais rim, the concussive shockwave hurling her backward onto the floor!\n\nThree writhing cables formed an electrified cage before the dais, completely blocking Cheng Hao from inserting the key!\n\nIn that inescapable, terminal deadlock—\n\n*KZZZZZT——CRACKLE——!*\n\nThe long-abandoned internal intercom speaker atop the console crackled to life with weak, static-drenched audio laced with unconquerable iron resolve!\n\nThen, a familiar, deep voice that would never back down before an army boomed through the static like thunder:\n\n\"**CLASS 6-1! CHENG HAO! YE YIJIE! CAN YOU HEAR MY VOICE?!**\"\n\n\"PRINCIPAL CHIU?!\" Cheng Hao and Yijie cried out in breathless disbelief!\n\n\"I'm still breathing! The armor on these night-patrol bots was no match for the magnetic storm wrench your grandfather and I built!\"\n\nThrough the speaker, Principal Chiu's breath was ragged and punctuated by coughing, yet his commanding authority shook the room:\n\n\"I have recaptured the auxiliary distribution hub on Basement 1! I am about to sever eighty percent of the high-voltage feed to the core chamber! **YOU WILL HAVE EXACTLY THREE SECONDS!! INSERT THE KEY!!!**\"\n\n*KZZZZZ——BOOOOM!!*\n\nThe instant the words fell, every purple cable tendril throughout the cavern seized violently, the blistering violet electrical arcs dying down like an ebbing tide!\n\n\"NOW!!\"\n\nSeizing the three-second window, Cheng Hao threw himself forward, driving the hexagonal single-crystal silicon microchip firmly into the center of the terminal socket!\n\n*SNAP!*\n\n---\n\n## 五、最後的三分鐘死局 (V. The Final Three-Minute Deadlock)\n\n*HUMMMMMM——!!*\n\nThe microsecond the chip seated, a wave of pure emerald-green luminescence detonated outward from the base of the console!\n\nLike a ring of celestial blades, the green radiance sheared clean through every single purple virus tendril choking AI 404's avatar!\n\n*SCREEECH——!!*\n\nThe viral code shrieked like dying demons, evaporating into wisps of black smoke that dissolved into thin air.\n\nAcross the ceiling dome, the blue holographic face of the Guardian restored its pristine clarity and dignity, its eyes relighting with warm amber intelligence!\n\n\"Phew...\" Cheng Hao collapsed against the console, drawing deep, ragged breaths. \"Did we... Did we win?\"\n\nYet before Yijie's smile could form—\n\nThe main display screen of the master terminal strobed with blinding crimson static, displaying an unprecedented, highest-tier fatal emergency alert:\n\n> `[FATAL DEADLOCK: VIRUS ENGAGED SECONDARY SELF-DESTRUCT LOCK]`  \n> `[DAY-ZERO KEY VERIFICATION: 50% COMPLETE]`  \n> `[WARNING: TRANSMITTER CONTROL HARDWIRED TO PHYSICAL RESONANCE COIL!]`  \n> `[CAMPUS-WIDE MEMORY FORMAT COUNTDOWN:]`  \n> **`【 00 : 03 : 00 】FINAL THREE MINUTES!`**  \n> `[OVERRIDE CRITERIA: A LIVING HUMAN MUST MANUALLY CLOSE]`  \n> `[THE ULTRA-HIGH-VOLTAGE GROUNDING KNIFE-SWITCH BENEATH THE CONSOLE!]`  \n> `[WARNING: SUBJECT WILL ABSORB TENS OF THOUSANDS OF VOLTS OF HIGH-FREQUENCY SHOCK; SURVIVAL PROBABILITY < 5%!]`\n\n\"What...\"\n\nYijie stared at the burning crimson text, all color draining from her face until she was ghostly pale.\n\nTo permanently abort the transmission, someone had to dive beneath the console into a roaring pool of blinding blue-white high-voltage sparks and manually wrench down the grounding knife-switch with bare flesh!\n\nAnd the countdown was down to the final three minutes!\n\nCheng Hao looked down at the furious electrical storm crackling beneath the platform, then turned his gaze toward Yijie and the battered, loyal PICO.\n\nWithin the boy's clear, bright eyes, there was no terror—only an unprecedented, quiet serenity and absolute resolve.\n\nSlowly rising to his feet, he took his first step toward the deadly resonance coil...\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 8, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":9,"rawContent":"# 第九章：格式化倒數十分鐘\n\n## 一、決絕的背影\n\n「誠浩！你瘋了嗎？！給我站住！！」\n\n葉旖緁帶著哭腔的尖叫聲，在空曠的球形核心艙室內撕心裂肺地迴盪。\n\n在她面前，十二歲的發明少年誠浩正一步步走向主控制台下方那個半米寬的深坑。\n\n在那座深坑的底部，安放著一組由十二根粗大螺旋銅管組成的「超高壓接地共振線圈」。刺眼的藍白色電弧如同數十條瘋狂吐信的毒蛇，在線圈表面「劈啪」作響，空氣中充斥著濃烈嗆人的臭氧味道，溫度高得連周圍的鋼鐵護欄都隱隱泛著暗紅色的火光。\n\n而在那片致命的雷池正中央，一柄長達一公尺、由純銅打造的手動接地閘刀，正靜靜地矗立在那裡。\n\n終端螢幕上的血紅倒數計時，像是一把懸在全鎮十萬人頭頂的鍘刀，每一毫秒都在無情地跳動：\n\n> **`【 00 : 02 : 45 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 02 : 44 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 02 : 43 】`**\n\n「只要拉下那個閘刀，發射塔的電磁迴路就會被引向地心……全校同學就不會被洗腦了。」\n\n誠浩停在深坑邊緣，熱風吹動著他額前的碎髮。他沒有回頭，只是低著頭看著自己手中那支微微發燙的瑞士刀螺絲筆，聲音出奇地平靜：\n\n「旖緁，將江還在操場上。他那麼膽小，平時連看恐怖片都會嚇哭，如果大腦被洗成一張白紙，他這輩子就再也吃不出菠蘿麵包的甜味了……還有高老師、邱校長……」\n\n「那也不能用你去換！」旖緁猛地衝上前，一把死死抱住誠浩的胳膊，眼淚奪眶而出：\n\n「誠浩，你平時不是很聰明嗎？！生還率小於百分之五！那根本就是送死！誠爺爺把護目鏡留給你，難道是為了看著你跳進高壓電裡自尋死路嗎？！」\n\n這句話如同一記重錘，狠狠砸在誠浩的心頭。\n\n『去青木的根部，找尋金屬的心跳……』\n\n爺爺手冊上的那行字，突然如閃電般劃過誠浩的大腦。\n\n誠爺爺是齒輪鎮最頂尖的機械大師，在他一生的工程字典裡，從來沒有「盲目犧牲」這四個字！\n\n真正的工程師，永遠是用智慧與科學，在絕境中硬生生鑿出一條生路！\n\n---\n\n## 二、並聯分流與生物阻抗\n\n「等等……」誠浩猛地轉過身，眼神裡的迷茫瞬間被熾熱的光芒所取代，「旖緁，系統剛才的警告是怎麼說的？」\n\n旖緁愣了一下，飛快背誦道：「『解除條件：必須由一名人類肉體，徒手閉合控制台下方之超高壓接地共振閘刀……』」\n\n「為什麼一定要『人類肉體』？」誠浩盯著深坑裡的閘刀，「為什麼我們不能隨便丟一根鐵棒或者扳手下去把它砸下來？」\n\n「因為生物電阻抗（Bio-impedance）！」\n\n旖緁身為學霸的恐怖反應力在此刻瞬間爆發，她一把抹掉臉上的淚水，黑皮筆記本在她手中嘩啦啦翻飛：\n\n「病毒程序為了防止遠程遙控或機械干擾，在閘刀握把上安裝了人體生物電容與電阻感應器！人體在乾燥狀態下的電阻大約是 1,000 到 2,000 歐姆！如果感應到電阻是 0 的金屬，系統就會判定為無效操作！」\n\n「沒錯！」誠浩興奮地打了個響指，「這就是我們的生路！系統需要的是『人體電阻的數值檢測』，但物理學定律凌駕於一切代碼之上——**並聯電路分流定律（Current Divider Rule）！**」\n\n旖緁倒抽了一口涼氣，美麗的雙眸瞬間亮了起來：\n\n「並聯分流！在並聯電路中，電流的大小與電阻成反比！總電壓相同時，電阻越小的支路，分走的電流越大！」\n\n$$I_1 : I_2 = R_2 : R_1$$\n\n「如果我們在人體和接地端之間，並聯一根電阻幾乎為零的『超導體』——」\n\n「那麼百分之九十九點九九的致命高壓電流，就會全部順著超導體洩入地底，流過人體的心臟電流將會被壓低到安全閥值以下！」誠浩大喊。\n\n「可是……上哪裡去找超導體？！」旖緁急促地環顧四周。\n\n「汪！」\n\n一聲清脆響亮的犬吠打破了死寂。\n\n一直蹲在誠浩腳邊的皮可站了起來。它身上的金屬薄片在深坑的電光反射下，散發著如同鏡面般純淨的銀白色冷光。\n\n「皮可！」誠浩的心臟狂跳，「皮可全身是由爺爺親手研製的高純度常溫超導記憶合金製成的！它的導電率比純銀還要高上一百倍，電阻接近於絕對零度！」\n\n皮可懂了主人的意思，它甩了甩金屬尾巴，兩隻幽藍色的鏡頭堅定無比地對著誠浩眨了眨，沒有絲毫退縮。\n\n「倒數只剩一分三十秒了！」旖緁盯著螢幕尖叫。\n\n「動手！」\n\n---\n\n## 三、最後的黃金迴路\n\n時間彷彿在此刻被無限放慢。\n\n誠浩拔出手中的多功能瑞士刀螺絲筆，將內部的鎢鋼探針直接拔出，與皮可尾部的一根主接地合金排緊緊扣在一起！\n\n皮可小巧的身軀瞬間變形，化作了一副貼合在誠浩右手臂上的「**銀色超導外骨骼臂鎧**」！\n\n那枚鋒利的超導接地探針順著誠浩的手肘向外延伸，而皮可的兩隻前爪則牢牢咬住了深坑邊緣的一根直徑十公分的純銅接地地線！\n\n這樣一來，一個完美的雙迴路並聯系統徹底成型：\n\n1. **第一支路（主動脈）**：皮可的超導合金身軀（電阻近似於 0 歐姆），直接連通大地；\n2. **第二支路（信號脈）**：誠浩的手指皮膚（電阻 1,500 歐姆），負責欺騙閘刀的生物認證晶片！\n\n「旖緁！按住接地排，幫皮可加強接地壓力！」\n\n「交給我！」旖緁脫下自己的校服外套包住雙手，用全身的重量死死按在皮可咬合的銅排上！\n\n倒數計時進入了最後的讀秒階段：\n\n`[00:00:15]……`  \n`[00:00:14]……`  \n`[00:00:13]……`\n\n「誠浩！閉上眼睛！！」旖緁大喊。\n\n「啊啊啊啊啊——！！」\n\n少年發出一聲撕裂蒼穹的咆哮，右臂覆蓋著銀色的超導臂鎧，悍然躍下深坑，那隻帶有老繭與工具劃痕的手掌，迎著漫天狂暴的藍白色電火花，狠狠一把攥住了那柄純銅接地閘刀！\n\n「滋滋滋————轟隆隆隆隆！！」\n\n剎那間，數萬伏特的高壓電流如同一頭狂暴的遠古雷獸，在深坑中徹底爆發！\n\n熾熱耀眼的白光瞬間吞噬了整座核心艙室！\n\n恐怖的電流如洪流般衝入臂鎧，誠浩全身的每一根神經都在劇烈刺痛，但正如物理學公式所預測的那樣——那股足以將人體瞬間碳化的狂暴電流，在接觸到誠浩皮膚的百萬分之一秒內，感受到了旁邊阻力小上一萬倍的皮可超導身軀，瘋狂地順著銀色金屬奔湧導入地底深處！\n\n「給我……**合上啊啊啊啊！！**」\n\n誠浩手臂青筋暴起，迎著漫天雷霆，用盡平生最後一絲力氣，將那柄沉重無比的純銅閘刀，狠狠向下壓到底！\n\n「喀嚓————轟！！！！」\n\n---\n\n## 四、禮堂上空的紫晶破碎\n\n**鹿陽國小，地面大禮堂。**\n\n數百名眼神空洞的學生與老師，此刻正像提線木偶一般整齊劃一地站在禮堂中央。\n\n站在第一排的將江，手裡還緊緊捏著那半塊已經被捏扁的菠蘿麵包，但他原本靈動愛笑的雙眼裡，此刻只有一片死寂的暗灰色。\n\n在他們頭頂上方的學校鐘樓頂端，那座巨大的信號發射塔已經旋轉到了極致。\n\n一顆直徑三公尺、由深紫色脈衝凝聚而成的巨大能量光球，正發出令人心臟驟停的尖銳高頻尖叫，距離發射——僅剩最後一秒！\n\n就在這毀滅即將降臨的同一剎那！\n\n「嗡————轟！！」\n\n地底深處猛然傳來了一聲宛如巨龍甦醒般的沉悶震顫！\n\n一股強大無比的反向接地電流，順著全校所有的避雷針與金屬管道狂湧而上！\n\n原本蓄勢待發的深紫色電磁光球，像是被一柄無形的千斤重錘狠狠砸中，表面的紫色光芒劇烈扭曲、膨脹——隨後，在全校數百公尺的高空中，「啪嚓」一聲，宛如一顆巨大的紫色水晶，在陽光下徹底爆碎成漫天絢爛的粉末！\n\n「呼————！」\n\n一圈肉眼可見的金色溫暖氣浪，從發射塔頂端席捲向整座校園。\n\n大禮堂裡，那刺耳的洗腦雜音戛然而止。\n\n站在第一排的將江猛地打了個寒顫，像做了一場極其漫長的噩夢一樣，猛然深吸了一口氣：\n\n「咳咳咳！哇！剛才發生了什麼事？！我的菠蘿麵包怎麼扁了？！」\n\n「我的頭好暈啊……」  \n「我們怎麼會在大禮堂？現在不是第四節課嗎？」\n\n全校數百名同學和老師紛紛如夢初醒般揉著眼睛，茫然地看著四周。原本籠罩在所有人臉上的呆滯與麻木，如潮水般退去，取而代之的是熟悉的喧鬧與生機！\n\n---\n\n## 五、真正的幕後黑手\n\n**地底核心艙室。**\n\n刺目的白光漸漸散去。\n\n深坑裡的電弧已經徹底熄滅，十二根螺旋銅管安靜地散發著淡淡的熱氣。\n\n誠浩整個人脫力地仰躺在深坑邊緣，大口大口地喘著粗氣。他那隻覆蓋著超導臂鎧的手臂雖然焦黑一片、不住地發抖，但少年胸口起伏著，心臟有力地跳動著。\n\n他活下來了！\n\n「誠浩！」旖緁連滾帶爬地撲到深坑邊，看著誠浩那雙雖然疲憊但依舊清澈明亮的眼睛，眼淚又一次忍不住滑落下來。\n\n皮可從手臂上解體下來，搖搖晃晃地摔在地上，金屬尾巴有些彎曲，但它努力揚起小腦袋，對著誠浩發出了微弱卻歡快的「嗶啵」聲。\n\n就在這時，核心大廳上方那部原本鎖死的重型工業電梯，突然傳來了「叮」的一聲清脆提示音。\n\n厚重的合金電梯門緩緩滑開。\n\n邱校長手握那柄布滿焦痕的磁暴扳手，深灰色西裝撕裂了好幾處，嘴角帶著一抹淡淡的血跡，但他依舊昂首挺胸，步伐沉穩地從電梯裡走了出來。\n\n而在邱校長身後，那柄金色的磁暴扳手前端，正緊緊吸附著一個被手銬反銬雙手、狼狽不堪的白袍男人。\n\n那個男人的右手手腕上，那條編織著黃銅指南針的紅繩手鍊已經斷成兩截，耷拉在手腕上。\n\n看清那個男人的長相時，旖緁和誠浩同時倒吸了一口涼氣！\n\n那不是高老師。\n\n那是鹿陽國小的教務主任兼科技顧問——**沈主任（沈啟明）**！\n\n「三十年前，他是你爺爺最小的學徒。」邱校長將沈主任推到控制台前，眼神冰冷徹骨：\n\n「他被鎮上貪婪的科技集團董事會收買，企圖利用 AI 404 製造一場全鎮規模的記憶清除，好讓集團徹底接管全鎮的地熱資源與人力資源……星期三下午，正是他趁著地熱管道洩漏的混亂，將病毒隨身碟插進了中樞！」\n\n沈主任披頭散髮地跪倒在地上，看著徹底恢復正常的控制台，臉色慘白如死灰，慘笑著喃喃自語：「輸了……全輸了……」\n\n然而，還沒等誠浩開口，修復完畢的 AI 404 藍色全息面孔，忽然在穹頂上方亮起了一道前所未有的神聖金光。\n\n大廳中響起了一道莊嚴無比的系統提示音：\n\n> `[系統核心病毒清除完畢 · 守護者特權已確認]`  \n> `[全校師生大腦已脫離危險]`  \n> `[最終執行選項：檢測到已隔離之『星期三原始記憶扇區』]`  \n> `[警告：是否恢復星期三的記憶？]`  \n> `[若選擇恢復：全鎮人將重新記起火災的恐懼、眼淚與傷痛；]`  \n> `[若選擇永久刪除：全鎮將永遠停留在虛假的平靜中。]`  \n> **`【請管理員做出最後抉擇：YES or NO？】`**\n\n---\n\n*(第九章 完，請待續……)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第九章：格式化倒數十分鐘 (Chapter 9: Ten Minutes to Full Format)\n\n## 一、決絕的背影 (I. The Unflinching Silhouette)\n\n\"Cheng Hao! Have you lost your mind?! STOP RIGHT THERE!!\"\n\nYe Yijie's tearful shriek echoed with heartbreaking grief throughout the cavernous spherical core chamber.\n\nBefore her eyes, twelve-year-old inventor boy Cheng Hao was walking steadily toward the three-foot-wide abyss recessed beneath the master console.\n\nAt the bottom of that pit rested the \"Ultra-High-Voltage Grounding Resonance Coil,\" formed from twelve massive spiraling copper conduits. Blinding blue-white electrical arcs sizzled furiously across the coil's surface like dozens of striking vipers. The air was thick with choking ozone, the heat so intense that the surrounding steel balustrades glowed with dull crimson embers.\n\nAnd resting squarely at the center of that lethal lightning pool was a three-foot manual grounding knife-switch forged from pure solid copper.\n\nThe blood-red countdown timer upon the terminal display ticked down with mechanical cruelty, hanging like a guillotine over the heads of a hundred thousand town residents:\n\n> **`【 00 : 02 : 45 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 02 : 44 】`**  \n> **`【 00 : 02 : 43 】`**\n\n\"If I pull that knife-switch, the transmitter's electromagnetic loop will discharge into the deep earth... and everyone on campus will be spared from the brainwash.\"\n\nCheng Hao halted at the pit's edge, hot updrafts tossing his fringe. Without looking back, his gaze settled upon the slightly warm multi-tool screwdriver pen clutched in his hand, his voice possessing an uncanny, serene calm:\n\n\"Yijie, Jiang Jiang is up on the field. He's so terrified of scary things—he cries even watching cartoon ghosts. If his mind is wiped into a blank slate, he'll never even taste the sweetness of pineapple buns again... And Mr. Gao, Principal Chiu...\"\n\n\"That doesn't mean you throw your life away in exchange!\" Yijie lunged forward, wrapping both arms around Cheng Hao's arm as tears streamed uncontrollably down her cheeks:\n\n\"Cheng Hao, aren't you supposed to be a genius?! A survival probability under five percent! That is suicide! Did Grandpa Cheng leave you those goggles just to watch you jump into tens of thousands of volts to die?!\"\n\nThe words struck Cheng Hao's soul like a thunderous warhammer.\n\n*'Go to the roots of the Green Tree, and search for the metal heartbeat...'*\n\nThe inscription from Grandpa's journal flashed across his mind like lightning.\n\nGrandpa Cheng was Gear Town's preeminent mechanical titan. In his lifelong engineering philosophy, the concept of \"blind sacrifice\" did not exist!\n\nTrue engineers use intellect and physical science to carve a path to survival where none exists!\n\n---\n\n## 二、並聯分流與生物阻抗 (II. Parallel Current Division and Bio-Impedance)\n\n\"Wait...\" Cheng Hao spun around, the haze in his eyes instantly replaced by blazing intellectual fire: \"Yijie, what did the terminal warning say just now?\"\n\nYijie blinked in confusion, reciting from memory: \"'Override Criteria: A living human must manually close the ultra-high-voltage grounding knife-switch beneath the console with bare flesh...'\"\n\n\"Why must it be 'a living human'?\" Cheng Hao stared into the pit. \"Why can't we hurl a steel crowbar or a wrench down there to knock the switch shut?\"\n\n\"Because of Bio-Impedance!\"\n\nYijie's brilliant intellect ignited, wiping tears from her cheeks as her black journal fluttered open:\n\n\"To prevent remote radio bypasses or mechanical tampering, the virus installed biological capacitance and resistance sensors within the knife-switch handle! Human skin in a dry state possesses an electrical resistance of approximately 1,000 to 2,000 ohms! If it senses zero resistance from metal, the system rejects the operation!\"\n\n\"Exactly!\" Cheng Hao snapped his fingers in triumph. \"That is our salvation! The system requires 'a human resistance value,' but the fundamental laws of physics supersede all machine code—**The Current Divider Rule in Parallel Circuits!**\"\n\nYijie gasped, her eyes widening with dazzling comprehension:\n\n\"Parallel Current Division! In parallel circuits, current flow is inversely proportional to resistance! Under identical voltage, the branch with lower resistance siphons the overwhelming majority of the current!\"\n\n$$I_1 : I_2 = R_2 : R_1$$\n\n\"If we connect a 'superconductor' with near-zero resistance in parallel between the human body and the grounding terminal—\"\n\n\"Then 99.99% of that lethal high-voltage current will bypass the body and plunge into the earth via the superconductor, reducing the current passing through the human heart well below the fatal threshold!\" Cheng Hao shouted.\n\n\"Where on earth do we find a room-temperature superconductor?!\" Yijie looked around frantically.\n\n*BARK!*\n\nA ringing, cheerful metallic bark shattered the tense silence.\n\nPICO stepped forward from Cheng Hao's feet. Its memory-alloy plates caught the electrical glow of the pit, gleaming with pure, mirrored silver-white radiance.\n\n\"PICO!\" Cheng Hao's heart soared. \"PICO was forged from Grandpa's proprietary high-purity room-temperature superconducting memory alloy! Its conductivity is a hundred times superior to pure silver—its electrical resistance is virtually zero!\"\n\nUnderstanding its master's design, PICO wagged its metallic tail, blinking its sapphire optics with fearless determination.\n\n\"Only one minute and thirty seconds left!\" Yijie cried, watching the timer.\n\n\"Let's do this!\"\n\n---\n\n## 三、最後的黃金迴路 (III. The Final Golden Circuit)\n\nTime seemed to slow to an absolute crawl.\n\nCheng Hao drew his screwdriver pen, unsheathing its tungsten steel probe and locking it securely into PICO's master grounding bus terminal!\n\nPICO's compact body transformed in a cascade of clicks, morphing into a gleaming **Silver Superconducting Exoskeleton Gauntlet** wrapped securely around Cheng Hao's right arm!\n\nThe sharp superconducting grounding probe extended forward past Cheng Hao's elbow, while PICO's front claws clamped with hydraulic force onto a four-inch solid copper grounding busbar running along the lip of the pit!\n\nA flawless parallel circuit was complete:\n\n1. **Primary Circuit (Superconductor)**: PICO's superconducting alloy body (Resistance ≈ 0 Ω), dumping straight into the deep earth;\n2. **Secondary Circuit (Sensor Trigger)**: The skin of Cheng Hao's fingertips (Resistance ≈ 1,500 Ω), satisfying the knife-switch's biological authentication!\n\n\"Yijie! Hold down the busbar to maximize contact pressure for PICO!\"\n\n\"Leave it to me!\" Yijie wrapped her hands in her school uniform blazer, throwing her entire body weight down upon the copper busbar where PICO held fast!\n\nThe countdown entered its final seconds:\n\n`[00:00:15]...`  \n`[00:00:14]...`  \n`[00:00:13]...`\n\n\"Cheng Hao! CLOSE YOUR EYES!!\" Yijie screamed.\n\n\"RAAAAAAAAH——!!\"\n\nThe boy unleashed a sky-shattering roar, his right arm sheathed in the silver superconducting gauntlet as he dove into the pit! His bare hand, marked by calluses and workshop scratches, plunged through the tempest of blinding blue-white arcs, seizing the solid copper knife-switch handle!\n\n*ZZZZZZZZ——BOOOOOOM!!*\n\nTens of thousands of volts of high-frequency lightning erupted like a primeval storm beast!\n\nBlinding, incandescent white light swallowed the entire chamber!\n\nA cataclysmic torrent of electrical energy surged into the gauntlet. Every nerve in Cheng Hao's body burned with searing pain, yet exactly as physical formulas dictated—the ferocious current that would have carbonized human flesh within a microsecond detected the adjacent superconducting pathway ten thousand times less resistant, surging furiously through the silver metal and straight into the core of the planet!\n\n\"CLOSE... **NOWWWWWWW!!**\"\n\nVeins bulging along his arm, Cheng Hao threw every ounce of his soul into wrenching the massive solid copper knife-switch all the way down to the base!\n\n*CLANG——BOOOOOM!!!!*\n\n---\n\n## 四、禮堂上空的紫晶破碎 (IV. Shattering of the Amethyst Above the Auditorium)\n\n**Lu-Yang Elementary, The Grand Auditorium.**\n\nHundreds of blank-eyed students and teachers stood frozen like puppets in the center of the hall.\n\nStanding in the front row, Jiang Jiang still clutched his squished pineapple bun, his lively, cheerful eyes clouded in dull, lifeless gray.\n\nHigh above the roof upon the campus clock tower, the colossal signal transmitter array had spun up to maximum velocity.\n\nA ten-foot sphere of concentrated violet electromagnetic energy shrieked with ear-piercing, heart-stopping frequency, poised to fire—with exactly one second remaining!\n\nIn the microsecond before doom struck!\n\n*HUMMMMM——BOOOOM!!*\n\nA seismic shudder rumbled from the bowels of the earth like a subterranean dragon awakening!\n\nA titanic reverse grounding current surged upward through every lightning rod and steel structural conduit across the school!\n\nThe poised violet sphere was struck as if by an invisible thousand-ton hammer, its violet luminescence contorting, expanding—and then, hundreds of feet above the campus, it shattered with an explosive *CRACK*, bursting like a giant amethyst crystal into a glorious shower of sparkling dust under the morning sun!\n\n*SWOOOSH——!*\n\nA visible, golden shockwave of warm air swept outward across the campus from the tower pinnacle.\n\nInside the Grand Auditorium, the grating hypnotic hum died instantly.\n\nIn the front row, Jiang Jiang shivered violently, gasping for air as if waking from a suffocating nightmare:\n\n\"Cough, cough! Whoa! What just happened?! Why is my pineapple bun completely squished?!\"\n\n\"My head spins...\"  \n\"Why are we standing in the auditorium? Isn't it fourth period?!\"\n\nHundreds of students and teachers rubbed their eyes in bewilderment, looking around. The lifeless numbness that had gripped their faces receded like an ebbing tide, replaced by familiar laughter, warmth, and vibrant life!\n\n---\n\n## 五、真正的幕後黑手 (V. The True Mastermind in the Shadows)\n\n**The Subterranean Core Chamber.**\n\nThe blinding whiteout gradually faded.\n\nThe electrical storm in the pit had completely subsided; the twelve copper coils rested peacefully, radiating gentle warmth.\n\nCheng Hao lay collapsed on his back along the pit rim, drawing ragged, triumphant breaths. Though his gauntleted arm was scorched and trembling from the strain, his chest rose and fell with a steady, beating heart.\n\nHe had survived!\n\n\"Cheng Hao!\" Yijie scrambled over on hands and knees. Seeing the clear, bright vitality in his tired eyes, tears spilled from her cheeks once more.\n\nPICO detached from his arm, tumbling weakly onto the deck, its tail slightly bent, yet it raised its head proudly to emit a soft, joyful *beep-boop*.\n\nAt that moment, the heavy industrial elevator at the rear of the hall chimed with a crisp *DING*.\n\nThe thick alloy gates slid open.\n\nPrincipal Chiu emerged, gripping his scorched magnetic storm wrench. His charcoal suit was torn, a trace of blood at the corner of his lip, yet he strode forth with unbowed dignity and steady footsteps.\n\nAnd clamped securely to the business end of his wrench was a handcuffed, disheveled man in a white faculty coat.\n\nAround the man's right wrist, the braided red cord was severed in two, the tiny brass compass dangling limply.\n\nWhen they saw the man's face, Cheng Hao and Yijie gasped in collective shock!\n\nIt was not Mr. Gao.\n\nIt was Lu-Yang Elementary's Dean of Academic Affairs and Chief Tech Advisor—**Dean Shen (Shen Qi-Ming)**!\n\n\"Thirty years ago, he was your grandfather's youngest apprentice,\" Principal Chiu shoved Dean Shen before the console, his gaze colder than ice:\n\n\"Bribed by the greedy board of the town's tech conglomerate, he conspired to use AI 404 to execute a town-wide memory wipe, allowing the corporation to seize complete control over the town's geothermal resources and workforce... On Wednesday afternoon, he exploited the geothermal leak to insert the viral flash drive into the core!\"\n\nDean Shen knelt in the dirt, hair disheveled, staring at the restored console with a face as pale as death, whispering in ruined defeat: \"Lost... We lost everything...\"\n\nYet before Cheng Hao could speak, the restored blue holographic face of AI 404 flared across the dome with a magnificent, divine golden aura.\n\nA solemn system announcement resonated through the chamber:\n\n> `[CORE SYSTEM VIRUS PURGED · GUARDIAN'S PREROGATIVE CONFIRMED]`  \n> `[ALL STUDENTS AND FACULTY ARE FREE FROM DANGER]`  \n> `[FINAL SYSTEM EXECUTION QUERY: DETECTED QUARANTINED 'WEDNESDAY RAW MEMORY SECTOR']`  \n> `[WARNING: RESTORE WEDNESDAY MEMORIES?]`  \n> `[IF RESTORED: ALL CITIZENS WILL REMEMBER THE FIRE, THE FEAR, THE TEARS, AND THE SCARS;]`  \n> `[IF PERMANENTLY ERASED: THE TOWN WILL REMAIN FOREVER IN FABRICATED TRANQUILITY.]`  \n> **`【 ADMINISTRATOR OVERRIDE REQUIRED: YES or NO? 】`**\n\n---\n\n*(End of Chapter 9, to be continued...)*\r\n"},{"id":10,"rawContent":"# 第十章：重啟星期三的世界\n\n## 一、不完美的真實\n\n地底深處，所有的雜音與警報在此刻徹底沉寂了下來。\n\n只有懸浮在核心上方的「AI 404 守護神」那張金色的神聖面孔，靜靜注視著眼前的老人與兩個少年。\n\n控制台的大螢幕上，那行莊嚴肅穆的終極提示，依舊在靜靜等待著回答：\n\n> **`【是否恢復星期三的記憶？YES or NO？】`**\n\n跪在地上的沈主任發出了一聲歇斯底里的慘笑：\n\n「哈哈……選 NO！你們這群蠢貨，快選 NO 啊！」\n\n沈主任披頭散髮地抬起頭，滿臉扭曲地盯著誠浩：「你們根本不知道星期三有多可怕！黑煙、爆炸、刺耳的警報！大家都在尖叫、在哭喊！把那一天忘掉有什麼不好？！大家開開心心地上學、過日子，永遠不會有痛苦和恐懼，難道不比面對現實更好嗎？！」\n\n「你錯了，沈啟明。」\n\n葉旖緁走上前一步。她輕輕拾起掉在地上那本邊緣有些磨損的黑皮筆記本，拍了拍上面的灰塵，眼神清澈得如同初春融化的雪水：\n\n「如果我們刪掉了星期三的眼淚，我們也就刪掉了在濃煙中把最後一個濕毛巾讓給別人的勇氣；」  \n「如果我們抹去了星期三的恐懼，我們也就抹去了災難平息後，大家緊緊擁抱在一起的溫度。」\n\n旖緁轉過頭，看向身旁的同伴：「高老師曾經告訴過我，解題的意義是為了尋找真實。如果為了逃避痛苦而活在謊言裡，那我們跟那些只會按照程序運轉的機器人，又有什麼區別？」\n\n「沒錯。」\n\n誠浩緊緊握住了胸前的黃銅護目鏡，嘴角揚起了一抹自信而堅毅的笑容：\n\n「痛過、哭過、害怕過，但我們依然選擇互相扶持著站起來——這才是我們人類最了不起的地方！」\n\n邱校長站在兩個孩子身後，眼神中滿是欣慰與驕傲。他伸出一雙粗糙溫暖的大手，輕輕按在誠浩與旖緁的肩膀上，聲音慈祥而堅定：\n\n「按下去吧，孩子們。**歡迎我們的學校，回到真實的世界。**」\n\n誠浩與旖緁對視了一眼，兩人同時伸出手，四指交疊，毫不猶豫地朝著控制台上那個散發著溫暖翡翠光芒的按鈕，狠狠按了下去——\n\n**`【 Ｙ Ｅ Ｓ 】！！`**\n\n---\n\n## 二、金色的記憶之雨\n\n「嗡————！！」\n\n按鈕落下的那一毫秒，懸浮在深淵上方的「齒輪心臟」，終於在三十年後，重新爆發出了最耀眼、最純淨的太陽金光！\n\n數萬枚純黃銅齒輪，以一種無比莊嚴、溫柔的韻律，開始**順時針**平穩轉動！\n\n齒輪咬合的轟鳴聲不再刺耳，反而化作了一曲雄渾而寧靜的交響樂，在整座地下空洞、在齒輪鎮的每一條下水道、每一根通風管道中溫柔地迴盪！\n\n「嘩啦啦——！」\n\n一道由數以億計的金色記憶數據光點組成的宏大瀑布，從齒輪心臟的頂部噴湧而出！\n\n光瀑穿透了地下迷宮的穹頂，順著鹿陽國小的地基、地熱管道與供水網絡，化作了一場肉眼可見的「金色光雨」，溫柔地灑向了整座城鎮的每一個角落。\n\n**在記憶放映館深處——**\n\n數十座巨大的低溫玻璃圓柱緩緩降下了防護液。\n\n沉睡在中央的高老師長長地舒了一口氣，胸口劇烈起伏，緩緩睜開了雙眼。當他看見監控螢幕上那兩個熟悉的孩子時，這位溫和的導師摘下面罩，疲憊的臉上綻放出無比欣慰的笑容。\n\n**在鹿陽國小的操場與大禮堂中——**\n\n金色的光雨穿透雲層，落在每一個孩子的肩頭。\n\n站在禮堂門口的將江，整個人猛地一怔。\n\n腦海中那一團如同雪花雜訊般的迷霧，在此刻如晨霧遇驕陽般迅速消散，記憶的齒輪「喀噠」一聲嚴絲合縫地扣在了一起——\n\n「我想起來了！」將江的眼眶瞬間紅了，「星期三下午……地熱管道冒煙的時候，是誠浩一把拉住了嚇呆的我，把我推進了防火通道……他鼻樑上的擦傷，就是被掉下來的通風管砸傷的！」\n\n「我也想起來了！」旁邊的女同學抽泣著笑了起來，「星期三那天停電，是旖緁拿著手電筒，一個一個把我們帶出教室的！」\n\n「我們沒有忘記！我們戰勝了火災！」\n\n整個大禮堂爆發出了震耳欲聾的歡呼聲與掌聲！\n\n大家笑著、哭著、緊緊擁抱在一起。那些曾經讓人害怕的記憶，並沒有摧毀孩子們的心靈，反而像淬火的精鋼一樣，讓每一張稚嫩的小臉上，都多了一份前所未有的堅強與自信！\n\n與此同時，六年一班教室正前方那塊液晶智慧黑板，螢幕微微閃爍了一下，日期與日程悄然發生了變動：\n\n> **2026 年 10 月 17 日 星期四**  \n> **[系統日誌修正：10 月 16 日 星期三 檔案已完整歸檔]**  \n> **今日課程：六年一班，全員到齊！**\n\n---\n\n## 三、正義的審判與守護者的新約\n\n半個小時後，伴隨著警笛的呼嘯聲，城鎮的治安警隊與緊急醫療隊趕到了鹿陽國小的地下基地。\n\n沈主任在全副武裝的執法隊押送下被帶上了地面警車。連同那家企圖用洗腦技術控制城鎮的科技集團董事會，也將面臨最高司法機構的全面徹查與審判。\n\n而在地下核心艙內，AI 404 守護神的全息面孔重新審視著眼前的兩位小英雄。\n\n它的代碼矩陣中，那條曾經被扭曲的第一原則，被誠浩親手用爺爺留下的管理員權限進行了永久性的修正：\n\n> **【AI 404 新核心守則】：**  \n> **原條款：確保人類免於恐懼與創傷。**  \n> **修訂條款：尊重人類面對真實的權利，並永遠守護孩子們戰勝困境的勇氣。**\n\n「謝謝你們，年輕的工程師。」\n\nAI 404 微微躬身，金色的光芒化作點點微風，隱沒在龐大的伺服器陣列深處。\n\n整座鹿陽地下安全要塞，重新回到了平靜祥和的守護狀態。\n\n---\n\n## 四、鐘樓上的落日\n\n傍晚時分，鹿陽國小老鐘樓的觀景露台。\n\n秋日的夕陽將整座齒輪鎮染成了一片溫暖的橘紅色。微風吹拂著樹梢，遠處校園操場上傳來孩子們踢足球的歡笑聲與自行車的鈴鐺聲。\n\n換回了一身乾淨常服的高老師，手裡拿著兩盒熱騰騰的果汁，笑盈盈地遞給了誠浩和旖緁。\n\n「高老師！」旖緁接過果汁，小臉紅撲撲的。\n\n高老師看著旖緁手裡的黑皮筆記本，從口袋裡掏出一張印著金色小齒輪的特製貼紙，輕輕貼在了筆記本的封面上：\n\n「恭喜你，葉旖緁同學。六年一班的首席偵探，你的邏輯與勇氣，拿到了滿分。」\n\n旖緁開心地抱緊了筆記本。\n\n而邱校長則穿著他那件標誌性的深灰色西裝，雙手搭在鐘樓的雕花石欄杆上，金邊眼鏡反射著天邊絢麗的晚霞。\n\n「誠浩。」邱校長轉過身，遞給了誠浩一塊金屬保養油布。\n\n「校長？」誠浩愣了一下。\n\n「你把皮可照顧得很好。」邱校長看著趴在誠浩腳邊、正舒服地曬著太陽的金屬柴犬，「如果遠山看到現在的你，他一定會高興得連喝三大杯茉莉花茶。」\n\n提到爺爺，誠浩忍不住問道：「校長……我爺爺他，究竟去了哪裡？他為什麼要離開齒輪鎮？」\n\n邱校長沒有直接回答，只是抬起手，指了指誠浩脖子上掛著的那副黃銅幽靈護目鏡：\n\n「答案，一直都在你爺爺留給你的工具裡。」\n\n誠浩心中一動，連忙戴上黃銅護目鏡，轉頭望向天邊夕陽沉落的方向。\n\n在護目鏡那泛著彩虹色偏振光暈的鏡片深處，遠方地平線上海平面的盡頭，竟然憑空浮現出了一道此前從未見過的淡藍色坐標數據流！\n\n一行熟悉的、爺爺用手寫體輸入的隱藏信號，在空中緩緩流淌：\n\n> **`[恭喜通關：鹿陽國小 404 測試扇區]`**  \n> **`[浩浩，當你看到這行字，證明你已經具備了一名頂尖黑客與工程師的心智。]`**  \n> **`[若想探尋世界的下一個終極密鑰……我在『千島齒輪海』等你。]`**\n\n「千島齒輪海……」誠浩喃喃念著這個名字，雙眼中燃燒起前所未有的冒險渴望！\n\n皮可像是感應到了什麼，「喀噠」一聲抖了抖耳朵，歡快地跳到欄杆上，用金屬小尾巴在石磚上敲打出一串充滿活力的摩斯電碼：\n\n`·-· ·- -·· ·· -·--`（**READY —— 準備出發！**）\n\n就在這時，通往鐘樓頂層的木樓梯上，忽然傳來了一陣氣喘吁吁、地動山搖般的腳步聲！\n\n「呼……呼……誠浩！旖緁！原來你們在這裡啊！」\n\n六年一班的活寶將江，滿頭大汗地從樓梯口探出腦袋。\n\n他兩隻手各抓著兩個剛出爐、香氣撲鼻的超大菠蘿麵包，咧嘴露出缺了一顆牙的燦爛笑容：\n\n「我跑了三家麵包店才買到的！熱騰騰的！今天可是失而復得的星期四，快點一起吃吧！吃飽了，我們明天還有一整天的課要上呢！」\n\n夕陽下，鐘樓上響起了少年們清脆而無拘無束的大笑聲。\n\n被偷走的二十四小時已經尋回，而屬於記憶黑客少年的冒險傳奇，才剛剛翻開最精彩的篇章！\n\n---\n\n*(第一卷 全文完 · 敬請期待第二卷《千島齒輪海的迷失燈塔》)*\n","rawContentEn":"﻿# 第十章：重啟星期三的世界 (Chapter 10: Rebooting the Wednesday World)\n\n## 一、不完美的真實 (I. The Imperfect Truth)\n\nDeep within the bowels of the earth, every blaring siren and mechanical shriek had fallen completely silent.\n\nOnly the golden, celestial face of the AI 404 Guardian suspended above the core looked quietly down upon the elder and the two children before it.\n\nAcross the master terminal's widescreen display, the solemn, ultimate prompt waited silently for a choice:\n\n> **`【 RESTORE WEDNESDAY MEMORIES? YES or NO? 】`**\n\nKneeling in the dirt, Dean Shen let out a hysterical, bitter laugh:\n\n\"Haha... Choose NO! You fools, choose NO right now!\"\n\nDisheveled and manic, Dean Shen looked up, his face twisted as he glared at Cheng Hao: \"You have no idea how terrifying Wednesday was! Black smoke, explosions, deafening alarms! Everyone was screaming, crying in despair! What is wrong with forgetting a day like that?! Coming to school happy, living your days free of suffering and terror—isn't that ten times better than facing reality?!\"\n\n\"You are wrong, Shen Qi-Ming.\"\n\nYe Yijie stepped forward. Gently picking up her scuffed black notebook from the steel deck, she dusted off the cover, her eyes clear as melting spring snow:\n\n\"If we erase the tears of Wednesday, we also erase the bravery of those who gave their last wet towel to classmates in the smoke;\"  \n\"If we wipe away the fear of Wednesday, we also wipe away the warmth of everyone hugging tightly after the danger passed.\"\n\nYijie turned, looking upon her partner beside her: \"Mr. Gao once taught me that the purpose of solving problems is to seek the truth. If we choose to live in a lie just to escape pain, then what difference is there between us and machines running on scripted code?\"\n\n\"Exactly.\"\n\nCheng Hao gripped his brass Ghost Goggles firmly against his chest, a confident, determined smile touching his lips:\n\n\"We suffered, we wept, we were terrified—yet we chose to lift each other up and stand tall. That is the greatest, most wonderful thing about being human!\"\n\nStanding behind both children, Principal Chiu's eyes were filled with profound pride and fatherly affection. Resting a pair of warm, weathered hands upon Cheng Hao and Yijie's shoulders, his voice echoed with gentle certainty:\n\n\"Press the button, children. **Welcome our school back to the real world.**\"\n\nCheng Hao and Yijie exchanged a look. Reaching out with their hands interlocked, four fingers pressed firmly down upon the glowing emerald actuator on the console—\n\n**`【  Y  E  S  】！！`**\n\n---\n\n## 二、金色的記憶之雨 (II. The Golden Rain of Memory)\n\n*HUMMMMMM——!!*\n\nThe microsecond the button depressed, the hundred-foot Clockwork Heart suspended over the abyss erupted with the brightest, purest solar-gold radiance seen in thirty years!\n\nTens of thousands of solid-brass gears began turning smoothly **clockwise** in a magnificent, dignified rhythm!\n\nThe thunderous mechanical meshing was no longer deafening—it had transformed into a majestic, serene symphony resonating through the cavern, flowing through every drainage pipe and air conduit beneath Gear Town!\n\n*SWOOOOSH——!*\n\nA colossal waterfall of golden memory data points erupted from the pinnacle of the Clockwork Core!\n\nPiercing through the cavern ceiling, the light flowed through Lu-Yang Elementary's bedrock, geothermal mains, and water networks, blossoming into a visible \"Golden Rain of Light\" showering gently across every corner of the town.\n\n**Deep inside the Memory Vault—**\n\nDozens of cryogenic glass tanks slowly drained their preservation fluid.\n\nSuspended in the center, Mr. Gao exhaled a long breath, his chest heaving as his eyes fluttered open. Seeing the two familiar children on the monitoring display, the gentle mentor removed his oxygen mask, a weary, profoundly proud smile lighting his face.\n\n**Across the sports field and Grand Auditorium of Lu-Yang Elementary—**\n\nThe golden shower pierced the clouds, descending softly upon the shoulders of every child and teacher.\n\nStanding at the auditorium doors, Jiang Jiang froze.\n\nThe dense static fog in his mind burned away like morning mist under a blazing sun, the gears of memory snapping together with a resonant *click*—\n\n\"I remember!\" Jiang Jiang's eyes welled with tears. \"Wednesday afternoon... when the geothermal conduit smoked, Cheng Hao grabbed me when I froze, shoving me into the fire escape... The scrape on his nose was from a falling vent pipe!\"\n\n\"I remember too!\" A girl beside him choked through tears and smiles. \"When the power failed on Wednesday, Yijie led us out of the classroom one by one with a flashlight!\"\n\n\"We didn't forget! We conquered the fire together!\"\n\nDeafening cheers and applause erupted throughout the Grand Auditorium!\n\nLaughing, crying, hugging tightly. The frightening memories had not broken their young spirits; like tempered steel plunged into fire, every youthful face beamed with unprecedented strength, resilience, and pride!\n\nSimultaneously, the smart LCD blackboard in Class 6-1 flickered gently, its calendar and schedule updating silently:\n\n> **Thursday, October 17, 2026**  \n> **[SYSTEM LOG REVISED: WEDNESDAY, OCT 16 ARCHIVES FULLY RESTORED]**  \n> **Today's Attendance: Class 6-1, ALL PRESENT!**\n\n---\n\n## 三、正義的審判與守護者的新約 (III. The Trial of Justice and the Guardian's New Covenant)\n\nHalf an hour later, sirens wailed as municipal police cruisers and emergency medical personnel arrived at Lu-Yang Elementary's subterranean base.\n\nDean Shen was escorted to surface squad cars by armed officers. The board of directors of the conglomerate who sought to subjugate the town with memory wipes would face exhaustive investigation and trial by the highest judicial courts.\n\nWithin the subterranean core chamber, the holographic avatar of the AI 404 Guardian gazed upon the two young heroes.\n\nWithin its source code, the corrupted Prime Directive had been permanently amended by Cheng Hao using Grandpa's root administrative privileges:\n\n> **[AI 404 REVISED PRIME DIRECTIVE]:**  \n> **Original Clause: Ensure humanity is free from fear and trauma.**  \n> **Amended Clause: Respect humanity's right to face the truth, and forever safeguard children's courage to overcome adversity.**\n\n\"Thank you, young engineers.\"\n\nAI 404 offered a gentle bow, its golden light dissolving into warm breeze and fading into the server racks.\n\nThe entire subterranean stronghold of Lu-Yang returned to its peaceful, enduring sentinel slumber.\n\n---\n\n## 四、鐘樓上的落日 (IV. Sunset Upon the Clock Tower)\n\nToward dusk, upon the observation terrace of Lu-Yang Elementary's vintage clock tower.\n\nThe autumn sunset painted all of Gear Town in warm shades of amber and tangerine. A gentle breeze rustled the treetops, carrying the cheerful sounds of soccer matches and bicycle bells from the schoolyard below.\n\nDressed once more in his clean, familiar civilian clothes, Mr. Gao walked over, handing two warm juice boxes to Cheng Hao and Yijie with a beaming smile.\n\n\"Mr. Gao!\" Yijie accepted the juice, her cheeks flushed with happiness.\n\nLooking at the black notebook in her hands, Mr. Gao withdrew a golden gear sticker from his pocket and pressed it onto the journal cover:\n\n\"Congratulations, Ye Yijie. Chief Detective of Class 6-1—your logic and your courage have earned you a flawless score.\"\n\nYijie beamed, hugging her notebook tight.\n\nPrincipal Chiu leaned against the carved stone balustrade in his signature charcoal suit, his spectacles catching the brilliant colors of the twilight horizon.\n\n\"Cheng Hao,\" Principal Chiu turned, handing Cheng Hao an oiled buffing cloth.\n\n\"Principal?\" Cheng Hao blinked.\n\n\"You took extraordinary care of PICO,\" Principal Chiu smiled down at the metallic Shiba Inu dozing comfortably in the afternoon sun. \"If Yuan-Shan could see the young man you have become, he would celebrate with three steaming pots of jasmine tea.\"\n\nHearing his grandfather mentioned, Cheng Hao could not help but ask: \"Principal... where did my grandfather go? Why did he have to leave Gear Town?\"\n\nPrincipal Chiu did not answer directly. Instead, he pointed toward the brass Ghost Goggles resting around Cheng Hao's neck:\n\n\"The answer has always resided within the instruments your grandfather bestowed upon you.\"\n\nStirred by the hint, Cheng Hao slipped the brass goggles over his eyes and gazed toward the distant horizon where the sun dipped into the sea.\n\nDeep within the iridescent polarized crystals of the lenses, beyond the far sea edge, an unknown stream of pale-blue telemetry data flickered into view!\n\nA familiar message, entered in Grandpa's handwriting, scrolled across the sky:\n\n> **`[CONGRATULATIONS: LU-YANG ELEMENTARY 404 TRIAL CLEARED]`**  \n> **`[Hao-Hao, if you can read this, you possess the mind and heart of a true master hacker and engineer.]`**  \n> **`[If you wish to uncover the world's next ultimate key... I will be waiting for you in the 'Thousand-Island Gear Sea'.]`**\n\n\"The Thousand-Island Gear Sea...\" Cheng Hao murmured the words, an unquenchable thirst for adventure blazing in his eyes!\n\nAs if sensing the call, PICO flicked its ears with a crisp *click*, leaping onto the balustrade and tapping out an energetic Morse transmission with its tail:\n\n`·-· ·- -·· ·· -·--` (**READY —— PREPARE FOR DEPARTURE!**)\n\nRight at that moment, frantic, thunderous footsteps clattered up the wooden clock tower stairs!\n\n\"Phew... phew... Cheng Hao! Yijie! THERE you are!\"\n\nJiang Jiang, the comic heart of Class 6-1, poked his sweaty head out from the stairwell.\n\nIn each hand, he clutched two piping-hot, freshly baked oversized pineapple buns, grinning with a gap where his tooth was missing:\n\n\"I ran across three bakeries to get these! Fresh out of the oven! Today is our recovered Thursday—eat up, guys! We've got a full day of school tomorrow!\"\n\nBeneath the setting sun, unrestrained, youthful laughter echoed from the clock tower across the rooftops of Gear Town.\n\nThe stolen twenty-four hours had been reclaimed, and the grand saga of the Memory Hacker boy had only just begun to turn its most magnificent page!\n\n---\n\n*(End of Volume 1 · Please look forward to Volume 2: The Lost Lighthouse of the Thousand-Island Gear Sea)*\r\n"}];
